helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154564				0	hr	Obrazac				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159176				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_LISTBOX_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_LB_FORM\"\>Specifies the logical form in which you want the search to take place.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155434	107			0	hr	The\<emph\> Form \</emph\>combo box is only visible if the current document is a form document with more than one logical form. It does not appear during a search in tables or queries.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151384				0	hr	Form documents may contain multiple logical forms. These are individual form components, which are each linked to a table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145086				0	hr	The \<emph\>Form\</emph\> combo box contains the names of all logical forms for which controls exist.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159414				0	hr	Sva polja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_ALLFIELDS\"\>Searches through all fields.\</ahelp\> If you are running a search in a table, all fields in the table will be searched. If you are running a search in a form, all fields of the logical form (entered under \<emph\>Form\</emph\>) will be searched. If you are running a search in a table control field, all columns that are linked to a valid database table field will be searched.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151054				0	hr	Note that the fields of the current logical form do not have to be identical to the fields of the form document. If the form document contains fields that point to multiple data sources (that is, multiple logical forms), the \<emph\>All Fields\</emph\> option will only search for the fields linked to data sources in the form document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150865				0	hr	Jedno polje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX_RADIOBUTTON_RID_SVXDLG_SEARCHFORM_RB_SINGLEFIELD\"\>Searches through a specified data field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154365				0	hr	Postavke				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158408				0	hr	Defines settings to control the search.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149809				0	hr	Položaj				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_POSITION\"\>Specifies the relationship of the search term and the field contents.\</ahelp\> The following options are available:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	hr	anywhere in the field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145744				0	hr	Returns all fields containing the search pattern anywhere in the field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	hr	beginning of field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	hr	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the beginning of the field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	hr	end of field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	hr	Returns all fields containing the search pattern at the end of the field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	hr	entire field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154127				0	hr	Returns all fields containing the search pattern as an exact match to the contents of the field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	hr	If the \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> check box is marked, this function is not available.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	hr	Primijeni oblik polja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_FORMATTER\"\>Specifies that all field formats are considered when searching in the current document.\</ahelp\> Field formats are all visible formats that are created using the following possibilities:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	hr	in table design mode for field properties,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150488				0	hr	in data source view on column formatting,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152941				0	hr	in forms on control properties.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156736				0	hr	If the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> box is marked, the data source view of the table or form is searched using the formatting set there. If the box is not marked, the database is searched using the formatting saved in the database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	hr	You have a date field, which is saved in "DD.MM.YY" format in the database (for example, 17.02.65). The format of the entry is changed in the data source view to "DD. MMM YYYY" (17 Feb 1965). Following this example, a record containing February 17 is only found when the \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> option is on:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150593				0	hr	Primijeni oblik polja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145253				0	hr	Search Pattern				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3083279				0	hr	uključeno				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155850				0	hr	"Feb" is returned, but not "2".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148590				0	hr	isključeno				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	hr	"2" is returned, but not "Feb".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151321				0	hr	It is recommended that you always search using field formatting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	hr	The following examples show possible issues when searching without field formatting. These issues depend on the database used and only occur for certain internal default formatting:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152971				0	hr	Rezultati pretraživanja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154273				0	hr	Cause				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153836				0	hr	"5" returns "14:00:00" as a time				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156332				0	hr	Time fields are not defined for dBase databases and must be simulated. To internally display the time "14:00:00", a 5 is necessary.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3157965				0	hr	"00:00:00" returns all records of a standard date field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146081				0	hr	The database stores a date value internally using a combined date/time field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	hr	"45.79" does not return "45.79" although the \<emph\>entire field\</emph\> option is selected under \<emph\>Position\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155518				0	hr	The view shown does not match what is stored internally. For example, if value 45.789 is stored in the database as a field of type Number/Double and the shown formatting is set to display only two decimals, "45.79" is only returned in searches with field formatting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148481				0	hr	In this case, standard formatting is formatting that refers to the internally stored data. It is not always visible to the user, especially if it is used for simulating data types (for example, time fields in dBase databases). This depends on the database used and the individual data type. Searching with field formatting is appropriate if you only want to find what is actually shown. This includes fields of type Date, Time, Date/Time and Number/Double.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507	31			0	hr	However, searching without \<emph\>Apply field format \</emph\>is appropriate for larger databases with no formatting issues, because it is faster.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153355				0	hr	If you are searching check boxes with \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\>, you will receive a "1" for marked check boxes, a "0" for unmarked check boxes, and an empty string for undefined (tristate) check boxes. If the search has been carried out without \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\>, you will see language-dependent default values "TRUE" or "FALSE".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150995	119			0	hr	If you use \<emph\>Apply field format\</emph\> when searching in list boxes, you find the text displayed in list boxes. If you do not use \<emph\>Apply field format,\</emph\> you will find the contents corresponding to the standard field format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150387				0	hr	Pazi na VELIKA/mala slova				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_CASE\"\>Specifies that upper and lower case are taken into consideration during the search.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145297				0	hr	Traženje unazad				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151249				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BACKWARD\"\>Specifies that the search process will run in reverse direction, from the last to the first record.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152484				0	hr	From top / From bottom				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156316				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_STARTOVER\"\>Restarts the search. A forward search restarts with the first record. A backwards search restarts with the last record.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163724				0	hr	Izraz sa zamjenskim znakovima				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_WILDCARD\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Allows a search with a * or ? wildcard.\</ahelp\> You can use the following wildcards:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146317				0	hr	Wildcards				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	hr	Značenje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3158411				0	hr	?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148874				0	hr	for exactly one arbitrary character				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	hr	"?loppy" returns "Floppy"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	hr	"M?ller" returns, for example, Miller and Moller				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148803				0	hr	*				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156138				0	hr	for 0 or more arbitrary characters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146135				0	hr	"*-*" returns "ZIP-Drive" and "CD-ROM"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	hr	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145762				0	hr	If you want to search for the actual characters ? or *, preface them with a backslash: "\\?" or "\\*". However, this is only necessary when \<emph\>Wildcard expression \</emph\>is enabled. When the option is not enabled, the wildcard characters are processed like normal characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147130				0	hr	Regularni izraz				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150982				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_REGULAR\"\>Searches with regular expressions.\</ahelp\> The same regular expressions that are supported here are also supported in the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Find & Replace dialog\"\>Find & Replace dialog\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154718				0	hr	Searching with regular expressions offers more options than searching with wildcard expressions. If you search with regular expressions, the following characters correspond to those used in searches with wildcards:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153705				0	hr	Search with wildcard expression				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	hr	Search with regular expressions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151045				0	hr	?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150384				0	hr	.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153793				0	hr	*				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150428				0	hr	.*				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150861				0	hr	Država				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477				0	hr	The \<emph\>State\</emph\> line shows the records returned by the search. If the search reaches the end (or the beginning) of a table, the search is automatically continued at the other end.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720				0	hr	In very large databases, finding the record in reverse search order can take some time. In this case, the status bar informs you that the records are still being counted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147389				0	hr	Search / Cancel				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Starts or cancels the search.\</ahelp\> If the search is successfully completed, the corresponding field in the table is highlighted. You can continue the search by clicking the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> button again. You can cancel a search process by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145080				0	hr	Zatvori				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156166				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_CLOSE\"\>Closes the dialog. The settings of the last search will be saved until you quit \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151183				0	hr	If several tables or forms are open, you can set different search options for each document. When you close the documents only the search options of the document last closed are saved.				20181231 09:50:43
