helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149716				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:DataFilterStandardFilter\"\>Specifies the logical conditions to filter your table data.\</ahelp\> This dialog is called \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> in Spreadsheet documents and \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> in database tables or database forms. The \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> dialog does not contain the \<emph\>More\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_idN105EE				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp#filters\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155555				0	hr	Kriterij filtra				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147834				0	hr	You can define a filter by indicating the type of line, the name of the field, a logical condition and a value or a combination of arguments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149751				0	hr	Operator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHERECOND3\"\>For the following arguments, you can choose between the logical operators AND / OR.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149182				0	hr	Naziv polja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHEREFIELD3\"\>Specifies the field names from the current table to set them in the argument.\</ahelp\> You will see the column identifiers if no text is available for the field names.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	hr	Uvjet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_LISTBOX_DLG_FILTERCRIT_LB_WHERECOMP3\"\>Specifies the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12090101.xhp\" name=\"comparative operators\"\>comparative operators\</link\> through which the entries in the \<emph\>Field name\</emph\> and \<emph\>Value\</emph\> fields can be linked.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149166				0	hr	Vrijednost				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"DBACCESS_EDIT_DLG_FILTERCRIT_ET_WHEREVALUE3\"\>Specifies a value to filter the field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	14			0	hr	The\<emph\> Value \</emph\>list box contains all possible values for the specified \<emph\>Field name\</emph\> . Choose the value to be used in the filter. You can also choose the \<emph\>- empty -\</emph\> or \<emph\>-not empty -\</emph\> entries..				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156118	15			0	hr	If you use the filter function in database tables or forms, then type the value in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>text box to be used for filtering.				20181231 09:50:43
