helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	hr	When you start a dialog to open or save a document, $[officename] initially displays your work directory. To change this directory:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - Paths\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802	5			0	hr	Click \<emph\>My Documents \</emph\>and click the\<emph\> Edit button, or \</emph\>double-click on \<emph\>My Documents\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3153880				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Select Path\</emph\> dialog, choose the work directory you want and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\workfolder.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	hr	You also use this procedure to change the directory displayed by $[officename] when you want to insert a graphic. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - Paths - Graphics\</emph\>, then follow step 3.				20181231 09:50:43
