helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Registering an Address Book				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152823				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>data sources; registering address books\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>address books; registering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>system address book registration\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering; address books\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154228				0	hr	\<variable id=\"data_addressbook\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_addressbook.xhp\" name=\"Registering an Address Book\"\>Registering an Address Book\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154927				0	hr	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you can register different data sources. The contents of the data fields are then available to you for use in various fields and controls. Your system address book is such a data source.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	hr	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> templates and wizards use fields for the contents of the address book. When activated, the general fields in the templates are automatically replaced with the fields from the data source of your address book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	hr	In order for the replacement to take place, you must tell \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> which address book you use. The wizard asking for this information appears automatically the first time you activate, for example, a business letter template. You can also call the wizard by following the steps listed below.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id5941648				0	hr	The address book data is read-only in %PRODUCTNAME Base. It is not possible to add, edit, or delete address data from within Base.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149096				0	hr	Address Data Source Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	hr	To call the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01170000.xhp\" name=\"Address Data Source\"\>Address Data Source\</link\> wizard, choose \<emph\>File - Wizards - Address Data Source\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	hr	Registering An Existing Address Book Manually				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Templates - Address Book Source\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110101.xhp\" name=\"Templates: Address Book Assignment\"\>\<emph\>Templates: Address Book Assignment\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Data source\</emph\> combo box, select the system address book or the data source you want to use as an address book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669	11			0	hr	If you have not yet registered the system address book in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the data source, click the \<emph\>Administrate\</emph\> button. This takes you to the \<emph\>Address Book Data Source Wizard\</emph\>, in which you can register your address book as a new data source in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Table\</emph\> combo box, select the database table you want to use as the address book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	hr	Under \<emph\>Field assignment\</emph\>, match the fields for first name, company, department, and so on to the actual field names used in your address book.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_idN10784				0	hr	When finished, close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_addressbook.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	hr	Now your data source is registered in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> as the address book. If you now open a template from the \<emph\>Business Correspondence\</emph\> category, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> can automatically insert the correct fields for a form letter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Pasting Contents in Special Formats				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	bm_id3620715				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;pasting formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;clipboard options\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formatted/unformatted text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats;pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;pasting in special formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10725				0	hr	\<variable id=\"pasting\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/pasting.xhp\"\>Pasting Contents in Special Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10743				0	hr	Contents that are stored on the clipboard can be pasted into your document using different formats. In %PRODUCTNAME you can choose how to paste the contents using a dialog or a drop-down icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10746				0	hr	The available options depend on the contents of the clipboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144547360				0	hr	In Writer text documents, you can press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl+Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+V to paste the contents of the clipboard as unformatted text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	hr	Pasting clipboard contents using an icon menu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10750				0	hr	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard Bar to open the menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10758				0	hr	Select one of the options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075B				0	hr	If you do not like the result, click the \<emph\>Undo\</emph\> icon and then paste again with another option.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10762				0	hr	Pasting clipboard contents using a dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10769				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10771				0	hr	Select one of the options and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	hr	If you are in a spreadsheet and the contents of the clipboard are spreadsheet cells, then a different \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears. Use the \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog to copy cells using basic or advanced options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077E				0	hr	\<emph\>Transpose\</emph\>: swaps the rows and the columns of the cell range to be pasted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN10785				0	hr	\<emph\>Link\</emph\>: pastes the cell range as a link. If the source file changes, the pasted cells change also.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN1078C				0	hr	The other options are explained in the help, when you call the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\> dialog from within %PRODUCTNAME Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pasting.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BA				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02070000.xhp\"\>Paste Special\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157896				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>databases; text formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables in text format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; spreadsheets to text format\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154824				0	hr	\<variable id=\"data_dbase2office\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_dbase2office.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\"\>Importing and Exporting Data in Text Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	hr	If you want to exchange data with a database that does not have an ODBC link and does not allow dBase import and export, you can use a common text format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	hr	Importing Data into $[officename]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3147275				0	hr	To exchange data in a text format use the $[officename] Calc import/export filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	hr	Export the desired data from the source database in a text format. The CSV text format is recommended. This format separates data fields by using delimiters such as commas or semi-colons, and separates records by inserting line breaks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>\<emph\>Open\</emph\>\</link\> and click the file to import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id1977904				0	hr	Select "Text CSV" from the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> combo box. Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	hr	The \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Text Import\"\>\<emph\>Text Import\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Decide which data to include from the text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3150986				0	hr	Once the data is in a $[officename] Calc spreadsheet, you can edit it as needed. Save the data as a $[officename] data source:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	hr	Save the current $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in dBase format in the folder of a dBase database. To do this, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>, then select the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> "dBase" and the folder of the dBase database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150400				0	hr	Exporting in CSV Text Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154140				0	hr	You can export the current $[officename] spreadsheet in a text format which can be read by many other applications.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3152933				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154216				0	hr	In \<emph\>File type\</emph\> select the filter "Text CSV". Enter a file name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_dbase2office.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	hr	This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"dBase Export\"\>\<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, in which you can select the character set, field delimiter and text delimiter. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. A warning informs you that only the active sheet was saved.				20181231 09:50:43
