helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	bm_id3729667				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating reports\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reports;creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;reports\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	hr	\<variable id=\"data_reports\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_reports.xhp\"\>Creating Reports\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	hr	A report is a Writer text document that can show your data in an organized order and formatting. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, you have a choice to create a report either manually using drag-and-drop in the Report Designer window, or semi-automatic by following a series of dialogs in the Report Wizard. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4094363				0	hr	The following list gives you some information to decide which method to use for your data:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8514358				0	hr	Report Designer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9764091				0	hr	Čarobnjak izvješća				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1579638				0	hr	Started by "Create Report in Design View" command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1886959				0	hr	Started by "Use Wizard to Create Report" command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id455030				0	hr	Full flexibility to use report headers and footers, page headers and footers, multi-column reports.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8409985				0	hr	Uses a Writer template to generate a report document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5931272				0	hr	Use drag-and-drop to position the record fields or other design elements like pictures or lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id9869075				0	hr	Select from several given choices to arrange the data records.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8611713				0	hr	Generates a one-time snapshot of the data. To see an updated report, execute the same report again to create a Writer document with the updated data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2866908				0	hr	You can choose to generate a one-time snapshot with fixed data, or a "live" report with links to the current data at the time when you open the Base file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4169743				0	hr	Saves the report as a Writer text document. Stores the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id408948				0	hr	Saves the report and the information how to create the report inside the Base file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id2891933				0	hr	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to create a new report with the current data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id6142765				0	hr	Choose Open in the context menu or double-click the report name to either see again the static snapshot of the data from first creation time, or to create a new report with the current data. This depends on your choice on the last page of the wizard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id1757560				0	hr	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to open the Report Designer window, with the report's information loaded.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4649189				0	hr	Choose Edit in the context menu of a report name to edit the Writer template file that was used to create the report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	hd_id8414258				0	hr	Creating a New Report Manually In Design View				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id3119602				0	hr	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4226508				0	hr	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id5758842				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Create Report in Design View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id4870754				0	hr	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Designer\</link\> guide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C4				0	hr	Creating a New Report With the Report Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105DC				0	hr	Open the database file where you want to create the new report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E0				0	hr	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Reports\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E8				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Report\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_reports.xhp	0	help	par_id8032166				0	hr	Follow the steps of the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01100000.xhp\"\>Report Wizard\</link\> to create the report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156410				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>start parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>command line parameters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>parameters;command line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arguments in command line\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156410				0	hr	Starting the $[officename] Software With Parameters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147009				0	hr	By starting the $[officename] software from the command line you can assign various parameters, with which you can influence the performance. The use of command line parameters is only recommended for experienced users.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	hr	For normal handling, the use of command line parameters is not necessary. A few of the parameters require a deeper knowledge of the technical background of the $[officename] software technology.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	hr	Starting the $[officename] Software From the Command Line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3156152				0	hr	Under Windows, select \<emph\>Run\</emph\> from the Windows Start menu, or open a Shell under UNIX® based platforms.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472	6			0	hr	Under Windows, type the following text in the \<emph\>Open \</emph\>text field and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	hr	Under UNIX based systems, type the following line of text, then press \<emph\>Return\</emph\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3147561	7			0	hr	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>{install}\\program\\soffice.exe {parameter} \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>{install}/program/soffice {parameter} \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3153360				0	hr	Replace \<emph\>{install}\</emph\> with the path to your installation of the $[officename] software (for example, \<emph\>C:\\Program Files\\Office\</emph\>, or \<emph\>~/office\</emph\>)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\start_parameters.xhp	0	help	par_id3158407				0	hr	Where required, replace \<emph\>{parameter}\</emph\> with one or more of the following command line parameters.				20181231 09:50:43
