helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152924				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>sending; AutoAbstract function in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoAbstract function for sending text to presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>outlines; sending to presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; copying by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; copying and pasting text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;data from text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152924				0	hr	\<variable id=\"copytext2application\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copytext2application.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Data From Text Documents\"\>Inserting Data From Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	hr	You can insert text into other document types, such as spreadsheets and presentations. Note that there is a difference between whether the text is inserted into a text frame, a spreadsheet cell, or into the outline view of a presentation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	hr	If you copy text to the clipboard, you can paste it with or without text attributes. Use the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V to paste.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3143270\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_paste.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3143270\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	hr	To select the format in which the clipboard contents will be pasted, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Paste\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>, then select the proper format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	hr	If a text document contains headings formatted with the Heading Paragraph Style, choose \<emph\>File - Send - Outline to Presentation\</emph\>. A new presentation document is created, which contains the headings as an outline.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3145316				0	hr	If you want to transfer each heading together with its accompanying paragraphs, select the \<emph\>File - Send - AutoAbstract to Presentation\</emph\> command. You must have formatted the headings with a corresponding Paragraph Style to be able to see this command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156024				0	hr	Copying Text Using Drag-and-Drop				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303				0	hr	If you select text and drag it into a spreadsheet with drag-and-drop, it will be inserted as text into the cell where you release the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	hr	If you drag text to the normal view of a presentation, an OLE object is inserted as a $[officename] plug-in.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copytext2application.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	hr	If you drag the text to the outline view of a presentation, it will be inserted at the cursor location.				20181231 09:50:43
