helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator_setcursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	hr	Double-click an object in the Navigator to jump directly to the position of the object in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator_setcursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	hr	You can use the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar to scroll to the previous or next object of a specific category.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator_setcursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	hr	Open the toolbar using the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> icon below the vertical scroll bar of a text document, or in the Navigator window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navigator_setcursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3153348				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Navigation\</emph\> toolbar, you first select the category, then click on one of the buttons, \<emph\>Previous Object\</emph\> or \<emph\>Next Object\</emph\>. The names of the buttons refer to the category, for example, the button "Next Object" is named "Next Page" or "Next Bookmark" according to the category.				20181231 09:50:43
