helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Comparing Versions of a Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154788				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>documents; comparing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comparisons;document versions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>versions; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changes;comparing to original\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function; comparing documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154788				0	hr	\<variable id=\"redlining_doccompare\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_doccompare.xhp\" name=\"Comparing Versions of a Document\"\>Comparing Versions of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4186223				0	hr	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3995178				0	hr	Imagine you have some co-authors or reviewers who collaborate with you writing your original document. One day you send out copies of your document to all reviewers. You ask them to edit the copy and send it back.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id9948423				0	hr	Normally, the reviewers enable change tracking by \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Record\</emph\> and you can easily see the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	hr	If one of the authors has made changes to a document without recording them, you can compare the changed document to your original document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3153087				0	hr	Open the reviewer's document and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Compare Document\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id4208807				0	hr	You should always start with opening the newer document and compare it with the older document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315				0	hr	A file selection dialog appears. Select your older original document and confirm the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	hr	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> combines both documents into the reviewer's document. All text passages that occur in the reviewer's document but not in the original are identified as having been inserted, and all text passages that got deleted by the reviewer are identified as deletions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_doccompare.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	hr	You can now accept or reject the insertions and deletions. At the end you may save the reviewer's document as a new original with a new name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Working with Queries				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	bm_id840784				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>databases;creating queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;data in databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries;defining (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;queries (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards;database queries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Query Wizard (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F9				0	hr	\<variable id=\"data_queries\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_queries.xhp\"\>Working with Queries\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10617				0	hr	If you often want to access only a subset of your data that can be well defined by a filter condition, you can define a query. This is basically a name for the new view at the filtered data. You open the query and see the current data in the table layout that you defined.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061A				0	hr	Creating a New Query With the Query Wizard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1061E				0	hr	In %PRODUCTNAME you can create a new query using the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/querywizard00.xhp\"\>Query Wizard\</link\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10632				0	hr	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10636				0	hr	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063E				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Use Wizard to Create Query\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	hr	Creating a New Query With the Design View				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064C				0	hr	Open the database file where you want to create the new query.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10650				0	hr	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Queries\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10658				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Create Query in Design View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	hr	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\"\>Query Design window\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067B				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_queries.xhp	0	help	par_idN10683				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Opening documents saved in other formats				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153988				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office;opening Microsoft documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; importing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; documents in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; documents from other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>loading; documents from other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;Microsoft documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; default file formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults; file formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>file formats; saving always in other formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Microsoft Office; as standard file format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files;importing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML converters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converters; XML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Document Converter Wizard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>wizards; document converter\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145313				0	hr	\<variable id=\"import_ms\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/import_ms.xhp\" name=\"Opening documents saved in other formats\"\>Opening documents saved in other formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	hr	You can open a document saved in another format by using the following procedure:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	5			0	hr	Select a format from the\<emph\> Files of type\</emph\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	hr	Select a file name and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	hr	If you always want the file dialogs to show another format by default, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - Load/Save - General\</emph\> and select that format as \<emph\>Standard file format\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154898				0	hr	Converting all documents of a folder				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147336				0	hr	Open the wizard, which guides you through the operation, to copy and convert all documents from Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel or Microsoft PowerPoint into OpenDocument file format documents. You can select a source and target directory, specify whether to convert documents and/or templates, and more besides.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3153824				0	hr	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01130000.xhp\" name=\"File - AutoPilot - Document Converter\"\>\<emph\>File - Wizards - Document Converter\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	hd_id4563127				0	hr	Opening HTML files in Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id9207434				0	hr	Choose the file type "HTML Document" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web. This is the default for HTML documents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id7215491				0	hr	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer/Web are now available to you, such as \<emph\>Show HTML source\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id2299874				0	hr	Choose "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id1727347				0	hr	All the options of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer are now available to you. Not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer offers for editing of documents can be saved in HTML format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01130100.xhp\" name=\"Working with VBA code\"\>Working with VBA code\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\import_ms.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010200.xhp\" name=\"Setting the default file format\"\>Setting the default file format\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158421				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility;general shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys; %PRODUCTNAME accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158421				0	hr	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcuts (%PRODUCTNAME Accessibility)\"\>Shortcuts (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159201				0	hr	You can control \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> without using a mouse device, using only the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149177				0	hr	On each module's main help page (for example, the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer or \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc main help page) there is a link to access the keyboard shortcuts' help for that module.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145382				0	hr	In addition, under the keyword "Accessibility" you find step-by-step instructions about how to control the selected module without a mouse device.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166460				0	hr	Working with the \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> user interface without mouse				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154749				0	hr	Activating menu bar, toolbars, windows, and document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	hr	Repeatedly pressing F6 switches the focus and circles through the following objects:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	hr	menu bar,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	hr	every toolbar from top to bottom and from left to right,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147618				0	hr	every free window from left to right,				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514				0	hr	dokument				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153252				0	hr	Press Shift+F6 or Shift+Ctrl+Tab to switch through objects in the opposite direction.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152473				0	hr	Press Ctrl+F6 to switch to the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152360				0	hr	Press F10 to switch to the menu bar and back.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	hr	Escape closes an open submenu, a toolbar, or the current free window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3161656				0	hr	Calling a menu command				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	hr	Press Alt or F6 or F10 to select the first menu (the \<emph\>File\</emph\> menu). With right arrow, the next menu to the right is selected; with left arrow, the previous menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153381				0	hr	Arrow down opens a selected menu. Any additional arrow down and up arrow move the selection through the menu commands. With right arrow you open any existing submenus.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148798				0	hr	Press Enter to execute the selected menu command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147086				0	hr	Executing an icon command				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	hr	Press F6 repeatedly until the first icon on the toolbar is selected. Use the right and left arrows to select an icon on a horizontal toolbar. Similarly, use the up and down arrows to select an icon on a vertical toolbar. The Home key selects the first icon on a toolbar and the End key, the last.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3144433				0	hr	Press Enter to execute the selected icon. If the selected icon normally demands a consecutive mouse action, such as inserting a rectangle, then pressing the Enter key is not sufficient: in these cases press Ctrl+Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	hr	Pressing Ctrl+Enter on an icon for creating a draw object. A draw object will be placed into the middle of the view, with a predefined size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150449				0	hr	Press Ctrl+Enter on the Selection tool to select the first draw object in the document. If you want to edit, size, or move the selected draw object, first use Ctrl+F6 to set the focus into the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	hr	If a toolbar is longer than can be displayed on screen, it shows an icon at the right or lower edge. Select the toolbar and press PageUp or PageDown to display the remaining icons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	hr	Special hints for toolbars				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149983				0	hr	Press the down arrow or right arrow to open the selected toolbar. This is equivalent to a mouse click. In the toolbar use the right arrow and left arrow keys. The Home and End keys select the first and last icon in the toolbar, respectively.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145365				0	hr	Close the toolbar with Esc. It is not possible to move the toolbar without a mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	hr	Selection from a combo box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146986				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3148645\" src=\"res/helpimg/zellvor.png\" width=\"1.528in\" height=\"0.292in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148645\"\>Combo box\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	hr	Select the combo box. Press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	hr	Use the down arrow or Page Down key to scroll down the combo box entries, or the up arrow or Page Up key to scroll upwards. The Home key takes you to the first entry and the End key takes you to the last entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145749				0	hr	Press Enter to execute the selected entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150685				0	hr	Selection in Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	hr	In several windows, dialogs, and in the table control field, there are tables to select data, for instance, in the right part of the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp\" name=\"Data Source View\"\>Data Source View\</link\>. The following keys are used for selections in these tables:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	hr	Spacebar: switches from selection of the current row and cancellation of any selection, but not if the current cell is in edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	hr	Ctrl+Spacebar: switches between selection of the current row and cancellation of this selection				20181231 09:50:43
