helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	hr	Alt+Up Arrow or Alt+Down Arrow: moves the window separator between table and form, for instance in the bibliography database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	hr	In a table control or in the data source view, the Tab key moves to the next column. To move to the next control, press Ctrl+Tab. To move to the previous control, press Shift+Ctrl+Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150592				0	hr	Size and Position of Windows and Dialogs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221				0	hr	First press Alt+Spacebar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	hr	A system menu opens with menu commands like \<emph\>Move\</emph\>, \<emph\>Resize\</emph\> and \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	hr	Choose a command (down arrow, then Enter).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155083				0	hr	Now you can use the arrow keys to move or resize the dialog or window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	hr	Press Enter to accept the change. Press Escape to cancel the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146988				0	hr	Docking and Undocking Windows and Toolbars				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147176				0	hr	Press F6 until the window or toolbar is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	hr	Press Ctrl+Shift+F10.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154479				0	hr	Selecting objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148993				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F4\</item\> to select the first object in the current document. When an object is selected, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next object, or press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to go back to the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152962				0	hr	Edit Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156379				0	hr	A selected OLE object can be activated with the Enter key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	hr	Edit Position and Size of Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405				0	hr	Use the arrow keys to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145619				0	hr	Set the grid resolution unit with \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> area. If you enter a number greater than 1 in the \<emph\>Subdivision\</emph\> area, you must press the arrow key as often as the number states to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	hr	Use the Alt and arrow keys to move the selected object by one pixel.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	hr	Use Ctrl+Tab to enter the handle edit mode. The upper left handle is the active handle, it starts blinking. Use Ctrl+Tab to select the next handle. Use (Esc) to exit the handle edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	hr	In the handle edit mode, the arrow keys move the selected handle, which changes the object size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147361				0	hr	Edit the Anchors of Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148534				0	hr	You can move the anchor of an object with the arrow keys. First enter the handle edit mode and select the anchor. Depending on the type of anchor, you can then move the anchor in different directions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3163808				0	hr	Select the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150646				0	hr	Enter the handle edit mode with Ctrl+Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150940				0	hr	The upper left handle starts blinking. Press Ctrl+Tab several times, until no handle blinks. This signals that now the anchor of the object is activated. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>In text documents you can press Shift+Ctrl+A to activate the anchor directly. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	hr	Use the arrow keys to move the anchor. The object follows the anchor as appropriate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152582				0	hr	You can change the anchor of the selected object for example in the object's context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148393				0	hr	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To Paragraph\</emph\>, the arrow keys move the object to the previous or next paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145615	69			0	hr	If the object is anchored\<emph\> To page\</emph\>, the keys Page Up or Page Down move it to the previous or next page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135				0	hr	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To character\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it through the current paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256	71			0	hr	If the object is anchored\<emph\> As character\</emph\>, no anchor icon exists. You cannot move the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149527				0	hr	If the object is anchored \<emph\>To frame\</emph\>, the Arrow keys move it to the next frame in the respective direction.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153270				0	hr	Controlling the Dividing Lines				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3158413	134			0	hr	Documents of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc, \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Draw, and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Impress can be split horizontally and vertically into separate views. Each view can show other parts of the document. Using the mouse, you can drag a dividing line from the scrollbar into the document.				20181231 09:50:43
