helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146117				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>defining; arrowheads and other line ends\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arrows; defining arrow heads\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines;defining ends\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146117				0	hr	\<variable id=\"lineend_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/lineend_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Line Ends\"\>Defining Line Ends\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	hr	You can define any object to be included in the list of available line ends.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	hr	Use the draw functions to create an object to be used as a line end.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3149795				0	hr	Select the object and choose \<emph\>Format - \</emph\>\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\<emph\>Drawing Object - \</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<emph\>Graphic - \</emph\>\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\>Line\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306				0	hr	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Arrow Styles\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3149765				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and assign a name to the new arrow style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\lineend_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Drawing Lines in Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143206				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>arrows; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indicator lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; drawing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lines; removing automatic lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing lines in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic lines/borders in text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143206				0	hr	\<variable id=\"line_intext\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/line_intext.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Lines in Text\"\>Drawing Lines in Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3144436				0	hr	You can incorporate lines into your text with custom angles, width, color, and other attributes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	hr	To define the line attributes and direction, use the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> drawing object as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3166410\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertdraw.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3166410\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3154285\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_line.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154285\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153254				0	hr	1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400	41			0	hr	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Show Draw Functions \</emph\>icon to open the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>toolbar, and click the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> icon. The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol with a line beside it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156117				0	hr	2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	hr	In your document, click where the line should begin. Hold down the mouse button and drag to the point where you want the line to end. If you also hold down the Shift key, you can draw only horizontal, vertical, and diagonal lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3159413\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159413\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	hr	3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153361	43			0	hr	Release the mouse button once the line has the desired direction and length. You can then draw more lines. End this function by pressing the Esc key or by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon from the \<emph\>Drawing \</emph\>bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hr	4.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	hr	After clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon, you can select all of the lines at the same time by clicking each line while holding down the Shift key. This multiple selection enables you to assign all of them a common color, width or other attribute.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049				0	hr	Create a horizontal line by applying the preset Paragraph Style \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\>. Click into an empty paragraph, and double-click the \<emph\>Horizontal Line\</emph\> Style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. If the entry for horizontal lines is not visible in the list of Paragraph Styles, select "All Styles" in the lower listbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	hr	You can draw a line above, beside or below a paragraph in a Writer text document by choosing \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	hr	Automatic lines in Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	hr	If you start a new line in a Writer text document by typing three or more hyphen characters and press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key, the characters are removed and the previous paragraph gets a line as a bottom border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id8849452				0	hr	To create a single line, type three or more hyphens (-), or underscores ( _ ), and then press Enter. To create a double line, type three or more equal signs (=), asterisks (*), tildes (~), or hash marks (#), and then press Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D0				0	hr	To remove an automatically drawn border, choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</emph\> and select no border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	hr	To undo an automatic border replacement once, choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E0				0	hr	To disable the automatic borders, choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect - Options\</emph\> and clear \<emph\>Apply border\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3145787				0	hr	The lines and other drawing objects that you insert in text are not defined in \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#html\" name=\"HTML\"\>HTML\</link\>, and are therefore not exported directly into HTML format. Instead, they are exported as graphics.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id641804				0	hr	When you enter a line width, you can append a measurement unit. A zero line width results in a hairline with a width of one pixel of the output medium.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\line_intext.xhp	0	help	par_id3154188				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Format - Paragraph - Borders\"\>Format - Paragraph - Borders\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
