helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SQL; executing SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>queries;creating in SQL view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>commands;SQL\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>executing;SQL commands\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	hr	\<variable id=\"data_enter_sql\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_enter_sql.xhp\" name=\"Executing SQL Commands\"\>Executing SQL Commands\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	hr	With the help of SQL commands you can control the database directly, and can also create and edit tables and queries.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	hr	Not all database types support all SQL instructions. If necessary, find out which SQL commands are supported by your database system.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	hd_id9577929				0	hr	To execute an SQL statement directly				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id7923825				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> to open a database file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id9448530				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - SQL\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3151176	91			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Create Query in SQL View\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154071\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbnewquerysql.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> or				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786	92			0	hr	Select an existing query from the list and click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156212\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_dbqueryedit.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156212\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3083443				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Query\</emph\> window, choose \<emph\>View - Switch Design View On/Off\</emph\>. Edit the SQL command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3152460	96			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Run\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3152886\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_sbaexecutesql.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152886\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The result of the query is displayed in the upper window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3149298	98			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> or \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3153159\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_save.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153159\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to save the query.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_enter_sql.xhp	0	help	par_id3153223				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/02010100.xhp\" name=\"Query Design\"\>Query Design\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Creating XML Filters 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id7007583				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>testing XML filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XML filters;creating/testing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id1413922				0	hr	\<variable id=\"xsltfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_create.xhp\"\>Creating XML Filters\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1053D				0	hr	Creating an XML Filter for %PRODUCTNAME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109A9				0	hr	When you create an XML filter for %PRODUCTNAME, you need to design an \<emph\>XSLT stylesheet\</emph\> that can convert to and from the OpenDocument XML file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109B0				0	hr	For more information about the OpenDocument XML format, go to \<link href=\"https://xml.openoffice.org/\"\>https://xml.openoffice.org/\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109C5				0	hr	If you want, you can include a \<emph\>template\</emph\> with your filter to apply %PRODUCTNAME styles to an XML document that you import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CC				0	hr	You can also include the \<emph\>Document Type Definition\</emph\> (DTD) for the external XML format so you can validate the XML format, for example, when you test the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10531				0	hr	To Create an XML Filter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E0				0	hr	Create an XSLT transformation \<emph\>stylesheet\</emph\> that maps the elements of the external XML format to the elements of the OpenDocument XML file format and back again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109E8				0	hr	Create a template that assigns %PRODUCTNAME styles to elements in the external XML format when you import a file in this format into %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109EC				0	hr	In %PRODUCTNAME Writer, create a text document, and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109F4				0	hr	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN109FC				0	hr	In the \<emph\>XML Filter\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and define the properties of the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A03				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Filter Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the XML filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CA1				0	hr	This name is displayed in the \<emph\>XML Filter Settings\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A09				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Application\</emph\> box, select the %PRODUCTNAME application that the filter is for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0F				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Name of File Type\</emph\> box, enter the file type that the filter is for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10CC6				0	hr	This name is displayed in the list of file types in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\>, \<emph\>Export\</emph\>, and \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialogs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A15				0	hr	In the \<emph\>File extension\</emph\> box, enter the extension for the exported file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1B				0	hr	To differentiate the file from other XML files, enter an extension other than *.xml.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A1F				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page, define the transformation properties for the filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A26				0	hr	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DocType\</emph\> box, enter the document type identifier for the external file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D0E				0	hr	This identifier is used to detect the file type on import.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A2C				0	hr	(Optional) In the \<emph\>DTD\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the DTD for the external file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10D1F				0	hr	This DTD is used to validate the files on export.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A32				0	hr	In the \<emph\>XSLT for export\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name of the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from OpenDocument format to the external format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A38				0	hr	In the \<emph\>XSLT for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and file name to the XSLT stylesheet that defines the transformation from the external format to OpenDocument format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A3E				0	hr	(Optional) In the \<emph\>Template for import\</emph\> box, enter the path and name of the template that defines the %PRODUCTNAME styles that are used in the imported file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A44				0	hr	The files that are specified on the \<emph\>Transformation\</emph\> tab page are copied to the local %PRODUCTNAME users directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A4C				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	hr	To Test an XML Filter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A5A				0	hr	You can perform basic tests on a custom XML filter in %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A91				0	hr	The document is not altered by these tests. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A60				0	hr	Create or open a text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A67				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - XML Filter Settings\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A6F				0	hr	In the list of filters, select the filter that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Test XSLTs\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A82				0	hr	To test an \<emph\>Export\</emph\> Filter, do one of the following in the \<emph\>Export\</emph\> area of the dialog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DEB				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>, select the %PRODUCTNAME document that you want to test, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10DF7				0	hr	To test the current document, click \<emph\>Current Document\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A99				0	hr	To test an \<emph\>Import\</emph\> Filter, click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Import\</emph\> area of the dialog, select a document, and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E32				0	hr	To validate the transformed file against the specified DTD, click \<emph\>Validate\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_id8579668				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter.xhp\"\>About XML Filters\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\xsltfilter_create.xhp	0	help	par_id5569017				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/xsltfilter_distribute.xhp\"\>Distributing XML filters\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Kreiranje oblih uglova				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150040				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>corner roundings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rectangles with round corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>legends;rounding corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>round corners\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customizing;round corners\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150040				0	hr	\<variable id=\"round_corner\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/round_corner.xhp\" name=\"Creating Round Corners\"\>Creating Round Corners\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	hr	When you insert a rectangle or a callout box using the drawing functions and activate the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, you see a small frame at the upper left corner of the object. The frame indicates the amount by which the corners are rounded. When the frame is positioned at the top left corner, no rounding occurs. When the frame is positioned on the handle centered at the top of the object, the corners are rounded as much as possible. You adjust the degree of rounding by moving the frame between these two positions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3150774\" src=\"res/helpimg/hand01.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150774\"\>Mouse pointer as hand\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\round_corner.xhp	0	help	par_id3148539				0	hr	If you place the cursor on the box it changes to a hand symbol. You can now drag the box to change the amount of rounding. An outline shows a preview of the result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143267				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>installing;ActiveX control\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Internet; Internet Explorer for displaying $[officename] documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>$[officename] documents;viewing and editing in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;%PRODUCTNAME documents in Internet Explorer\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	hr	\<variable id=\"activex\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/activex.xhp\" name=\"ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\"\>ActiveX Control to Display Documents in Internet Explorer\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	hr	Under Windows only, you can view any $[officename] document in a window of the Microsoft Internet Explorer. Install the ActiveX control in the $[officename] Setup program.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156346				0	hr	Installing the ActiveX control				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821				0	hr	Close $[officename] and the Quickstarter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3150771				0	hr	Click the Start button on the Windows taskbar. Choose \<emph\>Control Panel\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	hr	In the Control Panel, click \<emph\>Add or Remove Programs\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3156155				0	hr	In the list, click %PRODUCTNAME, then click \<emph\>Change\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_idN10706				0	hr	In the Installation Wizard, select \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3159399				0	hr	Open the \<emph\>Optional Components\</emph\> entry and find the \<emph\>ActiveX Control\</emph\> entry. Open the sub menu of the icon and select to install the feature.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	8			0	hr	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> and \<emph\>Install\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151384				0	hr	Viewing $[officename] documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	hr	In Internet Explorer, browse to a web page that contains a link to a $[officename] Writer document, for example.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	hr	Click the link to view the document in the Internet Explorer window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154072				0	hr	You may still right-click the link to save the file on your harddisk.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	hr	Editing $[officename] documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3154367				0	hr	The $[officename] document inside the Internet Explorer shows a set of read-only toolbar icons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3148451				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Edit file\</emph\> icon in the document's toolbar to open a copy of the document in a new $[officename] window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\activex.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	hr	Edit the copy of the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Slikama se dodaju područja na koja možete kliknuti.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	hr	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	hr	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	hr	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	hr	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	hr	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	hr	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	hr	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	hr	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	hr	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	hr	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	hr	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	hr	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	hr	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Showing Navigation Pane of the Help				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>Help; navigation pane showing/hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;navigation pane in Help window\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indexes;showing/hiding Help index tab\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150178				0	hr	\<variable id=\"navpane_on\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/navpane_on.xhp\" name=\"Showing Navigation Pane of the Help\"\>Showing Navigation Pane of the Help\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	hr	In the Help window, you can show or hide the navigation pane as needed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3156411				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3153345\" src=\"sfx2/res/indexon_small.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153345\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\navpane_on.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	hr	On the toolbar of the \<emph\>Help\</emph\> window, click the left icon to show or hide the navigation pane.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Editing Hyperlinks				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; editing hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;hyperlink text/formats/URLs\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text attributes; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>buttons;editing hyperlink buttons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL;changing hyperlink URLs\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	hr	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Hyperlinks\"\>Editing Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id4124881				0	hr	When you \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>-click a hyperlink in a Writer document, your web browser opens with the requested web address. If you don't use a mouse, position the cursor inside the hyperlink and open the context menu by Shift+F10, then choose Open Hyperlink.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145071				0	hr	Change the text of a hyperlink as follows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410	12			0	hr	Option 1: Click on the hyperlink. Then click the \<emph\>Hyperlink \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar. This works only in text documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id2690511				0	hr	If you leave the hyperlink by positioning the cursor somewhere else, only the visible text will be changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id1983092				0	hr	If you leave the hyperlink by entering a space character directly following the last character, the AutoCorrect - if enabled - will change the target URL to be the same as the visible text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id333262				0	hr	In all document types, you can open the Hyperlink dialog to edit a hyperlink. First set the cursor into the hyperlink or directly in front of the hyperlink, then click the Hyperlink icon on the Standard bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158432				0	hr	Change the URL of a hyperlink as follows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	hr	Option 1: As described above, open \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Dialog\"\>Hyperlink Dialog\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	hr	Option 2: Open \<link href=\"text/shared/main0209.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink Bar\"\>Hyperlink Bar\</link\> (\<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>). Click on the hyperlink, do not release the mouse button and drag the hyperlink to the Hyperlink Bar. Edit the URL on the Hyperlink Bar and press the Return key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148686				0	hr	Change the attribute of all hyperlinks				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148943				0	hr	Open the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10826				0	hr	Click the Character Styles icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	hr	Right-click the "Internet Link" or "Visited Internet Link" character style, and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	hr	In the dialog, select the new attributes, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	hr	Edit a hyperlink button				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3152361				0	hr	If the hyperlink is a button, click on the border to select it, or press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while clicking. Open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog through the context menu. You can edit the label text under "Caption," and modify the address in the "URL" field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Unosenje hiperveza				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	hr	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	hr	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	hr	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	hr	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	hr	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	hr	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	hr	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	hr	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	hr	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	hr	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hr	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
