helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Copying Graphics Between Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;pictures from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201				0	hr	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805				0	hr	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576				0	hr	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	hr	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	hr	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110				0	hr	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	hr	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	hr	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	hr	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Registering and Deleting a Database 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	hr	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	hr	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	hr	To register an existing database file:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	hr	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and select the database file. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	hr	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	hr	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	hr	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F3				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FB				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Prihvacanje i odbijanje izmjena				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150247				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>changes; accepting or rejecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>review function;accepting or rejecting changes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150247				0	hr	\<variable id=\"redlining_accept\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_accept.xhp\" name=\"Accepting or Rejecting Changes\"\>Accepting or Rejecting Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1491134				0	hr	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id1110200810120034				0	hr	In Writer text documents you can also accept or reject changes by choosing commands from the context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	hr	When you edit a document in which others have made changes, you can accept or reject the changes individually or all together.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	hr	If you have put multiple copies of the document in circulation, first merge these into one document (see \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_docmerge.xhp#redlining_docmerge\"/\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748				0	hr	Open the document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Accept or Reject\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346				0	hr	Select a change on the \<emph\>List\</emph\> tab. The change is selected and displayed in the document and you can now enter your decision with one of the buttons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	hr	If one author has modified another author's change, you will see the changes hierarchically arranged with a plus sign for opening up the hierarchy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	hr	If the list of changes is too long, you can switch to the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> tab in the dialog and specify that you only want to see the changes of certain authors, or only the changes of the last day, or that you want the list to be restricted in some other way.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_accept.xhp	0	help	par_id3143271				0	hr	Color-coded entries display the result of the filter that is set. Entries in black can be accepted or rejected and match the filter criteria. Entries in blue do not themselves match the filter criteria, but have subentries that are included by the filter. Gray entries cannot be accepted or rejected and do not match the filter criterion. Green entries do match the filter but cannot be accepted or rejected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Assistive Tools in $[officename]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399				0	hr	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	hr	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id8847010				0	hr	A current list of supported assistive tools can be found on the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\"\>Apache OpenOffice Wiki\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345				0	hr	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	hr	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797				0	hr	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	hr	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762				0	hr	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795				0	hr	Supported Assistive Tools				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	hr	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329				0	hr	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628				0	hr	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474				0	hr	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061				0	hr	Supported Input Devices				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	hr	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045				0	hr	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811				0	hr	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379				0	hr	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808				0	hr	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
