helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Changing the Title of a Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156324				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>titles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;document titles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; changing titles\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156324				0	hr	\<variable id=\"change_title\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/change_title.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Title of a Document\"\>Changing the Title of a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3152801				0	hr	You can specify a title for your document. Some file manager utilities can display the titles next to the filenames of your documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	hr	How to change the title of the current document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>. This opens the \<emph\>Properties of\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410				0	hr	Select the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3147242				0	hr	Type the new title in the \<emph\>Title\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\change_title.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100000.xhp\" name=\"Properties of\"\>Properties of\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Crtanje grafike s funkcijama crtanja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145136				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>resizing, see also scaling/zooming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scaling, see also zooming\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; drawing pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; drawings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drawing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; copying when moving in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; adding/editing/copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle drawings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square drawings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>handles; scaling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scaling; objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;moving and resizing with mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;objects, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; object sizes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;scaling/resizing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145136				0	hr	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_drawit\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/insert_graphic_drawit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Graphic Objects\"\>Editing Graphic Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Drawing\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, if it is not already open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	hr	Drawing objects can be subsequently edited and modified. Drawing objects created in this way are vector graphics, which you can scale freely without any loss of quality.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148491				0	hr	To create a rectangle, click the rectangle icon and move your cursor to the place in the document where you want one corner of the rectangle to be. Press the mouse button and hold it down while dragging to the opposite corner of the rectangle. When you release the mouse button, the rectangle is inserted in the document. It is selected, and you can edit its properties through the context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	hr	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon. \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"IMPRESS\"\>To draw multiple objects of the same type, double-click the icon. \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Draw multiple objects of the same type. Click the document without moving the mouse to stop drawing objects.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	hr	If you want to open up draw objects from the center instead of dragging from one corner to the other, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Option\</item\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Alt\</item\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while dragging. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>With some window managers, you may need to hold down also the meta key. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id9448225				0	hr	Holding down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> key while dragging changes the created object. For example, instead of a square with sides of different length, you obtain a square, or vice versa.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153626				0	hr	To scale the objects, first select them by clicking on them with the selection tool. You then see eight handles around the object. When you drag one of the four corner handles, the opposite corner remains fixed while the other three corners move. When you drag one of the side handles, the opposite side remains fixed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id224616				0	hr	To scale a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab repeatedly to highlight one of the handles. Then press an arrow key. To scale in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key. Press Esc to leave the point edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149669				0	hr	To move draw objects, first select them. To select more than one object, press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> key while clicking. Select text objects by clicking exactly on their edge. While holding down the mouse button, drag the objects to the new location. If you hold down \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\> while dragging, the objects can only be positioned in places compatible with the page margins and the other objects on the page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7199316				0	hr	To move a draw object using the keyboard, first select the object, then press an arrow key. To move in smaller steps, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while pressing an arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id7133399316				0	hr	To enter text to be a part of a graphics object, select the object and start typing your text. Click outside the object to end entering text. Double-click text inside an object to edit the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hr	To revert to normal text mode after creating and editing draw objects, click in an area of the document containing no draw or other objects. If you see a drawing cursor, first exit this mode by clicking the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\insert_graphic_drawit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/01140000.xhp\" name=\"Information about the individual icons\"\>Information about the individual icons\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155364				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>protected spaces;inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spaces; inserting protected spaces\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyphens;inserting custom\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional separators\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>separators; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>non-breaking dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;dashes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protected dashes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	hr	\<variable id=\"space_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/space_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\"\>Inserting Protected Spaces, Hyphens and Conditional Separators\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156136				0	hr	Ne-prelamajući razmaci				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	31			0	hr	To prevent two words from being separated at the end of a line, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> when you type a space between the words.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	hr	In Calc, you cannot insert non-breaking spaces.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146957				0	hr	Non-breaking dash				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148538				0	hr	An example of a non-breaking dash is a company name such as A-Z. Obviously you would not want A- to appear at the end of a line and Z at the beginning of the next line. To solve this problem, press Shift+Ctrl+ minus sign. In other words, hold down the Shift and Ctrl keys and press the minus key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163802				0	hr	Hyphen, dash				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154749	66			0	hr	In order to enter longer dashes, you can find under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>\<emph\>- Options\</emph\> the \<emph\>Replace dashes\</emph\> option (only on Windows systems). This option replaces one or two minus signs under certain conditions with an en-dash or an em-dash (see \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040100.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153561	67			0	hr	For additional replacements see the replacements table under \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>\<emph\>- \</emph\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040200.xhp\" name=\"Replace\"\>\<emph\>Replace\</emph\>\</link\>. Here you can, among other things, replace a shortcut automatically by a dash, even in another font.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153825				0	hr	Definite separator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154306	60			0	hr	To support automatic hyphenation by entering a separator inside a word yourself, use the keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+minus sign. The word is separated at this position when it is at the end of the line, even if automatic hyphenation for this paragraph is switched off.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\space_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04100000.xhp\" name=\"Special characters\"\>Special characters\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Uredjivanje legendi dijagrama				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147291				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>charts; editing legends\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>legends; charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; chart legends\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; chart legends\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147291				0	hr	\<variable id=\"chart_legend\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_legend.xhp\" name=\"Editing Chart Legends\"\>Editing Chart Legends\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008				0	hr	To edit a chart legend:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	hr	Double-click on the chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3154824				0	hr	A gray border appears around the chart and the menu bar now contains commands for editing the objects in the chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3153031				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Legend\</emph\> or double-click on the legend. This opens the \<emph\>Legend\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3147210				0	hr	Choose from the available tabs to make modifications, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3145674				0	hr	To select the legend, first double-click on the chart (see step 1), then click on the legend. You can now move the legend within the chart using the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_legend.xhp	0	help	par_id3154347				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Object Properties\"\>Format - Object Properties\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Protecting Records				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>changes; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting; recorded changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>records; protecting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	1			0	hr	\<variable id=\"redlining_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/redlining_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Records\"\>Protecting Records\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id1631824				0	hr	The review function is available in %PRODUCTNAME for text documents and spreadsheet documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	hr	To protect the changes made in a document during editing, choose \<emph\>Edit - Changes - Protect Records\</emph\>. To turn off the function or to accept or reject changes it is necessary to enter the correct password first.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Protect Records\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/password_dlg.xhp\" name=\"Password\"\>\<emph\>Password\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\redlining_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	hr	Enter a password consisting of at least 5 characters and confirm it. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155805				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>tables in text; defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables in spreadsheets;defining borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; around tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;table borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;table borders\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155805				0	hr	\<variable id=\"border_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/border_table.xhp\" name=\"Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\"\>Defining Borders for Tables and Table Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147008				0	hr	Setting a Predefined Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146957				0	hr	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	3			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Table \</emph\>toolbar (Writer) or on the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> bar to open the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	hr	Click one of the predefined border styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156156				0	hr	This \<emph\>adds\</emph\> the selected style to the current border style of the table cells. Select the blank border style at the top left of the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> window to clear all border styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153666				0	hr	Setting a Customized Border Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152472				0	hr	Select the table cells that you want to modify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147265				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties - Borders\</emph\> (Writer) or \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\> (Calc).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	hr	In the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area select the edge(s) that you want to appear in a common layout. Click on an edge in the preview to toggle the selection of an edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id31594132				0	hr	If you select more than one row or column, you can change the middle lines between rows or columns. Select the middle markers in the \<emph\>User-defined\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3153526				0	hr	Select a line style and color for the selected border style in the \<emph\>Line\</emph\> area. These settings apply to all border lines that are included in the selected border style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145606				0	hr	Repeat the last two steps for every border edge.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hr	Select the distance between the border lines and the page contents in the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\border_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149807				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to apply the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Inserting Charts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153910				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>charts; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>plotting data as charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; inserting charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; editing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; chart data\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153910				0	hr	\<variable id=\"chart_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/chart_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Charts\"\>Inserting Charts\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3139133				0	hr	Different methods exist to start a chart:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6772972				0	hr	Insert a chart based on data from cells in Calc or Writer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6049684				0	hr	These charts update automatically when the source data changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2356944				0	hr	Insert a chart with a default data set, and then use the Data Table dialog to enter your own data for that chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id866115				0	hr	These charts can be created in Writer, Impress and Draw. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146763				0	hr	Copy a chart from Calc or Writer into another document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id701315				0	hr	These charts are snapshots of the data at the time of copying. They do not change when the source data changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4439832				0	hr	In Calc, a chart is an object on a sheet, it cannot be a sheet of its own.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id719931				0	hr	Chart in a Calc spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	hr	Click inside the cell range that you want to present in your chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7211218				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Insert Chart\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7549363				0	hr	You see a chart preview and the Chart Wizard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9091769				0	hr	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> to create the chart. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3761406				0	hr	Chart in a Writer text document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155066	32			0	hr	In a Writer document, you can insert a chart based on the values in a Writer table. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id428479				0	hr	Click inside the Writer table. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7236243				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - Chart\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6171452				0	hr	You see a chart preview and the Chart Wizard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	7			0	hr	Follow the instructions in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> to create the chart. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id6436658				0	hr	Chart based on values of its own				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6944792				0	hr	In Writer, if you have not selected any cells, choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - Chart\</emph\> to insert a chart with default data. In Draw or Impress, choose \<emph\>Insert - Chart\</emph\> to insert a chart based on default data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\chart_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	hr	You can change the default data values by double-clicking on the chart and then choosing \<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\" name=\"View - Chart Data Table\"\>\<emph\>View - Chart Data Table\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
