helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10625				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"53251\"\>Specifies compatibility settings for text documents. These options help in fine-tuning %PRODUCTNAME when importing Microsoft Word documents.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	hr	Some of the settings defined here are only valid for the current document and must be defined separately for each document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	hr	Koristi metriku pisača za formatiranje dokumenta				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_PRINTER_METRICS\"\>Specifies that printer metrics are applied for printing and also for formatting the display on the screen.\</ahelp\> If this box is not checked, a printer independent layout will be used for screen display and printing.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155768				0	hr	If you set this option for the current document and then save the document, for example, in an older binary format, this option will not be saved. If you later open the file from the older format, this option will be set by default.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145640				0	hr	Dodaj razmake između odlomaka i tablice (u trenutnom dokumentu)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147339				0	hr	In $[officename] Writer, paragraph spacing is defined differently than in MS Word documents. If you have defined spacing between two paragraphs or tables, spacing is also added in the corresponding MS Word documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST\"\>Specifies whether to add MS Word-compatible spacing between paragraphs and tables in $[officename] Writer text documents.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146317				0	hr	Dodaj razmake na odlomke i tablice pri vrhu stranica (u trenutnom dokumentu)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE:CB_MERGE_PARA_DIST_PAGESTART\"\>Specifies whether paragraph spacing at the top of a page will also be effective at the beginning of a page or column if the paragraph is positioned on the first page of the document.\</ahelp\> The same applies for a page break.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145789				0	hr	If you import an MS Word document, the spaces are automatically added during the conversion.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149964				0	hr	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 tab stop formatting				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152777				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW_CHECKBOX_TP_OPTLOAD_PAGE_CB_TAB_ALIGNMENT\"\>Specifies how to align text at tab stops beyond the right margin, how to handle decimal tab stops, and how to handle tab stops close to a line break.\</ahelp\> If this check box is not selected, tab stops are handled in the same way as in other Office applications.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10810				0	hr	In text documents created by %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION, the new tab stop handling is used by default. In documents created by %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION, the previously used tab stop handling is applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	hr	Nemoj dodavati razmake između linija teksta				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10806				0	hr	Specifies that additional leading (extra space) between lines of text is not added, even if the font in use contains the additional leading attribute.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	hr	In text documents created by %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION, the additional leading is used by default. In documents created by %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION, the additional leading is not used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FF				0	hr	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 line spacing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10815				0	hr	If the option is off, a new process for formatting text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied. If the option is on, the previous method of formatting of text lines with proportional line spacing will be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10818				0	hr	In %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION and Microsoft Word documents of recent versions, the new process is used. In %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION, the previous process is used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081B				0	hr	Dodaj razmake na odlomke i tablice pri dnu ćelija tablica				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10846				0	hr	Specifies that the bottom spacing is added to a paragraph, even when it is the last paragraph in a table cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10849				0	hr	If the option is off, table cells will be formatted as in %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION. If the option is on, an alternative method of formatting table cells will be applied. The option is on by default for new documents created with %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION and for documents imported from Microsoft Word format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084C				0	hr	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 object positioning				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10864				0	hr	Specifies how to calculate the position of floating objects anchored to a character or paragraph with respect to the top and bottom paragraph spacing.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	hr	If the option is on, the floating objects are positioned as in %PRODUCTNAME versions prior to %PRODUCTVERSION. If the option is off, the floating objects are positioned using an alternative method that is similar to the method used by Microsoft Word. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086A				0	hr	The option will be set to off for new documents. For Writer documents created by a version prior to %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION the option is on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10821				0	hr	Use StarOffice 6.0/7 text wrapping around objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id4016541				0	hr	MS Word and Writer have different approaches on wrapping text around floating screen objects. Floating screen object are Writer frames and drawing objects, and the objects 'text box', 'graphic', 'frame', 'picture' etc. in MS Word.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id7280190				0	hr	In MS Word and in %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION, page header/footer content and footnote/endnote content does not wrap around floating screen objects. Text body content wraps around floating screen objects which are anchored in the page header. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id2782982				0	hr	In %PRODUCTNAME prior to %PRODUCTVERSION, the opposite was true.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	hr	If the option is off, which is the default setting, the new text wrapping will be applied. If the option is on, \<emph\>the former text wrapping will be applied.\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092A				0	hr	Uzmite u obzir prijelom linija kod postavljanja objekata				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	hr	Specifies how the complex iterative process of positioning floating objects that are anchored to a character or paragraph should work. In %PRODUCTNAME prior to version %PRODUCTVERSION, an iterative process was used, while in %PRODUCTNAME %PRODUCTVERSION a straightforward process is used, which is similar to the same process in Microsoft Word.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10943				0	hr	If the option is off, the %PRODUCTNAME iterative process of object positioning is used. If the option is on, the straightforward process is used to ensure compatibility with Microsoft Word documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	hd_id5240028				0	hr	Expand word space on lines with manual line breaks in justified paragraphs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id8599810				0	hr	If enabled, Writer adds spacing between words, in lines that end with Shift+Enter in justified paragraphs. If disabled, spacing between words will not be expanded to justify the lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_id8012634				0	hr	This setting is on by default for .odt text documents. It will be saved and loaded with the document in the .odt text document format. This setting cannot be saved in old .sxw text documents, so this setting is off for .sxw text documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10845				0	hr	Koristi kao standard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10848				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"879350288\"\>Click to use the current settings on this tab page as the default for further sessions with %PRODUCTNAME.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\optionen\01041000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10977				0	hr	The factory defaults are set as follows. Enabled are the following options, while all other options are disabled:				20181231 09:50:43
