helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3157892				0	hr	<META NAME="Info field name" CONTENT="Field Content">				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	22			0	hr	When you import an HTML containing these META tags, the contents of the tags are added to the corresponding $[officename] file property box. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id0926200812164481				0	hr	Keywords must be separated by commas. A keyword can contain white space characters or semicolons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163822				0	hr	Import Tips				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155307				0	hr	When you import an HTML document, following META tags are automatically converted to $[officename] fields: <META HTTP-EQUIV="REFRESH"...> and <META NAME="..." ...> , where NAME equals to AUTHOR, CREATED, CHANGED, CHANGEDBY, DESCRIPTION, KEYWORDS or CLASSIFICATION.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146				0	hr	Scripts, comments, and META tags that are positioned directly before a TABLE tag are inserted in the first cell of the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	hr	Scripts and META tags in the header of an HTML document are imported and anchored to the first paragraph in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	hr	To set the options for importing HTML tags, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>. A known META tag contains either "HTTP-EQUIV" or "NAME", and are imported as $[officename] notes. The only exception is <META NAME="GENERATOR"...>, which is ignored.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163717				0	hr	Export Tips				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180				0	hr	Notes and script fields at the beginning of the first paragraph in a document are exported to the header of an HTML document. If the document begins with a table, the first paragraph in the first cell of the table is exported to the header of the HTML document.				20181231 09:50:43
