helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150999				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02250000.xhp\" name=\"Bibliography Database\"\>Bibliography Database\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149119				0	hr	\<variable id=\"litdattext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BIB_DB_TBX\"\>Insert, delete, edit, and organize records in the bibliography database.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346				0	hr	If the fields in your database are read-only, ensure that the data source view is closed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150506				0	hr	The supplied bibliography database contains sample records of books about $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155356				0	hr	Use the toolbar to select a table in the bibliography database, to search for records, or to sort the records using filters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163802				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/source\"\>Lists the available tables in the current database. Click a name in the list to display the records for that table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3158432				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GRID_TRAVEL_FIRST\"\>Go to the first record in the table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149192				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GRID_TRAVEL_PREV\"\>Go to the previous record in the table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146795				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GRID_TRAVEL_NEXT\"\>Go to the next record in the table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144760				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GRID_TRAVEL_LAST\"\>Go to the last record in the table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157960				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GRID_TRAVEL_ABSOLUTE\"\>Type the number of the record that you want to display, and then press Enter.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	hr	Inserting a New Record				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149168	6			0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_GRID_TRAVEL_NEW\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Inserts a new record into the current table.\</ahelp\>To create a record, click the asterisk (*) button at the bottom of the table view. An empty row is added at the end of the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152920				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BIB_AUTHORITYTYPE_POS\"\>Select the type of record that you want to create. $[officename] inserts a number in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> column of the record that corresponds to the type that you select here.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156423				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BIB_IDENTIFIER_POS\"\>Enter a name for the record. The name appears in the \<emph\>Identifier\</emph\> column in the list of records.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155994				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_BIB_URL_POS\"\>Enter additional information for the selected record. If you want, you can also enter the information in the corresponding field in the table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163716				0	hr	Finding and Filtering Records				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147478				0	hr	You can search for records by matching a keyword to a field entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159181				0	hr	Entering Search key				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159125	11			0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/query\"\>Type the information that you want to search for, and then press Enter. To change the filter options for the search, long-click the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> icon, and then select a different data field. You can use wildcards such as % or * for any number of characters, and _ or ? for one character in your search. To display all of the records in the table, clear this box, and then press Enter. \</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155511				0	hr	SamoFiltar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/autoFilter\"\>Long-click to select the data field that you want to search using the term that you entered in the \<emph\>Search Key\</emph\> box. You can only search one data field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	hr	The list of table records is automatically updated to match the new filter settings.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590	30			0	hr	Use the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> to refine and to combine \<emph\>AutoFilter \</emph\>search options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155311				0	hr	To display all of the records in a table, click the \<emph\>Remove Filter\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147580				0	hr	Deleting a Record				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154471				0	hr	To delete a record in the current table, right-click the row header of the record, and then select \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. \<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETEROWS\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Deletes the selected record.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152941				0	hr	Changing the data source				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147214				0	hr	Izvor podataka				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151118				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/sdbsource\"\>Select the data source for the bibliography database.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	hr	Smještaj stupaca				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151282	36			0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/Mapping\"\>Lets you map the column headings to data fields from a different data source. To define a different data source for your bibliography, click the\<emph\> Data Source\</emph\> button on the record\<emph\> Object Bar\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"BIB_LISTBOX_RID_DLG_MAPPING_LB_CUSTOM4\"\>Select the data field that you want to map to the current \<emph\>Column name\</emph\>. To change the available data fields, select a different data source for your bibliography.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153947				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/DeleteRecord\"\>Deletes the current record.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151019				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/DeleteRecord\"\>Lets you choose a different data source for your bibliography.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02250000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153730				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Bib/InsertRecord\"\>Inserts a new record into the current table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Popis regularnih izraza				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146765				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>regular expressions; list of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146765				0	hr	\<variable id=\"02100001\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\"\>List of Regular Expressions\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149741				0	hr	Znak				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	hr	Rezultat/korištenje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id6600543				0	hr	Any character				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9824518.00000001				0	hr	Represents any single character unless otherwise specified.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152427				0	hr	.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149031				0	hr	Represents any single character except for a line break or paragraph break. For example, the search term "sh.rt" returns both "shirt" and "short".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154682				0	hr	^				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155351				0	hr	Only finds the search term if the term is at the beginning of a paragraph. Special objects such as empty fields or character-anchored frames, at the beginning of a paragraph are ignored. Example: "^Peter".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	hr	kn				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152542				0	hr	Only finds the search term if the term appears at the end of a paragraph. Special objects such as empty fields or character-anchored frames at the end of a paragraph are ignored. Example: "Peter$".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156414				0	hr	*				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	hr	Finds zero or more of the characters in front of the "*". For example, "Ab*c" finds "Ac", "Abc", "Abbc", "Abbbc", and so on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	hr	+				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	hr	Finds one or more of the characters in front of the "+". For example, "AX.+4" finds "AXx4", but not "AX4".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	hr	The longest possible string that matches this search pattern in a paragraph is always found. If the paragraph contains the string "AX 4 AX4", the entire passage is highlighted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	hr	?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153684				0	hr	Finds zero or one of the characters in front of the "?". For example, "Texts?" finds "Text" and "Texts" and "x(ab|c)?y" finds "xy", "xaby", or "xcy".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	hr	\\				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	hr	Search interprets the special character that follows the "\\" as a normal character and not as a regular expression (except for the combinations \\n, \\t, \\>, and \\<). For example, "tree\\." finds "tree.", not "treed" or "trees".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945				0	hr	\\n				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153700				0	hr	Represents a line break that was inserted with the Shift+Enter key combination. To change a line break into a paragraph break, enter \<emph\>\\n\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> and \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> boxes, and then perform a search and replace.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9262672				0	hr	\\n in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box stands for a line break that was inserted with the Shift+Enter key combination.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2366100				0	hr	\\n in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box stands for a paragraph break that can be entered with the Enter or Return key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153258				0	hr	\\t				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3157809				0	hr	Represents a tab. You can also use this expression in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150670				0	hr	\\<				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	hr	Only finds the search term if it appears at the beginning of a word. For example, "\\<book" finds "bookmark", but not "checkbook".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149576				0	hr	^$				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	hr	Finds an empty paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	hr	^.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	hr	Finds the first character of a paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282				0	hr	& WTF				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153961				0	hr	Adds the string that was found by the search criteria in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box to the term in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box when you make a replacement.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149650				0	hr	For example, if you enter "window" in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box and "&frame" in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, the word "window" is replaced with "windowframe".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150543				0	hr	You can also enter an "&" in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box to modify the \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> of the string found by the search criteria.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	hr	[abc123]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154630				0	hr	Represents one of the characters that are between the brackets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156293				0	hr	[a-e]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167				0	hr	Represents any of the characters that are between a and e.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id100520090232005				0	hr	The characters are ordered by their code numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155994				0	hr	[a-eh-x]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148676				0	hr	Represents any of the characters that are between a-e and h-x.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145318				0	hr	[^a-s]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153351				0	hr	Represents any character that is not between a and s.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156543				0	hr	\\xXXXX				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hr	Represents a special character based on its four-digit hexadecimal code (XXXX).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252				0	hr	The code for the special character depends on the font used. You can view the codes by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Special Character\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	hr	|				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154985				0	hr	Pronalazi izraze koji se javljaju prije ili nakon "|". Na primjer, "ovo|ono" pronalazi "ovo" i "ono".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147376				0	hr	{2}				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	hr	Defines the number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket occurs. For example, "tre{2}" finds "tree".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151289				0	hr	{1,2}				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	hr	Defines the number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket can occur. For example, "tre{1,2}" finds both "tree" and "treated".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id4870754				0	hr	{1,}				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id843836				0	hr	Defines the minimum number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket can occur. For example, "tre{2,}" finds "tree", "treee", and "treeeee".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	hr	( )				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2701803				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	hr	Defines the characters inside the parentheses as a reference. You can then refer to the first reference in the current expression with "\\1", to the second reference with "\\2", and so on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156061				0	hr	For example, if your text contains the number 13487889 and you search using the regular expression (8)7\\1\\1, "8788" is found.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	hr	You can also use () to group terms, for example, "a(bc)?d" finds "ad" or "abcd".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9200109				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5766472				0	hr	Use $ (dollar) instead of \\ (backslash) to replace references. Use $0 to replace the whole found string.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154790				0	hr	[:alpha:]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	hr	Represents an alphabetic character. Use [:alpha:]+ to find one or more of them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	hr	[:digit:]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	hr	Represents a decimal digit. Use [:digit:]+ to find one or more of them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153743				0	hr	[:alnum:]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153281				0	hr	Represents an alphanumeric character ([:alpha:] and [:digit:]).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	hr	[:space:]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	hr	Represents a white space character such as space.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	hr	[:print:]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	hr	Represents a printable character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	hr	[:cntrl:]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	hr	Represents a nonprinting character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	hr	[:lower:]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145730				0	hr	Represents a lowercase character if \<emph\>Match case\</emph\> is selected in \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	hr	[:upper:]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150092	231			0	hr	Represents an uppercase character if \<emph\>Match case\</emph\> is selected in \<emph\>Options.\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id5311441				0	hr	Examples				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id956834773				0	hr	e([:digit:])?    -- finds 'e' followed by zero or one digit. Note that currently all named character classes like [:digit:] must be enclosed in parentheses.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id952368773				0	hr	^([:digit:])$    -- finds lines or cells with exactly one digit.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9568773				0	hr	You can combine the search terms to form complex searches.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id71413				0	hr	To find three-digit numbers alone in a paragraph				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2924283				0	hr	^[:digit:]{3}$				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	hr	^ means the match has to be at the start of a paragraph, 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	hr	[:digit:] matches any decimal digit, 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	hr	{3} means there must be exactly 3 copies of "digit", 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	hr	$ means the match must end a paragraph. 				20181231 09:50:43
