helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03110000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3160463				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>full screen view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen; full screen views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>complete screen view\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;full screen\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03110000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3160463				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/03110000.xhp\" name=\"Full Screen\"\>Full Screen\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:FullScreen\"\>Shows or hides the menus and toolbars in Writer or Calc. To exit the full screen mode, click the \<emph\>Full Screen On/Off\</emph\> button.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152594				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FULLSCREENTOOLBOX\"\>In Writer and Calc, you can also use the shortcut keys \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+J to switch between the normal and full screen mode.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\03110000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154318	28			0	hr	You can still use shortcut keys in \<emph\>Full Screen\</emph\> mode, even though the menus are unavailable. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>To open the\<emph\> View\</emph\> menu, press Alt+V. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05290000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Grupa				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05290000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150603				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05290000.xhp\" name=\"Group\"\>Group\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05290000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153323				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Groups keep together selected objects, so that they can be moved or formatted as a single object.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05290000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150943				0	hr	Working with groups				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05290000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152909				0	hr	To edit the individual objects of a group, select the group, right-click, and then choose \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<emph\>Enter Group\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Group - Enter Group\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05290000.xhp	0	help	par_id3159158				0	hr	When you are editing a group, the objects that are not part of the group are faded.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05290000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	hr	Use Tab and Shift+Tab to move forwards and backwards through the objects in a group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05290000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154810				0	hr	To exit a group, right-click, and then choose \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"DRAW\"\>\<emph\>Exit Group\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Group - Exit Group\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20181231 09:50:43
