helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205	2			0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_IMAPDLG_UNDO\"\>Reverses the last command or the last entry you typed. To select the command that you want to reverse, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Undo \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10630				0	hr	To change the number of commands that you can undo, choose Tools - Options - $[officename] - Memory, and enter a new value in the number of steps box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3163803				0	hr	Some commands (for example, editing Styles) cannot be undone.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	hr	You can cancel the Undo command by choosing Edit - Redo.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166410				0	hr	About the Undo command in database tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148492				0	hr	When you are working with database tables, you can only undo the last command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155504	4			0	hr	If you change the content of a record in a database table that has not been saved, and then use the\<emph\> Undo\</emph\> command, the record is erased.				20181231 09:50:43
