helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3152482				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>Specifies the link type of the selected link.\</ahelp\> Queries about the various types of links differ in the number of records displayed. The following options are available:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155334				0	hr	Inner Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the internal join, the results table contains only the records for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link is created by a corresponding WHERE clause.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156372				0	hr	Lijevi Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the left join, the results table contains all fields of the left table and only those fields of the right table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the LEFT OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155607				0	hr	Right Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150647				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>With the right join, the results table contains all fields of the right table and only those fields of the left table for which the content of the linked fields is the same.\</ahelp\> In $[officename] SQL this type of link corresponds to the RIGHT OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158215				0	hr	Full Join				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id3163665				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_QRY_JOINTYPE\"\>For a full join, the results table contains all fields of the left and right tables.\</ahelp\> In the SQL of $[officename] this type of link corresponds to the FULL OUTER JOIN command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200912031976				0	hr	Natural				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010101.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200912031977				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Inserts the keyword NATURAL into the SQL statement that defines the relation. The relation joins all columns that have the same column name in both tables. The resulting joined table contains only one column for each pair of equally named columns.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Sorting and Grouping				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3486434				0	hr	\<variable id=\"rep_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_sort.xhp\"\>Sorting and Grouping\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the Sorting and Grouping dialog of \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Design\</link\>, you can define the fields that should be sorted in your report, and the fields that should be kept together to form a group.\</ahelp\> If you group your report by a certain field, all records with the same value of that field will be kept together in one group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id876186				0	hr	The Groups box shows the fields in an order from top to bottom. You can select any field, then click the Move Up or Move Down button to move this field up or down in the list. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	hr	The sorting and grouping will be applied in the order of the list from top to bottom.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Lists the fields that will be used for sorting or grouping. The field at the top has the highest priority, the second field has the second priority, and so on.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to open a list from which you can select a field.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field up in the list.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Moves the selected field down in the list.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the sorting order.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Header.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to show or hide the Group Footer.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select to create a new group on each changed value, or on other properties.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id0409200922142041				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Removes the selected field from the list.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	hr	By default a new group is created on every changed value of a record from the selected field. You can change this property depending on the type of field:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	hr	For fields of type Text, you can select Prefix Characters and enter a number n of characters in the text box below. The records which are identical in the first n characters will be grouped together.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7112338				0	hr	For fields of type Date/Time, you can group the records by the same year, quarter, month, week, day, hour, or minute. You can additionally specify an interval for weeks and hours: 2 weeks groups data in biweekly groups, 12 hours groups data in half-day groups.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	hr	For fields of type AutoNumber, Currency, or Number, you specify an interval.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the group interval value that records are grouped by.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the level of detail by which a group is kept together on the same page.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	hr	When you specify to keep together some records on the same page, you have three choices:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	hr	No - page boundaries are not taken into account.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	hr	Whole Group - prints the group header, detail section, and group footer on the same page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id9089022				0	hr	With First Detail - prints the group header on a page only if the first detail record also can be printed on the same page.				20181231 09:50:43
