helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id1821955				0	hr	\<variable id=\"rep_navigator\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_navigator.xhp\"\>Report Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1150852				0	hr	You can open the Report Navigator window of the \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/rep_main.xhp\"\>Report Designer\</link\> by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Report Navigator\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1111484				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The Report Navigator reveals the structure of the report. You can use the Report Navigator to insert functions into the report.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id8314157				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click an entry in the Report Navigator. The corresponding object or area is selected in the Report Design view. Right-click an entry to open the context menu.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id2932828				0	hr	To enter functions to the report				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>In the context menu of the Report Navigator, you see the same commands as in the Report Design view, plus additional commands to create new functions or to delete them.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	hr	Functions can be entered using a syntax as specified by the \<link href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenFormula\"\>OpenFormula\</link\> proposal.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id4095583				0	hr	See \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Database\"\>Wiki page about Base\</link\> for some more help regarding the functions in a report.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	hd_id311593				0	hr	To calculate a sum for each client				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id3948789				0	hr	Open the Report Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id5391399				0	hr	Open the Groups entry and the group where you want to calculate the cost. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6989654				0	hr	The group has a sub entry called functions. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1803643				0	hr	Open the context menu (right click) on the functions entry, choose to create a new function, and select it. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id868251				0	hr	In the property browser you see the function. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6247749				0	hr	Change the name to e.g. CostCalc and the formula to [CostCalc] + [enter your cost column name].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1565904				0	hr	In the initial value enter 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1569261				0	hr	Now you can insert a text field and bind it to your [CostCalc] (appears in the data field list box).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9256874				0	hr	Maybe you have to set the initial value to the value of the field like [field].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id4601886				0	hr	If there are blank fields in the cost column, use the following formula to replace the blank fields' content with zero:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id1754509				0	hr	[SumCost] + IF(ISBLANK([field]);0;[field])				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the formula that defines the function. Use OpenFormula syntax.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the initial value to be displayed before the function is evaluated.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Deep traversing is enabled, functions are evaluated considering all lower levels of hierarchy.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\rep_navigator.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If Pre evaluation is enabled, functions are evaluated considering all lower levels of hierarchy.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
