helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Math shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	hr	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcuts ($[officename] Math Accessibility)\"\>Shortcuts ($[officename] Math Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150298				0	hr	You can control $[officename] Math without a mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150343				0	hr	Inserting a Formula Directly				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	hr	If you want to insert a formula into a text document, and you already know the correct writing, you can proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	hr	Write the formula into your text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	hr	Select the formula				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	hr	Choose the command \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154767				0	hr	Inserting a Formula using a Window				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	hr	If you want to use the $[officename] Math interface to edit a formula, choose the command \<emph\>Insert - Object - Formula\</emph\> without any text selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	hr	The cursor waits in the Commands window and you can type the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	hr	You can compose formulas using the Selection window. Open it with the menu \<emph\>View - Selection\</emph\> if it is not already open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155625				0	hr	If the Selection window is open, use F6 to switch from the Commands window to the Selection window and back.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154554				0	hr	Selection window				20181231 09:50:43
