helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145792				0	hr	\<variable id=\"attributes\"\>\<link href=\"text/smath/guide/attributes.xhp\" name=\"Changing Default Attributes\"\>Changing Default Attributes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154484				0	hr	Can default formats in $[officename] Math be modified?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870				0	hr	Some parts of formulas are always formatted bold or italic by default.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	hr	You can remove these attributes using "nbold" and "nitalic". Example:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3143231				0	hr	a + b				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810				0	hr	nitalic a + bold b.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\attributes.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	hr	In the second formula, the a is not italic. The b is bold. You cannot change the plus sign by this method.				20181231 09:50:43
