helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215				0	hr	Adding a New Symbol				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3143233				0	hr	To add a symbol to a symbol set, select a font in the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> box, and then click a symbol in symbols pane. In the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> box, type a name for the symbol. In the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box, select a symbol set, or type a new name to create a new symbol set. The right preview pane displays the symbol that you selected. Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389				0	hr	Modifying the Name of a Symbol				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147296				0	hr	To change the name of a symbol, select the old name in the \<emph\>Old symbol\</emph\> list box. Then enter the new name in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> box. Check whether the desired character is in the preview window before you click the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157870				0	hr	Symbol Set				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145825				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_5\"\>The \<emph\>Symbol s\</emph\>\<emph\>et\</emph\> list box contains the names of all existing symbol sets. You can modify a symbol set or create a new one.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154554				0	hr	Creating a New Symbol Set				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145594				0	hr	To create a new symbol set, type a name for it in the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box and add at least one symbol. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog. The new symbol set is now available under the new name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153736				0	hr	Pismo				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Displays the name of the current font and enables you to select a different font.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150564				0	hr	Podskup				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145295				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_LB_FONTS_SUBSET\"\>If you selected a non-symbol font in the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> list box, you can select a Unicode subset in which to place your new or edited symbol. When a subset has been selected, all symbols belonging to this subset of the current symbol set are displayed in the symbols list above.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148386				0	hr	Oblik pisma				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_COMBOBOX_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_3\"\>The current typeface is displayed. You can change the typeface by selecting one from the list box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156262				0	hr	Dodaj				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153922				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_1\"\>Click this button to add the symbol shown in the right preview window to the current symbol set.\</ahelp\> It will be saved under the name displayed in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> list box. You must specify a name under \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> or \<emph\>Symbol Set\</emph\> to be able to use this button. Names cannot be used more than once.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150756				0	hr	Izmijeni				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147570				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_2\"\>Click this button to replace the name of the symbol shown in the left preview window (the old name is displayed in the \<emph\>Old symbol\</emph\> list box) with the new name you have entered in the \<emph\>Symbol\</emph\> list box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154640				0	hr	Moving a Symbol to Another Symbol Set				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151174				0	hr	As an example, to transfer the large ALPHA from the "Greek" set to the "Special" set, select the old set (Greek) and then the ALPHA symbol using the two top list boxes. The symbol appears in the left preview window. In the \<emph\>Symbol set\</emph\> list box, select the "Special" set. Click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> and then \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The ALPHA symbol is now only in the "Special" symbol set.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145414				0	hr	Obriši				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_PUSHBUTTON_RID_SYMDEFINEDIALOG_3\"\>Click to remove the symbol shown in the left preview window from the current symbol set.\</ahelp\> There will be no security query. Deleting the last remaining symbol of a symbol set also deletes the symbol set.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527				0	hr	You can also click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> at any time to close the dialog without saving any of the changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090903.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Symbols with Indices				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090903.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155959				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090903.xhp\" name=\"Symbols with Indices\"\>Symbols with Indices\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090903.xhp	0	help	par_id3150300				0	hr	A third example of how to use \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\> to create symbols with indexes is shown below. You can copy the example into the clipboard and use it in your own formula in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
