helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150208				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_NEXTMARK\"\>Moves the cursor to the next marker (to the right).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149051				0	hr	"Markers" are placeholders. They take the form of <?> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090904.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Matrix with Varying Font Sizes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090904.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155960				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090904.xhp\" name=\"Matrix with Varying Font Sizes\"\>Matrix with Varying Font Sizes\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090904.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	hr	Here is an example of how to create a matrix with varying font sizes in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can copy this example to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window using the clipboard and use it in your own formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090904.xhp	0	help	par_id3153915				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3150213\" src=\"res/helpimg/smzb5.png\" width=\"16.51cm\" height=\"4.971cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150213\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090904.xhp	0	help	par_id3146965				0	hr	func G^{(%alpha" ," %beta)}_{ x_m x_n} = left[ matrix { arctan(%alpha) # arctan(%beta) ## x_m + x_n # x_m - x_n }right]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090500.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	(Uglate) zagrade				20181231 09:50:43
