helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Import formula				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154659				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>importing; %PRODUCTNAME Math formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154660				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>MathML; import from file\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659				0	hr	Import Formula from File				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150251				0	hr	\<variable id=\"formelimportierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ImportFormula\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This command opens a dialog for importing a formula.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153916				0	hr	The \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> dialog is set up like the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Open\"\>Open\</link\> dialog under \<emph\>File\</emph\>. Use the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> dialog to load, edit and display a formula saved as a file in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153917				0	hr	You can import MathML files created by other applications as well. The MathML source must have a \<item type=\"code\"\>math\</item\> element with an \<item type=\"code\"\>xmlns\</item\> attribute with value "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML". The languages MathML and StarMath are not fully compatible, therefore you should revise the import result. For details about the language MathML see its \<link href=\"http://www.w3.org/TR/#tr_MathML\"\>specification\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154661				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>MathML; import via clipboard\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154662				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>importing; MathML\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154661				0	hr	Import MathML from Clipboard				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150252				0	hr	\<variable id=\"mathmlimportierentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ImportMathMLClipboard\" visibility=\"visible\"\>This command transforms MathML clipboard content to StarMath and inserts it at the current cursor position.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153918				0	hr	If the transformation fails, nothing is inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\06020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153919				0	hr	This command handles only MathML content. If you have copied a %PRODUCTNAME Math formula to clipboard, insert it using the command \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02060000.xhp\" name=\"Paste\"\>Paste\</link\> under \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Veličine pisama				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153816				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>font sizes; in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sizes; of fonts in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153816				0	hr	Veličine pisama				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	hr	\<variable id=\"schriftgroessentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FONTSIZE\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Use this dialog to specify the font sizes for your formula. Select a base size and all elements of the formula will be scaled in relation to this base.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146968				0	hr	Osnovna veličina				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145115				0	hr	\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\"STARMATH:METRICFIELD:RID_FONTSIZEDIALOG:1\"\>All elements of a formula are proportionally scaled to the base size.  To change the base size, select or type in the desired point (pt) size from the \<emph\>Base size\</emph\> \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#drehfeld\" name=\"spin box\"\>spin box\</link\>. You can also use other units of measure or other \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#metrik\" name=\"metrics\"\>metrics\</link\>, which are then automatically converted to points.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153005				0	hr	To permanently change the default size (12 pt) used in $[officename] Math, you must first set the size (for example, 11 pt) in the \<emph\>Basic size\</emph\> spin box and then click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153735				0	hr	Relative Sizes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	hr	In this section, you can determine the relative sizes for each type of element with reference to the base size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150935				0	hr	Tekst				20181231 09:50:43
