helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03060000.xhp\" name=\"Display All\"\>Display All\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148571				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_ADJUST\"\>Displays the entire formula in the maximum size possible so that all elements are included. The formula is reduced or enlarged so that all formula elements can be displayed in the work area. \<emph\>Show All\</emph\> is equivalent to the \<emph\>Entire Formula\</emph\> icon on the toolbar.\</ahelp\> The current scale is displayed on the status bar. A selection of available scale options is accessible through the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#kontextmenue\" name=\"context menu\"\>context menu\</link\>. The context menu in the work area also contains the scale options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Pisma				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156261				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>fonts; in $[officename] Math\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formula fonts; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; formula fonts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156261				0	hr	Pisma				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153716				0	hr	\<variable id=\"schriftartentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FONT\"\>Defines the fonts that can be applied to formula elements.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154639				0	hr	Formula Fonts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	hr	You can define fonts for the variables, functions, numbers and inserted text that form the elements of your formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156318				0	hr	The list boxes in the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialog display a default font for all elements. To change to a different font, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>, then select the element type. A new dialog box appears. Select the desired font and check any desired attributes, then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. To set the changes as the default fonts, click the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148831				0	hr	If you want to mark individual text segments with a font other than that used for the whole text, then enter the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010000.xhp\" name=\"FONT\"\>Font\</link\> command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	hr	Varijable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147516				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH_LISTBOX_RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG_1\"\>You can select the fonts for the variables in your formula.\</ahelp\> For example, in the formula x=SIN(y), x and y are variables, and will reflect the assigned font.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150708				0	hr	Funkcije				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152950				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:2\"\>Select the fonts for names and properties of functions.\</ahelp\> For example, the functions in the formula x=SIN(y) are =SIN( ).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149805				0	hr	Brojevi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154610				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:3\"\>You can select the fonts for the numbers in your formula.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153529				0	hr	Tekst				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153780				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:4\"\>Define the fonts for the text in your formula here.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152963				0	hr	Custom Fonts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154566				0	hr	In this section of the \<emph\>Fonts\</emph\> dialog you can define fonts, with which you can format other text components in the formula. The three basic fonts \<emph\>Serif, Sans\</emph\> and \<emph\>Fixed\</emph\> are available. You can add any other font to each standard installed basic font. Every font installed on your system is available for you to use. Select the \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> button to expand the selection offered in the list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151315	17			0	hr	These custom fonts are used if you set a different font with the FONT command in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153670				0	hr	Serif				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151108				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:5\"\>You can specify the font to be used for the \<emph\>font serif\</emph\> format.\</ahelp\> Serifs are the small "guides" that can be seen, for example, at the bottom of a capital A when the Times serif font is used. Using serifs is quite helpful since it guides a reader's eye in a straight line and can speed up reading.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150836				0	hr	Bez				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:6\"\>You can specify the font to be used for \<emph\>sans\</emph\> font formatting.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149340				0	hr	Fiksno				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154198				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:LISTBOX:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:7\"\>You can specify the font to be used for \<emph\>fixed\</emph\> font formatting.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159194				0	hr	Izmijeni				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\05010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146932				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"STARMATH:MENUBUTTON:RID_FONTTYPEDIALOG:1\"\>Click one of the choices from this pop-up menu to access the \<link href=\"text/smath/01/05010100.xhp\" name=\"Fonts\"\>Fonts\</link\> dialog, where you can define the font and attributes for the respective formula and for custom fonts.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
