helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153545	74			0	hr	To create the \<emph\>much greater than\</emph\> relation with two placeholders, type \<emph\><?> gg <?> \</emph\>or \<emph\>>>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156000				0	hr	Type \<emph\>ll\</emph\> or \<emph\><<\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window to insert the \<emph\>much less than\</emph\> relation into the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153749				0	hr	The \<emph\>is defined as\</emph\> relation with two placeholders is inserted by typing \<emph\><?>def<?>\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154068				0	hr	Insert the \<emph\>picture by\</emph\> correspondence character with two placeholders by typing \<emph\><?> transl <?>\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149592				0	hr	The \<emph\><?>transr<?>\</emph\> command inserts the \<emph\>original by\</emph\> correspondence character with two placeholders.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154735				0	hr	When entering information manually in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window, note that a number of operators require spaces for the correct structure. This is especially true if you are working with values instead of placeholders. For example, for the "is considerably greater" relation, type either \<emph\>10 gg 1\</emph\> or \<emph\>a gg b\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
