helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\02090000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	hr	"Markers" are placeholders. They take the form of <?> in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Matrix in Bold Font				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/smath/01/03090906.xhp\" name=\"Matrix in Bold Font\"\>Matrix in Bold Font\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	hr	Here is an example of how to create a bold font matrix in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>. You can copy this example to the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window using the clipboard and use it in your own formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/smzb6.png\" width=\"9.511cm\" height=\"7.99cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090906.xhp	0	help	par_id3154763				0	hr	bold { f(x", "y) = left [ stack { x + y over z + left lbrace matrix { 2 # 3 # 4 ## 4 # 5 # 6 ## 6 # 7 # 8} right rbrace # {y + sin (x)} over %alpha # z + y over g } right ]}				20181231 09:50:43
