helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3004547				0	hr	The open, low, high, and closing values of a row build together one data unit in the chart. A stock price data series consists of several rows containing such data units. The column containing the transaction volume builds an optional second data series.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6401867				0	hr	Depending on the chosen variant, you do not need all columns.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id18616				0	hr	Stock Chart Variants				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	hr	Choose the \<emph\>Stock\</emph\> chart type on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart wizard\</link\>. Then select one of the four variants.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4569231				0	hr	Tip 1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	hr	Based on\<emph\> low\</emph\>\<emph\>and high \</emph\>column the Type 1 shows the distance between bottom price (low) and top price (high) by a vertical line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	hr	Based on\<emph\> low, high,\</emph\> and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column Type 1 shows an additional horizontal mark for the closing price.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5947141				0	hr	Tip 2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	hr	Based on \<emph\>open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column Type 2 generates the traditional "candle stick" chart. Type 2 draws the vertical line between the bottom and top price and adds a rectangle in front, which visualizes the range between the opening and closing price. %PRODUCTNAME uses different fill colors for raising values (the opening price is lower than the closing price) and falling values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	hr	Tip 3				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	hr	Based on \<emph\>volume, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\> column chart Type 3 draws a chart like Type 1, with additional bars for the transaction volume.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4313791				0	hr	Tip 4				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	hr	Based on all five data columns \<emph\>volume, open, low, high\</emph\>, and \<emph\>close\</emph\>, Type 4 combines a chart of Type 2 with a bar chart for the transaction volume.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	hr	Because measurement for transaction volume might be "units", a second y axis is introduced in chart Type 3 and Type 4. The price axis is shown on the right side and the volume axis on the left side.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id2318796				0	hr	Setting the Data Source				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id399182				0	hr	Charts based on its own data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5298318				0	hr	To change the data series of a chart having its own data, choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/03010000.xhp\"\>Chart Data Table\</link\> from the View menu or from the context menu of the chart in edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	hr	In an embedded chart data table, the data series are always organized in columns.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	hr	For a new stock chart first use a column chart. Add the columns you need and enter your data in the order which are shown in the example, leave out the columns you do not need for the desired variant. Use Switch Columns to change the column order. Close the chart data table. Now use the Chart Type dialog to change to the stock chart variant. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6182744				0	hr	If you have already got a stock chart and you want to change the variant, then first change the chart type to a column chart, add or remove columns so that it fits to the variant, and then change the chart type back to a stock chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	hr	Do not write the name of a data series in a row. Write the name into the field above the role name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	hr	The order of the rows determines how the categories are arranged in the chart. Use Switch Rows to change the order.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id888698				0	hr	Charts based on Calc or Writer tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3394573				0	hr	You can choose or alter a data range on the second page of the Chart wizard or in the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_range.xhp\"\>Data Range\</link\> dialog. For fine tuning use the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_data_series.xhp\"\>Data Series\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7594225				0	hr	To specify a data range do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id5081637				0	hr	Enter the data range in the text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9759514				0	hr	In Calc, an example data range would be "$Sheet1.$B$3:$B$14". Note that a data range may consist of more than one region in a spreadsheet, e.g. "$Sheet1.A1:A5;$Sheet1.D1:D5" is also a valid data range. In Writer, an example data range would be "Table1.A1:E4".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1614429				0	hr	As long as the syntax is not correct, %PRODUCTNAME shows the text in red.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id1589098				0	hr	In Calc, click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog, then drag to select the data range. When you release the mouse, the data are entered. Click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> again to add a data range. In the input field of the minimized dialog, click after the entry and type a semicolon. Then drag to select the next range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id8746910				0	hr	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	hr	Your stock chart data are "in columns", if the information in a row belongs to the same "candle stick".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id5675527				0	hr	Fine Tuning the Data Ranges of Table Based Stock Charts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3486434				0	hr	You can organize data series and edit the source for parts of single data series on the third page of the Chart wizard or on the page Data Series in the Data Range dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id3068636				0	hr	Organize Data Series				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2480849				0	hr	In the part data series on the left side of the dialog, you can organize the data series of the actual chart. A stock chart has at least one data series containing the prices. It might have a second data series for transaction volume.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id4181951				0	hr	If you have got more than one price data series, use the up and down arrows to order them. The order determines the arrangement in the chart. Do the same for volume data series. You cannot switch price and volume data series.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2927335				0	hr	To remove a data series, select the data series in the list and click Remove.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2107303				0	hr	To add a data series, select one of the existing data series and click Add. You get an empty entry below the selected one, which has the same type. If you have no price data series or no volume data series, you must first select a range for these series in the Data Range dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id4071779				0	hr	Setting Data Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7844477				0	hr	In the Data Ranges dialog you can set or change the data range of each component of the selected data series.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id6478469				0	hr	In the upper list you see the role name of the components and the current values. When you have selected a role, you can change the value in the text box below the list. The label shows the selected role. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	hr	Enter the range into the text box or click on \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	hr	Select Open Values, Close Values, High Values, and Low Values in any order. Specify only the ranges for those roles which you need for the chosen variant of the stock chart. The ranges need not be next to each other in the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	hd_id876186				0	hr	Legenda				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	hr	The legend displays the labels from the first row or column or from the special range that you have set in the Data Series dialog. If your chart does not contain labels, the legend displays text like "Row 1, Row 2, ...", or "Column A, Column B, ..." according to the row number or column letter of the chart data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2377697				0	hr	The legend shows the value from the range, which you entered in the \<emph\>Range for Name\</emph\> field in the \<emph\>Data Range\</emph\> dialog. The default entry is the column header of the closing price column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_stock.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	hr	Select one of the position options. When the chart is finished, you can specify other positions using the Format menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Chart Type Line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id2187566				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;line\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9422894				0	hr	\<variable id=\"type_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Line\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id389721				0	hr	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826349				0	hr	Linija				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2334665				0	hr	A line chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series can be connected by a line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8956572				0	hr	Points only - this subtype plots only points.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id500808				0	hr	Points and lines - this subtype plots points and connects points of the same data series by a line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8366649				0	hr	Lines only - this subtype plots only lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id476393				0	hr	3D lines - this subtype connects points of the same data series by a 3D line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2655720				0	hr	Mark \<emph\>Stack series\</emph\> to arrange the points' y values cumulative above each other. The y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the first column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked points. If you select \<emph\>Percent\</emph\>, the y values are scaled as percentage of the category total.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3682058				0	hr	Mark \<emph\>Smooth lines\</emph\> to draw curves through the points instead of straight lines. Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> for a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/smooth_line_properties.xhp\"\>dialog\</link\> to change the curves' properties.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Mreže				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>axes; inserting grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids; inserting in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	hr	Mreže				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	hr	\<variable id=\"gitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertGrids\"\>You can divide the axes into sections by assigning gridlines to them. This allows you to get a better overview of the chart, especially if you are working with large charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> The Y axis major grid is activated by default.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156286				0	hr	Glavna mreža				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511				0	hr	Defines the axis to be set as the major grid.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	hr	X os				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_X_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the X axis of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	hr	\<variable id=\"sytextxgitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleGridHorizontal\"\>The \<emph\>Horizontal Grid On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar toggles the visibility of the grid display for the X axis. Note: This only works if the \<emph\>Minor grid\</emph\> check boxes in \<emph\>Insert - Grids\</emph\> are cleared.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Otherwise, the minor grid remains visible when the major grid is turned off.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	hr	Y os				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Y_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the Y axis of the chart.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150344				0	hr	\<variable id=\"sytextygitter\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleGridVertical\"\>The \<emph\>Vertical Grid On/Off\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar toggles the visibility of the grid display for the Y axis. Note: This only works if the X-axis \<emph\>Minor grid\</emph\> is not selected in \<emph\>Insert - Grids\</emph\>.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Otherwise, the minor grid remains visible when the major grid is turned off.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166430				0	hr	Z os				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Z_MAIN\"\>Adds gridlines to the Z axis of the chart.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you're working with 3D charts.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146978				0	hr	Minor grids				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156449				0	hr	Use this area to assign a minor grid for each axis. Assigning minor grids to the axis reduces the distance between the major grids.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153308				0	hr	X os				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148704				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_X_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the X axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153917				0	hr	Y os				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154536				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Y_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the Y axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148607				0	hr	Z os				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04070000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153247				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_GRID:CB_Z_HELP\"\>Adds gridlines that subdivide the Z axis into smaller sections.\</ahelp\> This option is only available if you're working with 3D charts.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Chart Type Pie 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	bm_id7621997				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>donut charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pie charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;pie/donut\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	hd_id3365276				0	hr	\<variable id=\"type_pie\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_pie.xhp\"\>Chart Type Pie\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id245979				0	hr	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	hd_id5799432				0	hr	Pita				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	hr	A pie chart shows values as circular sectors of the total circle. The length of the arc, or the area of each sector, is proportional to its value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	hr	Pie - this subtype shows sectors as colored areas of the total pie, for one data column only. In the created chart, you can click and drag any sector to separate that sector from the remaining pie or to join it back.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	hr	Exploded pie - this subtype shows the sectors already separated from each other. In the created chart, you can click and drag any sector to move it along a radial from the pie's center.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	hr	Donut - this subtype can show multiple data columns. Each data column is shown as one donut shape with a hole inside, where the next data column can be shown. In the created chart, you can click and drag an outer sector to move it along a radial from the donut's center.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_pie.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	hr	Exploded donut - this subtype shows the outer sectors already separated from the remaining donut. In the created chart, you can click and drag an outer sector to move it along a radial from the pie's center.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Poravnanje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05020201.xhp\" name=\"Alignment\"\>Alignment\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hr	Modifies the alignment of axes or title labels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	hr	Some of the options listed here are not available for all labels. For example, there are different options for 2D and 3D object labels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145750				0	hr	Show labels				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_AXIS_LABEL:CB_AXIS_LABEL_SCHOW_DESCR\"\>Specifies whether to show or hide the axis labels.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436	75			0	hr	\<variable id=\"sytextbeschr\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAxisDescr\"\>The\<emph\> AxesTitle On/Off \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> bar switches the labeling of all axes on or off.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717				0	hr	Rotiraj tekst				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ToggleAxisDescr\"\>Defines the text direction of cell contents.\</ahelp\> Click one of the ABCD buttons to assign the required direction.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150327				0	hr	ABCD wheel				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_CTR_DIAL\"\>Clicking anywhere on the wheel defines the variable text orientation.\</ahelp\> The letters "ABCD" on the button correspond to the new setting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154254				0	hr	ABCD button				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_STACKED\"\>Assigns vertical text orientation for cell contents.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	hr	If you define a vertical x-axis label, the text may be cut off by the line of the x-axis.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166432				0	hr	Stupnjeva				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SCH_ALIGNMENT_DEGREES\"\>Allows you to manually enter the orientation angle.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152985				0	hr	Tijek teksta				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155089				0	hr	Determines the text flow of the data label.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148837				0	hr	Preklapanje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_AXIS_LABEL:CB_AXIS_LABEL_TEXTOVERLAP\"\>Specifies that the text in cells may overlap other cells.\</ahelp\> This can be especially useful if there is a lack of space. This option is not available with different title directions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157982				0	hr	Prekid				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_AXIS_LABEL:CB_AXIS_LABEL_TEXTBREAK\"\>Allows a text break.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159205				0	hr	The following options are not available for all chart types:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152872				0	hr	Redoslijed				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159230				0	hr	The options on this tab are only available for a 2D chart, under \<emph\>Format - Axis - Y Axis\</emph\> or \<emph\>X Axis\</emph\>. In this area, you can define the alignment of the number labels on the X or Y axis.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146963				0	hr	Pločica				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3155758				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_SIDEBYSIDE\"\>Arranges numbers on the axis side by side.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151195				0	hr	Stagger odd				20181231 09:50:43
