helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147301				0	hr	Automatski				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3147404				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_AXIS_LABEL:RB_AXIS_LABEL_AUTOORDER\"\>Automatically arranges numbers on the axis.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149353				0	hr	Problems may arise in displaying labels if the size of your chart is too small. You can avoid this by either enlarging the view or decreasing the font size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	hd_id1106200812235146				0	hr	Text Direction				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05020201.xhp	0	help	par_id1106200812235271				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specify the text direction for a paragraph that uses complex text layout (CTL). This feature is only available if complex text layout support is enabled.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Chart Type Column and Line 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id5976744				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>column and line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combination charts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8596453				0	hr	\<variable id=\"type_column_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Line\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id4818567				0	hr	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id2451551				0	hr	Stupac i linija				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3101901				0	hr	A Column and Line chart is a combination of a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Column chart\</link\> with a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Line chart\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7910397				0	hr	Select one of the variants				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5244300				0	hr	Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn side by side so that you can easily compare their values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7163609				0	hr	Stacked Columns and Lines. The rectangles of the column data series are drawn stacked above each other, so that the height of a column visualizes the sum of the data values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1842097				0	hr	You can insert a second y-axis with \<link href=\"text/schart/01/04040000.xhp\"\>Insert - Axes\</link\> after you finish the wizard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8297677				0	hr	To specify a data range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8871120				0	hr	The leftmost columns (or the top rows) of the selected data range provide the data that are shown as Columns objects. The other columns or rows of the data range provide the data for the Lines objects. You can change this assignment in the \<emph\>Data Series\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2952055				0	hr	Select the data range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id594500				0	hr	Click one of the options for data series in rows or in columns.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1944944				0	hr	Check whether the data range has labels in the first row or in the first column or both.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id6667683				0	hr	Organizing data series				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7616809				0	hr	In the Data Series list box you see a list of all data series in the current chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9770195				0	hr	The column data series are positioned at the top of the list, the line data series at the bottom of the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1446272				0	hr	To organize the data series, select an entry in the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3779717				0	hr	Click Add to add another data series below the selected entry. The new data series has the same type as the selected entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5056611				0	hr	Click Remove to remove the selected entry from the Data Series list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7786492				0	hr	Use the Up and Down arrow buttons to move the selected entry in the list up or down. This way you can convert a Column data series to a List data series and back. This does not change the order in the data source table, but changes only the arrangement in the chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id265816				0	hr	Editing data series				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6768700				0	hr	Click an entry in the list to view and edit the properties for that entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id1924497				0	hr	In the Data Ranges list box you see the role names and cell ranges of the data series components. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5081942				0	hr	Click an entry, then edit the contents in the text box below. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2958464				0	hr	The label next to the text box states the currently selected role. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id883816				0	hr	Enter the range or click \<emph\>Select data range\</emph\> to minimize the dialog and select the range with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5091708				0	hr	The range for a data role, like Y-Values, must not include a label cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id974456				0	hr	Editing categories or data labels				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2767113				0	hr	Enter or select a cell range that will be used as text for categories or data labels. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id301828				0	hr	The values in the Categories range will be shown as labels on the x axis.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id8996246				0	hr	Inserting chart elements				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id5729544				0	hr	Use the Chart Elements page of the Chart Wizard to insert any of the following elements:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2932828				0	hr	Chart titles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	hr	Legenda				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	hr	Visible grid lines				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	hr	For additional elements use the Insert menu of the chart in edit mode. There you can define the following elements:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	hr	Sekundarne osi				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	hr	Sekundarne mreže				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	hr	Naslovi podataka				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	hr	Statistics, for example mean value, error indicator and regression curve				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7889950				0	hr	To set different data labels and statistics elements for each data series, use the properties dialog of the data series.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Odrednice				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149400				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>aligning; 2D charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; aligning\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149400				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"Options\"\>Options\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155067				0	hr	Use this dialog to define alignment and spacing for 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	hr	Align data series to:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145228				0	hr	In this area you can choose between two Y axis scaling modes. The axes can only be scaled and given properties separately.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147346				0	hr	Glavna y os				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_1\"\>This option is active as default. All data series are aligned to the primary Y axis.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143221				0	hr	Secondary Y axis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_OPTIONS:RBT_OPT_AXIS_2\"\>Changes the scaling of the Y axis. This axis is only visible when at least one data series is assigned to it and the axis view is active.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166423				0	hr	Postavke				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150365				0	hr	Define the settings for a bar chart in this area. Any changes apply to all data series of the chart, not to the selected data only.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145584				0	hr	Prored				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_GAP\"\>Defines the spacing between the columns in percent.\</ahelp\> The maximal spacing is 600%.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384				0	hr	Preklapanje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156447				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_OPTIONS:MT_OVERLAP\"\>Defines the necessary settings for overlapping data series.\</ahelp\> You can choose between -100 and +100%.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	hr	Spajanje linija				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_OPTIONS:CB_CONNECTOR\"\>For "stacked" and "percent" column (vertical bar) charts, mark this check box to connect the column layers that belong together with lines.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id9842219				0	hr	Show bars side by side				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id9800103				0	hr	If two axes are shown in a bar chart, and some data series are attached to the first axis, while some other data series are attached to the second axis, then both sets of data series are shown independently, overlapping each other.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2144535				0	hr	As a result, bars attached to the first y-axis are partly or completely hidden by bars attached to the second y-axis. To avoid this, enable the option to display bars side by side. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The bars from different data series are shown as if they were attached only to one axis.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id24414				0	hr	Clockwise direction				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2527237				0	hr	Available for pie and donut charts. \<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The default direction in which the pieces of a pie chart are ordered is counterclockwise. Enable the \<emph\>Clockwise direction\</emph\> checkbox to draw the pieces in opposite direction.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id401013				0	hr	Starting angle				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id761131				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Drag the small dot along the circle or click any position on the circle to set the starting angle of a pie or donut chart. The starting angle is the mathematical angle position where the first piece is drawn. The value of 90 degrees draws the first piece at the 12 o'clock position. A value of 0 degrees starts at the 3 o'clock position.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id553910				0	hr	In 3D pie and donut charts that were created with older versions of the software, the starting angle is 0 degrees instead of 90 degrees. For old and new 2D charts the default starting angle is 90 degrees.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id1414838				0	hr	When you change the starting angle or the direction, only current versions of the software show the changed values. Older versions of the software display the same document using the default values: Always counterclockwise direction and a starting value of 90 degrees (2D pie charts) or 0 degrees (3D pie charts).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3179723				0	hr	Degrees				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id2164067				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enter the starting angle between 0 and 359 degrees. You can also click the arrows to change the displayed value.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524613				0	hr	Plot missing values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524650				0	hr	Sometimes values are missing in a data series that is shown in a chart. You can select from different options how to plot the missing values. The options are available for some chart types only.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524823				0	hr	Leave gap				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524811				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, no data will be shown. This is the default for chart types Column, Bar, Line, Net.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524811				0	hr	Assume zero				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091052489				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, the y-value will be shown as zero. This is the default for chart type Area.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524837				0	hr	Continue line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200910524938				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a missing value, the interpolation from the neighbor values will be shown. This is the default for chart type XY.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0305200910524937				0	hr	Include values from hidden cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04060000.xhp	0	help	par_id030520091052494				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Check to also show values of currently hidden cells within the source cell range.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Chart Type Area				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	bm_id4130680				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>area charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;area\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id310678				0	hr	\<variable id=\"type_area\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_area.xhp\"\>Chart Type Area\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id916776				0	hr	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	hd_id961943				0	hr	Područje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	hr	An area chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series are connected by a line. The area between each two lines is filled with a color. The area chart's focus is to emphasize the changes from one category to the next.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	hr	Normal - this subtype plots all values as absolute y values. It first plots the area of the last column in the data range, then the next to last, and so on, and finally the first column of data is drawn. Thus, if the values in the first column are higher than other values, the last drawn area will hide the other areas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id3640247				0	hr	Stacked - this subtypes plots values cumulative stacked on each other. It ensures that all values are visible, and no data set is hidden by others. However, the y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the last column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked areas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_area.xhp	0	help	par_id4585100				0	hr	Percent - this subtype plots values cumulative stacked on each other and scaled as percentage of the category total.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Područje grafikona				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149670				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>charts; formatting areas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; chart areas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149670				0	hr	Područje grafikona				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05080000.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	2			0	hr	\<variable id=\"diagrammflaeche\"\>\<ahelp visibility=\"visible\" hid=\".uno:DiagramArea\"\>Opens the\<emph\> Chart Area\</emph\> dialog, where you can modify the properties of the chart area. The chart area is the background behind all elements of the chart.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Chart Type Column and Bar				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	bm_id4919583				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>column charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bar charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;column and bar\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id649433				0	hr	\<variable id=\"type_column_bar\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_column_bar.xhp\"\>Chart Type Column and Bar\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3430585				0	hr	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826960				0	hr	Stupac				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2244026				0	hr	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with vertical bars. The height of each bar is proportional to its value. The x axis shows categories. The y axis shows the value for each category.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id1281167				0	hr	Normal - this subtype shows all data values belonging to a category next to each other. Main focus is on the individual absolute values, compared to every other value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id3249000				0	hr	Stacked - this subtype shows the data values of each category on top of each other. Main focus is the overall category value and the individual contribution of each value within its category.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6968901				0	hr	Percent - this subtype shows the relative percentage of each data value with regard to the total of its category. Main focus is the relative contribution of each value to the category's total.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	hr	You can enable a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D view\</link\> of the data values. The "realistic" scheme tries to give the best 3D look. The "simple" scheme tries to mimic the chart view of other Office products.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id7359233				0	hr	For 3D charts, you can select the shape of each data value from Box, Cylinder, Cone, and Pyramid.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	hd_id955839				0	hr	Traka				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id6596881				0	hr	This type shows a bar chart or bar graph with horizontal bars. The length of each bar is proportional to its value. The y axis shows categories. The x axis shows the value for each category.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_bar.xhp	0	help	par_id8750572				0	hr	The subtypes are the same as for the Column type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\choose_chart_type.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Choosing a Chart Type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\choose_chart_type.xhp	0	help	hd_id9072237				0	hr	\<variable id=\"choose_chart_type\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/choose_chart_type.xhp\"\>Choosing a Chart Type\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\choose_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7085787				0	hr	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20181231 09:50:43
