helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Statistike				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147428				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Statistics\"\>Statistics\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	hr	\<variable id=\"statistik\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:InsertStatistics\"\>Use the\<emph\> Statistics \</emph\>dialog to determine if you want to display statistical functions when working with 2D objects, such as mean, error category or regression.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3401287				0	hr	An error bar is an indicator line that spans over a range from y - NegativeErrorValue to y + PositiveErrorValue. In this term, y is the value of the data point. When "standard deviation" is selected, y is the mean value of the data series. NegativeErrorValue and PositiveErrorValue are the amounts calculated by the error bar function or given explicitly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	hr	The\<emph\> Insert - Statistics \</emph\>menu item is only available for 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	hr	Kategorije greške				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	hr	In\<emph\> Error category \</emph\>area, you can select the individual types of display for the error category in question.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152989				0	hr	Nema funkcije				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_STAT:RBT_NONE\"\>Specifies that you do not want any functions to be displayed.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145117				0	hr	Konstantna vrijednost				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_MINUS\"\>Displays a constant value change. Set the positive value in the + spin box and the negative value in the\<emph\> -\</emph\> spin box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159204				0	hr	Postotka				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150048				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_PERCENT\"\>Displays a percentage. The display refers to the corresponding data point. Set the percentage in the spin box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id8977629				0	hr	Functions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id7109286				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Select a function to calculate the error bars.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id5154576				0	hr	Standard Error: Displays the standard error.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_STAT:RBT_VARIANT\"\>Displays the variance between the number of data points and respective values.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_STAT:RBT_SIGMA\"\>Displays the standard deviation (square root of the variance).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149870				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:METRICFIELD:TP_STAT:MTR_FLD_BIGERROR\"\>Displays the highest error margin in % according to the highest value of the data group. Set the percentage in the spin button.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id350962				0	hr	Cell Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6679586				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Click Cell Range and then specify a cell range from which to take the positive and negative error bar values.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3872188				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click a button to shrink the dialog, then use the mouse to select the cell range in the spreadsheet. Click the button again to restore the dialog to full size.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id2633747				0	hr	From Data Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id6633503				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For a chart with its own data, the error bar values can be entered in the chart data table. The Data Table dialog shows additional columns titled Positive Y-Error-Bars and Negative Y-Error-Bars.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573839				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to add to the displayed value as the positive error value.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573862				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value to subtract from the displayed value as the negative error value.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573844				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the address range from where to get the positive error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573970				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the address range from where to get the negative error values. Use the Shrink button to select the range from a sheet.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id0428200810573977				0	hr	Same value for both				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id0428200810573991				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Enable to use the positive error values also as negative error values. You can only change the value of the "Positve (+)" box. That value gets copied to the "Negative (-)" box automatically.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
