helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Chart Type XY				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	bm_id84231				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>scatter charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XY charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;XY (scatter)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error indicators in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error bars in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>averages in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>statistics in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variances in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>standard deviation in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>regression curves in charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>trend lines in charts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id9346598				0	hr	\<variable id=\"type_xy\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_xy.xhp\"\>Chart Type XY (Scatter)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id2003845				0	hr	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id7757194				0	hr	XY (razbacano)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5977965				0	hr	An XY chart in its basic form is based on one data series consisting of a name, a list of x‑values, and a list of y‑values. Each value pair (x|y) is shown as a point in a coordinate system. The name of the data series is associated with the y‑values and shown in the legend.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4381847				0	hr	Choose an XY chart for the following example tasks:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1336710				0	hr	scale the x‑axis				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1221655				0	hr	generate a parameter curve like a spiral				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id3397320				0	hr	draw the graph of a function				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7657399				0	hr	explore the statistical association of quantitative variables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8925138				0	hr	Your XY chart may have more than one data series.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5461897				0	hr	XY Chart Variants				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id8919339				0	hr	You can choose an XY chart variant on the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\>, or by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Chart Type \</item\>for a chart in edit mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4634235				0	hr	The chart is created with default settings. After the chart is finished, you can edit its properties to change the appearance. Line styles and icons can be changed on the Line tab page of the data series properties dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5482039				0	hr	Double-click any data point to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Series\</item\> dialog. Here you can click the Statistics tab and enable the display of statistical values. Some available values are mean value, variance, standard deviation, percentage, error margins, and regression curves or trend lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id0805200810492449				0	hr	For 2D charts, you can choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</item\> to enable the display of error bars.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6221198				0	hr	You can enable the display of mean value lines and trend lines using commands on the Insert menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id1393475				0	hr	Points only				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6571550				0	hr	Each data point is shown by an icon. %PRODUCTNAME uses default icons with different forms and colors for each data series. The default colors are set in Tools - Options - Charts - Default Colors. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id5376140				0	hr	Samo linije				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id4408093				0	hr	This variant draws straight lines from one data point to the next. The data points are not shown by icons. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7261268				0	hr	The drawing order is the same as the order in the data series. Mark \<emph\>Sort by X Values\</emph\> to draw the lines in the order of the x values. This sorting applies only to the chart, not to the data in the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6949369				0	hr	Točke i linije				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9611499				0	hr	This variant shows points and lines at the same time.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id6765953				0	hr	3D linije				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7422711				0	hr	The lines are shown like tapes. The data points are not shown by icons. In the finished chart choose \<link href=\"text/schart/01/three_d_view.xhp\"\>3D View\</link\> to set properties like illumination and angle of view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	hd_id239265				0	hr	Glatke linije				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id7957396				0	hr	Mark Smooth Lines to draw curves instead of straight line segments. The x values must be sorted. Therefore you cannot smooth parameter curves like spirals.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id1202124				0	hr	Click Properties to set details for the curves.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id5989562				0	hr	\<emph\>Cubic Spline\</emph\> interpolates your data points with polynomials of degree 3. The transitions between the polynomial pieces are smooth, having the same slope and curvature. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id6128421				0	hr	The Resolution determines how many line segments are calculated to draw a piece of polynomial between two data points. You can see the intermediate points if you click any data point.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_xy.xhp	0	help	par_id9280373				0	hr	\<emph\>B-Spline\</emph\> uses the data points as control points to form a B-spline curve. Those curves are built piecewise from polynomials. The \<emph\>Data points order\</emph\> sets the degree k of these polynomials. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Chart Wizard - Chart Type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	bm_id4266792				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>charts;choosing chart types\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	hd_id1536606				0	hr	\<variable id=\"wiz_chart_type\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard - Chart Type\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id6006958				0	hr	On the first page of the Chart Wizard you can \<link href=\"text/schart/01/choose_chart_type.xhp\"\>choose a chart type\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	hd_id3919186				0	hr	To choose a chart type				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3453169				0	hr	Choose a basic \<link href=\"text/schart/01/choose_chart_type.xhp\"\>chart type\</link\>: click any of the entries labeled Column, Bar, Pie, and so on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8406933				0	hr	The contents on the right side will change to offer more options depending on the basic chart type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8230231				0	hr	Optionally, click any of the options. While you change the settings in the wizard, watch the preview in the document to see how the chart will look.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3267006				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F1\</item\> and point to a control to see an extended help text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7251503				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> on any wizard page to close the wizard and create the chart using the current settings.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3191625				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> to see the next wizard page, or click the entries on the left side of the wizard to go to that page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id7659535				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Back\</emph\> to see the previous wizard page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id8420056				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> to close the wizard without creating a chart.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id2284920				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to go to the named wizard page.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3184301				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a basic chart type.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id2129276				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a sub type of the basic chart type.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id9719229				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enables a 3D look for the data values.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id3860896				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select the type of 3D look.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id4041871				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select a shape from the list.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id9930722				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Displays stacked series for Line charts.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\wiz_chart_type.xhp	0	help	par_id5749687				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Stack series display values on top of each other.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
