helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154486				0	hr	Default printer settings				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	hr	To set the default printing options for $[officename] Impress, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153914				0	hr	Setting printer options for the current presentation				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3154651				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149870				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>, and then select the printer options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3150431				0	hr	These settings override the default printer options in \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - Print\</emph\> for the current print job only.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id4555192				0	hr	Choosing a print layout for handouts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id7197790				0	hr	Click the Handout tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id1104159				0	hr	On the Tasks pane, click the Layouts tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id9354533				0	hr	Select the number of slides to print per page of paper.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id6556596				0	hr	Defining print options for handouts				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6744285				0	hr	Click the Handout tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id996734				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Page Number\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Header and Footer\</emph\> dialog box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6752220				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> to enter the header and footer text for handouts.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id5703909				0	hr	You see four areas on this dialog with check boxes for Header, Date and time, Footer, and Page number. These four areas correspond to the four areas in the corners of the handout master view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id4984282				0	hr	Enter text for header, footer, and date. Check the \<emph\>Page number\</emph\> box, if you want to number the handout pages. Ensure the \<emph\>Header\</emph\> check box is enabled if you want your header text to be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id816064				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Apply to All\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id863063				0	hr	The fields in the handout master view on screen are not updated, but the text that you entered will be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id5036164				0	hr	Printing handouts or notes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id2901394				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Print\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id5674611				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id1308023				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Handouts\</emph\> or \<emph\>Notes\</emph\> and click OK on both dialogs.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id6821192				0	hr	If you want another layout of the slides on the printed paper pages, use the mouse to move the slides around on the Handout view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151389				0	hr	Printing a range of slides				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3146318				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>View - Slide Sorter\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	hr	Hold down Shift, and click the range of slides that you want to print.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Print range \</emph\>area, click \<emph\>Pages\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\printing.xhp	0	help	par_id3154561				0	hr	Enter the slide numbers you want to print, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153191				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>footers;slide masters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide masters; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers and footers; slide masters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;headers/footers in all slides\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153191	1			0	hr	\<variable id=\"footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/footer.xhp\" name=\"Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\"\>Adding a Header or a Footer to All Slides\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1356547				0	hr	Every slide is based on a slide master. The text, pictures, tables, fields or other objects that you place on the slide master are visible as a background on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id704672				0	hr	Masters exist for slides, notes, and handouts. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8403576				0	hr	To edit a slide master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the slide master.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5641651				0	hr	To edit a notes master, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Notes Master\</emph\>. Click the Close Master View icon on the Master View toolbar, or choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>, to leave the notes master.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1583300				0	hr	To edit a handout master, click the Handout tab above the slide. Click the Normal tab to leave the handout master.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id7251808				0	hr	Adding predefined header or footer objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5015411				0	hr	Every type of master has some predefined areas to hold the date, footer, and slide numbers. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8217413				0	hr	When you switch to the master view, you can move that areas to any position on the master. You can enter additional text and resize the areas. You can select the contents of the areas and apply text formats. For example, you can change the font size or color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id7549668				0	hr	A predefined Header Area is available only for notes and handouts. If you want a header on all slides, you can move the Footer Area on the slide master to the top.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1829889				0	hr	Objects that you insert on a slide master are visible on all slides that are based on that slide master.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id8843043				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>View - Header and Footer\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1876583				0	hr	You see a dialog with two tab pages: \<emph\>Slide\</emph\> and \<emph\>Notes and Handouts\</emph\> where you can enter contents to the predefined areas. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id4101077				0	hr	By default, the \<emph\>Date and Time\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the format is set to Fixed and the text input box is empty, so no date and time is visible on the slides.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id204779				0	hr	By default, the \<emph\>Footer\</emph\> checkbox is enabled, but the text input box is empty, so no footer is visible on the slides.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1453901				0	hr	By default, the \<emph\>Slide number\</emph\> checkbox is cleared, so no slide numbers are visible.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1445966				0	hr	Enter or select the contents that should be visible on all slides.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id1956236				0	hr	If you want to change the position and formatting of the master objects, choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id5259559				0	hr	You see the slide master with areas near the bottom. You can move the areas , and you can select the fields and apply some formatting. You can also enter some text here which will be shown next to the fields.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id2521439				0	hr	Click the Date Area and move the time and date field. Select the <date/time> field and apply some formatting to change the format for the date and time on all slides. The same applies to the Footer Area and the Slide Number Area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id4712057				0	hr	Adding text objects as header or footer objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	hr	You can add a text object to the master page for your slides to act as a header or a footer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>View - Master - Slide Master\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295	12			0	hr	On the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, select the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154654\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_texttoolbox.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154654\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	hr	Drag in the master page to draw a text object, and then type or paste your text.				20181231 09:50:43
