helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4231086				0	hr	You can apply different methods to insert spreadsheet cells into your Impress slides or Draw pages:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9209875				0	hr	Insert a native table - you enter the data into the cells and apply fancy formatting using the Table Design section on the Tasks pane.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3044526				0	hr	Insert a new table as an OLE object or insert an existing file as an OLE object - you can specify the link to a file to be a live link to the latest data saved in a spreadsheet file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id137333				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of columns for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of rows for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551581				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Define the vertical alignment of selected or all cell contents. Split or merge cells.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551553				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All selected cells are merged into one cell.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551535				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The selected cell is split into several cells. You see the Split Cells dialog box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551651				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are align at the top of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551697				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned vertically centered in the cells.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551632				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned at the bottom of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10626				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Selects the current table.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551734				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all rows.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080035				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the height of the selected or all rows to the same size. The height of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080063				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all rows will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all rows containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080408008				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new row will be inserted at the bottom of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new rows as the selection has will be inserted below the selection.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080050				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All rows of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163012				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all columns.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163092				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the width of the selected or all columns to the same size. The width of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163046				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all columns will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all columns containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163128				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new column will be inserted at the right border of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new columns as the selection has will be inserted right of the selection.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163127				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All columns of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163151				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Align the table within the page or slide.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id8594317				0	hr	Inserting a native table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	hr	Go to the Impress slide or Draw page where you want to insert the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id248115				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Table\</item\> or use the Table icon on the Standard toolbar to insert a table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2748496				0	hr	Double-click the table and enter or paste the data into the cells. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8270210				0	hr	Select some cell contents and right-click to open the context menu. Choose commands to change the cell's contents, like font size and line spacing.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6820276				0	hr	Right-click the table border to open the table's context menu. Use the table's context menu to enter a name and description for the table, or to distribute the rows or columns equally, among other commands.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551725				0	hr	Select some cells and right-click to open a context menu, where you can insert or delete rows and columns, among other commands. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080355171				0	hr	To select a rectangular area of cells, point to a cell in one corner of the rectangle, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the opposite corner of the rectangle, then release the mouse button. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551880				0	hr	To select one cell, point to that cell, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the next cell and back, then release the mouse button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	hr	Inserting a new $[officename] Calc spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	hr	You can add a blank $[officename] Calc spreadsheet to a slide as an OLE object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	hr	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	18			0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Spreadsheet\</emph\>. Click in the spreadsheet to enter your data. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2466505				0	hr	Click outside the spreadsheet to view the slide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870				0	hr	To resize the spreadsheet without resizing the cells, double-click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle. To resize the cells of the spreadsheet, click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215				0	hr	Inserting $[officename] Calc spreadsheets from a file				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154765				0	hr	When you insert an existing spreadsheet into your slide, changes that are made to the original spreadsheet file are not updated on your slide. You can, however, make changes to the spreadsheet in your slide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145112				0	hr	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153075				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Create from file\</emph\>, and click \<emph\>Search\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	20			0	hr	Locate the file you want to insert, and then click\<emph\> OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id1616565				0	hr	Enable the \<emph\>Link to file\</emph\> checkbox to insert the file as a live link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155256				0	hr	The entire spreadsheet is inserted into your slide. If you want to change the sheet that is displayed, double-click the spreadsheet, and then select a different sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Slide Layout\"\>Format - Slide Layout\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150335				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04150100.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Object - OLE Object\"\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154702				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] Impress\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	hr	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress\"\>Using Shortcut Keys in $[officename] Impress\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148610				0	hr	You can use the keyboard to access $[officename] Impress commands as well as to navigate through the workspace. $[officename] Impress uses the same shortcut keys as $[officename] Draw to create \<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"drawing objects\"\>drawing objects\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149602				0	hr	Selecting placeholders				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150212				0	hr	$[officename] Impress \<emph\>AutoLayouts\</emph\> use placeholders for slide titles, text, and objects. To select a placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>. To move to the next placeholder, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166467				0	hr	If you press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> after you reach the last placeholder in a slide, a new slide is inserted after the current slide. The new slide uses the same layout as the current slide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157871				0	hr	During a Slide Show				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650				0	hr	To start a slide show, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+F2\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149354				0	hr	Advance to the next slide or to the next animation effect				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	hr	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153035				0	hr	Advance to the next slide without playing object animation effects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155263				0	hr	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+PageDown\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154558				0	hr	Return to previous slide				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145590				0	hr	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+PageUp\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153003				0	hr	Go to a specific slide				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	hr	Type the page number of the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150337				0	hr	Sortiranje slajdova				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153732	21			0	hr	When you first switch to Slide Sorter, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to change the keyboard focus to the workspace. Otherwise, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> to navigate to the workspace, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149882				0	hr	Selecting and deselecting slides				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155930				0	hr	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to select, and then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>. To add to the selection, use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide(s) that you want to add, and press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\> again. To deselect a slide, navigate to the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Spacebar\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145248				0	hr	Copying a slide:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	hr	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to copy, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+C\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148769				0	hr	Move to the slide where you want to paste the copied slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+V\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148388	25			0	hr	Select \<emph\>Before \</emph\>or \<emph\>After\</emph\> the current slide, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155367				0	hr	Moving a slide:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155987				0	hr	Use the arrow keys to navigate to the slide that you want to move, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+X\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171				0	hr	Navigate to the slide where you want to move the slide, and then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+V\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3083282	29			0	hr	Select \<emph\>Before \</emph\>or \<emph\>After\</emph\> the current slide, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Showing a Slide Show				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	bm_id5592516				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>running slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide shows; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations; starting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>starting; slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide shows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>slide transitions;automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic slide transition\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id4901272				0	hr	\<variable id=\"show\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/show.xhp\" name=\"Showing a Slide Show\"\>Showing a Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9636829				0	hr	Different ways exist to start a slide show. Once a slide show is running, you can take control pressing keys or clicking the mouse buttons.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	hr	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id9954527				0	hr	Running a Slide Show				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show\</emph\> to run the show.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4199957				0	hr	If you want all shows to start from the current slide instead of the first slide, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3209936				0	hr	Click to advance to the next effect or to the next slide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	hr	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id5694143				0	hr	Showing an automatic slide show (kiosk mode)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	hr	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id2361522				0	hr	On the Task Pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\> to open that tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Apply to All Slides\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	hr	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	hr	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	hr	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	hr	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	hr	Running a slide show from a file				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	hr	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	hr	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	hr	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_move.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Moving Objects to a Different Layer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_move.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150752				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>objects; moving in layers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layers; moving objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving; between layers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_move.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150752				0	hr	\<variable id=\"layer_move\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layer_move.xhp\" name=\"Moving Objects to a Different Layer\"\>Moving Objects to a Different Layer\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_move.xhp	0	help	par_idN10622				0	hr	Drawings in %PRODUCTNAME Draw support layers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_move.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	hr	Click and hold the object until its edges flash.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_move.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	hr	Drag the object to the name tab of the layer you want to move it to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layer_move.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	hr	Release the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	About Layers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>layers; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	hr	\<variable id=\"layers\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/layers.xhp\" name=\"About Layers\"\>About Layers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	3			0	hr	Layers are available in $[officename] Draw, not in $[officename] Impress. Layers allow you to assemble elements on a page that are related. Think of layers as individual workspaces that you can hide from view, hide from printing, or lock. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id7036957				0	hr	Layers do not determine the stacking order of objects on your page, except for the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer which is always in front of other layers. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id1614734				0	hr	The stacking order of objects on your page is determined by the sequence in which you add the objects. You can rearrange the stacking order by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id398876				0	hr	The areas on a layer that do not contain objects are transparent.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146962				0	hr	$[officename] Draw provides three default layers:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153073				0	hr	Izgled				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053				0	hr	Kontrole				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	hr	Dimenzijske linije				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156397				0	hr	You cannot delete or rename the default layers. You can add your own layers by \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Layer\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	hr	The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer is the default workspace. The \<emph\>Layout\</emph\> layer determines the location of title, text, and object placeholders on your page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	hr	The \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer can be used for buttons that have been assigned an action, but that should not be printed. Set the layer's properties to not printable. Objects on the \<emph\>Controls\</emph\> layer are always in front of objects on other layers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	hr	The \<emph\>Dimension Lines\</emph\> layer is where you draw, for example, the dimension lines. By switching the layer to show or hide, you can easily switch these lines on and off.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\layers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154507				0	hr	You can lock a layer to protect its contents, or hide a layer and its contents from view or from printing. When you add a new layer to a page, the layer is added to all of the pages in your document. However, when you add an object to a layer, it is only added to the current page. If you want the object to appear on all of the pages, add the object to the master page (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Master\</item\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150207				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>3D rotation objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>3D objects; generating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; to curves, polygons, 3D\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extrusion objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150207				0	hr	\<variable id=\"3d_create\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/3d_create.xhp\" name=\"Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\"\>Converting 2D Objects to Curves, Polygons, and 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	hr	You can convert two dimensional (2D) objects to create different shapes. $[officename] can convert 2D objects to the following object types:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	hr	Curved object based on Bézier curves				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762				0	hr	Polygon object consisting of straight line segments				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	hr	3D object with shading and a light source				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	hr	3D rotation object with shading and a light source				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id31490481				0	hr	Two types of 3D objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31472951				0	hr	The Status bar displays "3D scene selected". The 3D scenes are built from objects which have dimensions in x, y, and z coordinates. Examples are the objects inserted by the 3D Objects toolbar, and rectangles, ellipses, or text that got created by the Rectangle, Ellipse, or Text icons left on the Drawing toolbar, or any Custom Shapes, and that got converted to 3D by using the context menu "Convert - To 3D". These 3D scenes can be entered (for example, by pressing F3), and the objects can be rotated in 3D. Microsoft Office doesn't know these real 3D objects. When exporting these 3D scenes to Microsoft Office formats, a snapshot of the current view will be exported as a bitmap. 3D bars in charts are of this type, too.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id31506541				0	hr	The Status bar displays "Shape selected". The Custom Shapes can be viewed in a 2D mode or in a 3D mode. At any time, you can switch the view between the two modes. You use the Basic Shapes, Symbol Shapes, and the following icons on the Drawing toolbar to create Custom Shapes. The Custom Shapes can be changed using the 3D Settings toolbar. They do not form a 3D scene, they cannot be illuminated by more than one light source, they show no reflections, and there are some more limitations. You can convert them to a 3D scene, but then they are no longer Custom Shapes. Custom Shapes in 2D or 3D mode can be exported to and imported from Microsoft Office formats.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149048				0	hr	To convert an object to a curved shape:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147295				0	hr	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3150654				0	hr	Desnom tipkom miša kliknite na objekt i odaberite \<emph\>Konverzija - U krivulju\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145828				0	hr	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1027558\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1027558\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object. You can also drag the control points of a handle to modify the shape of the curve.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153738				0	hr	To convert a 2D object to a polygon:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241				0	hr	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148774				0	hr	Desnom tipkom miša kliknite na objekt i odaberite  \<emph\>Konverzija - U Poligon.\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3155368				0	hr	To modify the shape of the object, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7219458\" src=\"svx/res/cd015.png\" width=\"0.2201inch\" height=\"0.2201inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7219458\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar, and drag the handles of the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153919				0	hr	To convert a 2D object to a 3D object:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3147172				0	hr	Select a 2D object on the slide or page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN1088B				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Extrusion On/Off\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id2490920\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_extrusiontoggle.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2490920\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar, or right-click the object and choose \<emph\>Convert - To 3D\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3148828				0	hr	To edit the properties of the 3D object, use the \<emph\>Line and Filling\</emph\> toolbar and the \<emph\>3D Settings\</emph\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	hr	To convert a text object to 3D, use the \<emph\>Fontwork\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3821222\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fontworkgalleryfloater.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3821222\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145410				0	hr	To convert a 2D object to a 3D rotation object:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\3d_create.xhp	0	help	par_id3154260				0	hr	A 3D rotation object is created by rotating the selected object around its vertical axis.				20181231 09:50:43
