helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Zooming With the Keypad				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149018				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>zooming;keyboard\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; zooming\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	hr	\<variable id=\"change_scale\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/change_scale.xhp\" name=\"Zooming With the Keypad\"\>Zooming With the Keypad\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3148487				0	hr	You can use the keypad to quickly enlarge or reduce the view on your slide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3149501				0	hr	To zoom in, press the Plus Sign.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	hr	To zoom out, press the Minus Sign.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id7954954				0	hr	If you are using a mouse with a scroll wheel, you can hold down Ctrl and turn the wheel to change the zoom factor in all main modules of %PRODUCTNAME.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\change_scale.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut keys for presentations\"\>Shortcut keys for presentations\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Using Gluepoints				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	bm_id0919200803534995				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>glue points;using\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	hr	\<variable id=\"gluepoints\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/gluepoints.xhp\"\>Using Gluepoints\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803040964				0	hr	In Impress and Draw, you can connect each two shapes with a line called a \<link href=\"text/simpress/02/10100000.xhp\"\>connector\</link\>. When you draw a connector between shapes, the connector will be attached to a gluepoint on each shape. Each shape has some default gluepoints, and the positions of the default gluepoints depend on the specific shape. You can add your own custom gluepoints to a shape and then attach connectors to the custom gluepoints.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041099				0	hr	To add and edit gluepoints				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id091920080304108				0	hr	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041082				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Drawing toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041186				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Glue Points\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041160				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon on the Gluepoints toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041115				0	hr	Click inside the shape where you want to add the new gluepoint.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041133				0	hr	If the shape is filled, you can click anywhere inside the shape. If the shape is unfilled, you can click the border to insert a glue point. Once inserted, you can drag the glue point to another position inside the shape.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041250				0	hr	With the four icons next to the \<emph\>Insert Glue Point\</emph\> icon, you choose the directions which will be permitted for a connector at this gluepoint. You can choose one or more directions for a particular gluepoint.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041298				0	hr	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is active, the gluepoint moves when you resize the object to keep its position relative to the object borders.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\gluepoints.xhp	0	help	par_id0919200803041223				0	hr	If the \<emph\>Glue Point Relative\</emph\> icon is not active, the icons next to it are no longer grayed out. With these icons you can decide where a gluepoint will be placed when the size of the object is changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Selecting Underlying Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154492				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>objects; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting; hidden objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>covered objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>underlying objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154492				0	hr	\<variable id=\"select_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/select_object.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Underlying Objects\"\>Selecting Underlying Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159238				0	hr	To select an object that is covered by other objects, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click through the objects until you reach the underlying object. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift when you click.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\select_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	hr	To select an object that is covered by another object using the keyboard, press Tab to cycle through the objects on the slide. To cycle through the objects in reverse order, press Shift+Tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Pomicanje Objekata 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146121				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>objects;moving in slides\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;objects in slides\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146121				0	hr	\<variable id=\"move_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/move_object.xhp\" name=\"Moving Objects\"\>Moving Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	hr	You can move selected objects in your slide by dragging them, using the arrow keys, or by copying the objects and pasting them in another location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\move_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	hr	The arrow keys let you move objects more precisely than with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
