helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Consolidating Data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>values; consolidating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>consolidating data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>combining;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; merging ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;data ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	hr	\<variable id=\"consolidate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/consolidate.xhp\" name=\"Consolidating Data\"\>Consolidating Data\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153191				0	hr	During consolidation, the contents of the cells from several sheets will be combined in one place.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	hd_id892056				0	hr	To Combine Cell Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	hr	Open the document that contains the cell ranges to be consolidated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154513				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Consolidate\</item\> to open the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	hr	From the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\> box select a source cell range to consolidate with other areas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	hr	If the range is not named, click in the field next to the \<emph\>Source data area\</emph\>. A blinking text cursor appears. Type a reference for the first source data range or select the range with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> to insert the selected range in the \<emph\>Consolidation areas\</emph\> field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153816				0	hr	Select additional ranges and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\> after each selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157983				0	hr	Specify where you want to display the result by selecting a target range from the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150215				0	hr	If the target range is not named, click in the field next to \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> and enter the reference of the target range. Alternatively, you can select the range using the mouse or position the cursor in the top left cell of the target range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153813				0	hr	Select a function from the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> box. The function specifies how the values of the consolidation ranges are linked. The "Sum" function is the default setting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149315				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to consolidate the ranges.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	hr	Dodatne postavke				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147250				0	hr	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Consolidate\</emph\> dialog to display additional settings:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3156400				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Link to source data\</emph\> to insert the formulas that generate the results in the target range, rather than the actual results. If you link the data, any values modified in the source range are automatically updated in the target range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150538				0	hr	The corresponding cell references in the target range are inserted in consecutive rows, which are automatically ordered and then hidden from view. Only the final result, based on the selected function, is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3149945				0	hr	Under \<emph\>Consolidate by\</emph\>, select either \<emph\>Row labels\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column labels\</emph\> if the cells of the source data range are not to be consolidated corresponding to the identical position of the cell in the range, but instead according to a matching row label or column label.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	hr	To consolidate by row labels or column labels, the label must be contained in the selected source ranges.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3150478				0	hr	The text in the labels must be identical, so that rows or columns can be accurately matched. If the row or column label does not match any that exist in the target range, it will be appended as a new row or column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147468				0	hr	The data from the consolidation ranges and target range will be saved when you save the document. If you later open a document in which consolidation has been defined, this data will again be available.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153039				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Consolidate\"\>Data - Consolidate\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Kopiraj samo vidljive celije				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150440				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>cells; copying, deleting, formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;visible and invisible\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invisible cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filters;copying visible cells only\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	hr	\<variable id=\"cellcopy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellcopy.xhp\" name=\"Only Copy Visible Cells\"\>Only Copy Visible Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	hr	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	hr	$[officename] behavior depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	hr	Method and Action				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	hr	Rezultat				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	hr	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	hr	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	hr	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	hr	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	hr	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	hr	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Unosenje Formule u Preglednik formula				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar; input line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input line in formula bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; inputting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	hr	\<variable id=\"formula_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Formulas in the Formula Bar\"\>Entering Formulas in the Formula Bar\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6848353				0	hr	You can enter formulas in several ways: using the icons, or by typing on the keyboard, or by a mixture of both methods.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	hr	Click the cell in which you want to enter the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> icon on the Formula Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	hr	You will now see an equals sign in the input line and you can begin to input the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	hr	After entering the required values, press Enter or click \<emph\>Accept\</emph\> to insert the result in the active cell. If you want to clear your entry in the input line, press Escape or click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	hr	You can also enter the values and the formulas directly into the cells, even if you cannot see an input cursor. Formulas must always begin with an equals sign.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id4206976				0	hr	You can also press the + or - key on the numerical keyboard to start a formula. NumLock must be "on". For example, press the following keys in succession:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	hr	+ 5 0 - 8 Enter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8171330				0	hr	You see the result \<item type=\"literal\"\>42\</item\> in the cell. The cell contains the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=+50-8\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	hr	If you are editing a formula with references, the references and the associated cells will be highlighted with the same color. You can now resize the reference border using the mouse, and the reference in the formula displayed in the input line also changes. \<emph\>Show references in color \</emph\>can be deactivated under \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - View\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	7			0	hr	\<variable id=\"tip\"\>If you would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9. For example, in the formula =SUM(A1:B12)*SUM(C1:D12) select the section SUM(C1:D12) and press F9 to view the subtotal for this area. \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	hr	If an error occurs when creating the formula, an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error message\"\>error message\</link\> appears in the active cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Formula bar\"\>Formula bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Selecting Multiple Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>cells; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>marking cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple cells selection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selection modes in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; selecting ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153361				0	hr	\<variable id=\"mark_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/mark_cells.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Multiple Cells\"\>Selecting Multiple Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	hr	Select a rectangular range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149261				0	hr	With the mouse button pressed, drag from one corner to the diagonally opposed corner of the range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151119				0	hr	Mark a single cell				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hr	Učinite nešto od navedenog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	hr	Click, then Shift-click the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	hr	Pressing the mouse button, drag a range across two cells, do not release the mouse button, and then drag back to the first cell. You can now move the individual cell by drag and drop.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154942				0	hr	Select various dispersed cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072060				0	hr	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	hr	Mark at least one cell. Then while pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, click each of the additional cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id1001200901072023				0	hr	Click the STD / EXT / ADD area in the status bar until it shows ADD. Now click all cells that you want to select.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146971				0	hr	Switch marking mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	hr	On the status bar, click the box with the legend STD / EXT / ADD to switch the marking mode:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3159264				0	hr	Field contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	hr	Effect of clicking the mouse				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568				0	hr	STD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3148486				0	hr	A mouse click selects the cell you have clicked on. Unmarks all marked cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	hr	EXT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3150305				0	hr	A mouse click marks a rectangular range from the current cell to the cell you clicked.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	hr	ADD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	hr	A mouse click in a cell adds it to the already marked cells. A mouse click in a marked cell unmarks it. Alternatively, Ctrl-click the cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\mark_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3154487				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0208.xhp\" name=\"Status bar\"\>Status bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Defining Database Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154758				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>tables; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; defining database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;database ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154758				0	hr	\<variable id=\"database_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Database Ranges\"\>Defining a Database Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hr	You can define a range of cells in a spreadsheet to use as a database. Each row in this database range corresponds to a database record and each cell in a row corresponds to a database field. You can sort, group, search, and perform calculations on the range as you would in a database.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801	82			0	hr	You can only edit and access a database range in the spreadsheet that contains the range. You cannot access the database range in the %PRODUCTNAME Data Sources view. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10648				0	hr	To Define a Database Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	hr	Select the range of cells that you want to define as a database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10654				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Define Range\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153715				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066A				0	hr	Click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	hr	Specify the options for the database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_define.xhp	0	help	par_idN10675				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Applying Multiple Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154759				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; selecting multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>appending sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154759				0	hr	\<variable id=\"multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multitables.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Sheets\"\>Applying Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148576				0	hr	Inserting a Sheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Sheet\</item\> to insert a new sheet or an existing sheet from another file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203598				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a dialog box where you can assign macros to sheet events.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id05092009140203523				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens a window where you can assign a color to the sheet tab.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id050920091402035				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to select all sheets in the document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200914020391				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to deselect all sheets in the document, except the current sheet.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154491				0	hr	Selecting Multiple Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	hr	The sheet tab of the current sheet is always visible in white in front of the other sheet tabs. The other sheet tabs are gray when they are not selected. By clicking other sheet tabs while pressing \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> you can select multiple sheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	hr	You can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift\</item\>+\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\>+\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Page Down\</item\> to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	hr	Undoing a Selection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	hr	To undo the selection of a sheet, click its sheet tab again while pressing the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> key. The sheet that is currently visible cannot be removed from the selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156382				0	hr	Calculating Across Multiple Sheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	hr	You can refer to a range of sheets in a formula by specifying the first and last sheet of the range, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM(Sheet1.A1:Sheet3.A1) \</item\>sums up all A1 cells on Sheet1 through Sheet3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Stvaranje DataPilot Tabela 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491				0	hr	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating DataPilot Tables\"\>Creating DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	hr	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Data - DataPilot - Start\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialog appears. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\> dialog. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	hr	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	hr	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated datapilot table. The listbox can be used to filter the DataPilot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated DataPilot table to use another page field as a filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	hr	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	hr	By double-clicking on one of the fields in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area you can call up the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	hr	Use the \<emph\>Data Field\</emph\> dialog to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the Ctrl key while clicking the desired calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	hr	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	hr	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	hr	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	hr	Exit the DataPilot dialog by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The DataPilot table is inserted further down.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Oblikovanje brojeva s Decimalama				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; formatting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	hr	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	hr	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	hr	To format numbers with decimals:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	hr	Set the cursor at the number and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> to start the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialog you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256				0	hr	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Deaktiviranje automatskih promjena				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>deactivating; automatic changes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; deactivating automatic changes in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoInput function on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text in cells;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; AutoInput function of text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input support in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; input in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell input;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date formats;avoiding conversion to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	hr	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	hr	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	hr	The following shows you how to deactivate and reactivate the automatic changes in $[officename] Calc:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	hr	Automatic text or number completion				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	hr	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	hr	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	hr	Automatic conversion to date format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	hr	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	hr	To ensure that an entry is interpreted as text, add an apostrophe at the beginning of the entry. The apostrophe is not displayed in the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	hr	Quotation marks replaced by custom quotes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Custom Quotes\</emph\> tab and unmark \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	hr	Cell content always begins with uppercase				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab. Unmark \<emph\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	hr	Replace word with another word				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\>. Go to the \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - AutoCorrect\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Entering Fractions 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>fractions; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering fractions \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;fractions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	hr	\<variable id=\"fraction_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/fraction_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Fractions \"\>Entering Fractions \</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	hr	You can enter a fractional number in a cell and use it for calculation:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155133				0	hr	Enter "0 1/5" in a cell (without the quotation marks) and press the input key. In the input line above the spreadsheet you will see the value 0.2, which is used for the calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	hr	If you enter "0 1/2" AutoCorrect causes the three characters 1, / and 2 to be replaced by a single character. The same applies to 1/4 and 3/4. This replacement is defined in \<emph\>Tools - AutoCorrect\</emph\> - \<emph\>Replace\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\fraction_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145367	44			0	hr	If you want to see multi-digit fractions such as "1/10", you must change the cell format to the multi-digit fraction view. Open the context menu of the cell, and choose \<emph\>Format cells. \</emph\>Select "Fraction" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, and then select "-1234 10/81". You can then enter fractions such as 12/31 or 12/32 - the fractions are, however, automatically reduced, so that in the last example you would see 3/8.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Kopiranje formula				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151113				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151113				0	hr	\<variable id=\"formula_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Formulas\"\>Copying Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	hr	There are various ways to copy a formula. One suggested method is:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	hr	Select the cell containing the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+ C to copy it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	hr	Select the cell into which you want the formula to be copied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V. The formula will be positioned in the new cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	hr	If you want to copy a formula into multiple cells, there is a quick and easy way to copy into adjacent cell areas:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	hr	Select the cell containing the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	hr	Position the mouse on the bottom right of the highlighted border of the cell, and continue holding down the mouse button until the pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	hr	With the mouse button pressed, drag it down or to the right over all the cells into which you want to copy the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	hr	When you release the mouse button, the formula will be copied into the cells and automatically adjusted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	hr	If you do not want values and texts to be automatically adjusted, then hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key when dragging. Formulas, however, are always adjusted accordingly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Kopiranje na mnogostruke listove				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; transferring values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	hr	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	hr	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hr	Select all desired sheets by holding down the Shift or Ctrl key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	hr	You can use Shift+Ctrl+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	hr	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the sheets, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Updating DataPilot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>Pivot table import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; refreshing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	hr	\<variable id=\"datapilot_updatetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_updatetable.xhp\" name=\"Updating DataPilot Tables\"\>Updating DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	hr	If the data of the source sheet has been changed, $[officename] recalculates the DataPilot table. To recalculate the tables, choose \<emph\>Data - DataPilot - Refresh\</emph\>. Do the same after you have imported an Excel Pivot table into $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Applying AutoFilter				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>filters, see also AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; filter values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; filter sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drop-down menus in sheet columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	hr	\<variable id=\"autofilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autofilter.xhp\" name=\"Applying AutoFilter\"\>Applying AutoFilter\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	hr	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	hr	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	hr	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	hr	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different color for the arrow button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id9216589				0	hr	When you apply an additional AutoFilter on another column of a filtered data range, then the other combo boxes list only the filtered data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	hr	To display all records again, select the \<emph\>-all-\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose \<emph\>-Standard-\</emph\>, the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose \<emph\>-Top 10-\</emph\> to display the highest 10 values only. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	hr	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id4303415				0	hr	To assign different AutoFilters to different sheets, you must first define a database range on each sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	hr	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"Data - Filter - AutoFilter\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Zastita Celija od Promjena 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>protecting;cells and sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell protection; enabling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; protecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; hiding for printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet protection\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	hr	\<variable id=\"cell_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Cells from Changes\"\>Protecting Cells from Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	hr	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can protect sheets and the document as a whole. You can choose whether the cells are protected against accidental changes, whether the formulas can be viewed from within Calc, whether the cells are visible or whether the cells can be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261				0	hr	Protection can be provided by means of a password, but it does not have to be. If you have assigned a password, protection can only be removed once the correct password has been entered.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	hr	Note that the cell protection for cells with the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute is only effective when you protect the whole sheet. In the default condition, every cell has the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute. Therefore you must remove the attribute selectively for those cells where the user may make changes. You then protect the whole sheet and save the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	hr	These protection features are just switches to prevent accidental action. The features are not intended to provide any secure protection. For example, by exporting a sheet to another file format, a user may be able to surpass the protection features. There is only one secure protection: the password that you can apply when saving an OpenDocument file. A file that has been saved with a password can be opened only with the same password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	hr	Select the cells that you want to specify the cell protection options for.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> and click the \<emph\>Cell Protection\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	hr	Select the protection options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id31529866655				0	hr	Uncheck \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to allow the user to change the currently selected cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152898	10			0	hr	Select \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to prevent changes to the contents and the format of a cell. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069A				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Hide formula\</emph\> to hide and to protect formulas from changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A1				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Hide when printing\</emph\> to hide protected cells in the printed document. The cells are not hidden onscreen.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152872				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	hr	Apply the protection options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	hr	To protect the cells from being changed / viewed / printed according to your settings in the \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> dialog, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	hr	To protect the structure of the document, for example the count, \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\"\>names\</link\>, and order of the sheets, from being changed, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	hr	(Optional) Enter a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	hr	If you forget your password, you cannot deactivate the protection. If you only want to protect cells from accidental changes, set the sheet protection, but do not enter a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810	13			0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	hr	            \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>         				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Writing Multi-line Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; multi-line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multi-line text in cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	hr	\<variable id=\"text_wrap\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_wrap.xhp\" name=\"Writing Multi-line Text\"\>Writing Multi-line Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	hr	Pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys inserts a manual line break. This shortcut only works directly in the cell, not in the input line.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	hr	If you want the text to automatically break at the right border of the cell, proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	hr	Select all the cells where you want the text to break at the right border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	hr	In \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Automatic line break\</emph\> option and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell\"\>Format - Cell\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Spremanje i otvaranje listova u HTMl-u				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150542				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening; sheets in HTML\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150542				0	hr	\<variable id=\"html_doc\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/html_doc.xhp\" name=\"Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\"\>Saving and Opening Sheets in HTML\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154124				0	hr	Saving Sheets in HTML				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	hr	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc saves all the sheets of a Calc document together as an HTML document. At the beginning of the HTML document, a heading and a list of hyperlinks are automatically added which lead to the individual sheets within the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	hr	Numbers are shown as written. In addition, in the <SDVAL> HTML tag, the exact internal number value is written so that after opening the HTML document with \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> you know you have the exact values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	hr	To save the current Calc document as HTML, choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Save as type\</emph\> list box, in the area with the other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc filters, choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	hr	Enter a \<emph\>File name\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149379				0	hr	Opening Sheets in HTML				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149959				0	hr	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> offers various filters for opening HTML files, which you can select under \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Files of type\</emph\> list box:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	hr	Choose the file type "HTML Document (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc)" to open in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	hr	All \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc options are now available to you. However, not all options that \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc offers for editing can be saved in HTML format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01020000.xhp\" name=\"File - Open\"\>File - Open\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\html_doc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01070000.xhp\" name=\"File - Save As\"\>File - Save As\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Izmjena tablicnih pogleda				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147304				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>row headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column headers; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; views\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views; tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids;hiding lines in sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;headers/grid lines\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;table views\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147304				0	hr	\<variable id=\"table_view\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_view.xhp\" name=\"Changing Table Views\"\>Changing Table Views\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	hr	To permanently hide column and line headers in a table:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hr	Under the menu item \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc,\</emph\> go to the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page. Unmark\<emph\> Column/row headers\</emph\>. Confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3147436				0	hr	To hide grid lines:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_view.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	hr	Under the menu item \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>\<emph\>,\</emph\> go to the \<emph\>View\</emph\> tab page. Unmark \<emph\>Grid lines\</emph\>. Confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Definiranje pozadinske boje i grafike				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	hr	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\"\>Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id9520249				0	hr	You can define a background color or use a graphic as a background for cell ranges in $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144760				0	hr	Applying a Background Color to a $[officename] Calc Spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	hr	Select the cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> (or \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> from the context menu).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3152938				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	hr	Graphics in the Background of Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	hr	Select the graphic and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153575				0	hr	The graphic is inserted anchored to the current cell. You can move and scale the graphic as you want. In your context menu you can use the \<emph\>Arrange - To Background\</emph\> command to place this in the background. To select a graphic that has been placed in the background, use the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Navigator\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id51576				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/background.xhp\"\>Watermarks\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>\<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7601245				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Formatting Spreadsheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154125				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells and pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154125				0	hr	\<variable id=\"format_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\" name=\"Designing Spreadsheets\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153912	13			0	hr	Formatting Text in a Spreadsheet 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3144772				0	hr	Označite tekst kojeg želite oblikovati.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155268	15			0	hr	Choose the desired text attributes from the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. You can also choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog will appear in which you can choose various text attributes on the \<emph\>Font\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149899				0	hr	Formatting Numbers in a Spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3159226				0	hr	Select the cells containing the numbers you want to format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	18			0	hr	To format numbers in the default currency format or as percentages, use the icons on the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>Bar. For other formats, choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>. You can choose from the preset formats or define your own on the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153483				0	hr	Formatting Borders and Backgrounds for Cells and Pages				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154733				0	hr	You can assign a format to any group of cells by first selecting the cells (for multiple selection, hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\> key when clicking), and then activating the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog in \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cell\</item\>. In this dialog, you can select attributes such as shadows and backgrounds.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	hr	To apply formatting attributes to an entire sheet, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>. You can define headers and footers, for example, to appear on each printed page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	hr	An image that you have loaded with \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Background\</item\> is only visible in print or in the page preview. To display a background image on screen as well, insert the graphic image by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Picture - From File\</item\> and arrange the image behind the cells by choosing \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Arrange - To Background\</item\>. Use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\> to select the background image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2837916				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\"\>Number Formatting Options\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_table.xhp	0	help	par_id2614215				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\"\>Backgrounds for Cells\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	19xx/20xx godina				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>years; 2-digits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates; 19xx/20xx\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	hr	\<variable id=\"year2000\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/year2000.xhp\" name=\"19xx/20xx Years\"\>19xx/20xx Years\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	hr	The year in a date entry is often entered as two digits. Internally, the year is managed by $[officename] as four digits, so that in the calculation of the difference from 1/1/99 to 1/1/01, the result will correctly be two years.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	hr	Under \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you can define the century that is used when you enter a year with only two digits. The default is 1930 to 2029.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	hr	This means that if you enter a date of 1/1/30 or higher, it will be treated internally as 1/1/1930 or higher. All lower two-digit years apply to the 20xx century. So, for example, 1/1/20 is converted into 1/1/2020.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>HTML WebQuery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges; inserting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external data; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; inserting external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>web pages; importing data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>WebQuery filter\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>external data;WebQuery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting; external data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data sources; external data\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	hr	\<variable id=\"webquery\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/webquery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\"\>Inserting External Data in Table (WebQuery)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	hr	With the help of the \<emph\>Web Page Query ($[officename] Calc)\</emph\> import filter, you can insert tables from HTML documents in a Calc spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	hr	You can use the same method to insert ranges defined by name from a Calc or Microsoft Excel spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	hr	The following insert methods are available:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	hr	Inserting by Dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	hr	Set the cell cursor at the cell where the new content will be inserted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Link to External Data\</emph\>. This opens the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\"\>External Data\</link\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	hr	Enter the URL of the HTML document or the name of the spreadsheet. Press Enter when finished. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open a file selection dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	hr	In the large list box of the dialog, select the named ranges or tables you want to insert.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	hr	You can also specify that the ranges or tables are updated every n seconds.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	hr	The import filter can create names for cell ranges on the fly. As much formatting as possible is retained, while the filter intentionally does not load any images.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149021				0	hr	Inserting by Navigator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	hr	Open two documents: the $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in which the external data is to be inserted (target document) and the document from which the external data derives (source document).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	hr	In the target document open the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	hr	In the lower combo box of the Navigator select the source document. The Navigator now shows the range names and database ranges or the tables contained in the source document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842	20			0	hr	In the Navigator select the \<emph\>Insert as link\</emph\> drag mode \<image id=\"img_id3152985\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	hr	Drag the desired external data from the Navigator into the target document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	hr	If you have loaded an HTML document with the \<emph\>Web Page Query\</emph\> filter as the source document, you will find the tables in the Navigator, named continuously from "HTML_table1" onwards, and also two range names that have been created:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152873				0	hr	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_all\</item\> - designates the entire document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149897				0	hr	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_tables\</item\> - designates all HTML tables in the document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149126				0	hr	Editing the external data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3159228				0	hr	Open \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>. Here you can edit the link to the external data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154650				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External data dialog\"\>External data dialog\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Grouping DataPilot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	bm_id4195684				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function;grouping table entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping entries in DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	hr	\<variable id=\"datapilot_grouping\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp\"\>Grouping DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	hr	The resulting DataPilot table can contain many different entries. By grouping the entries, you can improve the visible result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	hr	Select a cell or range of cells in the DataPilot table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Data - Outline - Group\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	hr	Depending on the format of the selected cells, either a new group field is added to the DataPilot table, or you see one of the two \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090400.xhp\"\>Grouping\</link\> dialogs, either for numeric values, or for date values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_id3328653				0	hr	The DataPilot table must be organized in a way that grouping can be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	hr	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	hr	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	hr	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the spreadsheet, you can freeze them, which allows you to see the columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	hr	Select the row below, or the column to the right of the row or column that you want to be in the frozen region. All rows above, or all columns to the left of the selection are frozen.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	hr	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	hr	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	hr	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	hr	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Cells in Currency Format				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	hr	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	hr	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can give numbers any currency format. When you click the \<emph\>Currency\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150791\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_currencyfield.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150791\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>bar to format a number, the cell is given the default currency format set under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	hr	Exchanging of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	hr	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euros in another country and does not become dollars.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	hr	You can change the currency format in the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog (choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab) by two country settings. In the \<emph\>Language\</emph\> combo box select the basic setting for currency symbol, decimal and thousands separators. In the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list box you can select possible variations from the default format for the language.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	hr	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a german locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A point is used before the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list box , you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	hr	If, under \<emph\>Language\</emph\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Entering Matrix Formulas				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153969				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>matrices; entering matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;matrix formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153969				0	hr	\<variable id=\"matrixformula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/matrixformula.xhp\" name=\"Entering Matrix Formulas\"\>Entering Matrix Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	hr	The following is an example of how you can enter a matrix formula, without going into the details of matrix functions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	hr	Assume you have entered 10 numbers in Columns A and B (A1:A10 and B1:B10), and would like to calculate the sum of each row in Column C.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	hr	Using the mouse, select the range C1:C10, in which the results are to be displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	hr	Press F2, or click in the input line of the Formula bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	hr	Enter an equal sign (=).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	hr	Select the range A1:A10, which contains the first values for the sum formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	hr	Press the (+) key from the numerical keypad.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	hr	Select the numbers in the second column in cells B1:B10.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	hr	End the input with the matrix key combination: Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\matrixformula.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	hr	The matrix area is automatically protected against modifications, such as deleting rows or columns. It is, however, possible to edit any formatting, such as the cell background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Formatiranje brojeva kao teksta				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; for numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; entering without number formats \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell formats; text/numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	hr	\<variable id=\"text_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers as Text\"\>Formatting Numbers as Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	hr	You can format numbers as text in $[officename] Calc. Open the context menu of a cell or range of cells and choose \<emph\>Format Cells - Numbers\</emph\>, then select "Text" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list. Any numbers subsequently entered into the formatted range are interpreted as text. The display of these "numbers" is left-justified, just as with other text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	hr	If you have already entered normal numbers in cells and have afterwards changed the format of the cells to "Text", the numbers will remain normal numbers. They will not be converted. Only numbers entered afterwards, or numbers which are then edited, will become text numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	hr	If you decide to enter a number directly as text, enter an apostrophe (') first. For example, for years in column headings, you can enter '1999, '2000 and '2001. The apostrophe is not visible in the cell, it only indicates that the entry is to be recognized as a text. This is useful if, for example, you enter a telephone number or postal code that begins with a zero (0), because a zero (0) at the start of a sequence of digits is removed in normal number formats.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell - Numbers\"\>Format - Cell - Numbers\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Primjenjivanje traženja cilja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>goal seek example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	hr	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	hr	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966				0	hr	Goal Seek Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871				0	hr	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	hr	I = C * n* i				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	hr	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of $15,000.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	hr	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>$100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	hr	Place the cursor in the cell containing the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>, and choose \<emph\>Tools - Goal Seek\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Goal Seek\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	hr	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	hr	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	hr	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	hr	A dialog appears informing you that the Goal Seek was successful. Click \<emph\>Yes\</emph\> to enter the result in the cell with the variable value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Goal Seek\"\>Goal Seek\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Sorting Database Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150767				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; sorting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sorting; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;sorting in databases\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150767				0	hr	\<variable id=\"database_sort\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_sort.xhp\" name=\"Sorting Database Ranges\"\>Sorting Database Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id3145751				0	hr	Click in a database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121549				0	hr	If you select a range of cells, only these cells will get sorted. If you just click one cell without selecting, then the whole database range will get sorted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10635				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Sort\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id121020081121547				0	hr	The range of cells that will get sorted is shown in inverted colors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN10645				0	hr	Select the sort options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063D				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_sort.xhp	0	help	par_id1846980				0	hr	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in another document\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	hr	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	hr	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	hr	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	hr	To Reference a Cell in the Same Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	hr	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	hr	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	hr	=Sheet2.A1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	hr	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	hr	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	hr	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	hr	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	hr	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	hr	Confirm the formula by clicking the green check mark.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	hr	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	hr	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>addressing; relative and absolute\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; absolute/relative\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute addresses in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative addresses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>absolute references in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>relative references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; to cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; references\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	hr	\<variable id=\"relativ_absolut_ref\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\" name=\"Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\"\>Addresses and References, Absolute and Relative\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163712				0	hr	Relative Addressing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	hr	The cell in column A, row 1 is addressed as A1. You can address a range of adjacent cells by first entering the coordinates of the upper left cell of the area, then a colon followed by the coordinates of the lower right cell. For example, the square formed by the first four cells in the upper left corner is addressed as A1:B2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	hr	By addressing an area in this way, you are making a relative reference to A1:B2. Relative here means that the reference to this area will be adjusted automatically when you copy the formulas.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149377				0	hr	Absolute Addressing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3154943				0	hr	Absolute references are the opposite of relative addressing. A dollar sign is placed before each letter and number in an absolute reference, for example, $A$1:$B$2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	hr	$[officename] can convert the current reference, in which the cursor is positioned in the input line, from relative to absolute and vice versa by pressing Shift +F4. If you start with a relative address such as A1, the first time you press this key combination, both row and column are set to absolute references ($A$1). The second time, only the row (A$1), and the third time, only the column ($A1). If you press the key combination once more, both column and row references are switched back to relative (A1)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	hr	$[officename] Calc shows the references to a formula. If, for example you click the formula =SUM(A1:C5;D15:D24) in a cell, the two referenced areas in the sheet will be highlighted in color. For example, the formula component "A1:C5" may be in blue and the cell range in question bordered in the same shade of blue. The next formula component "D15:D24" can be marked in red in the same way.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154704				0	hr	When to Use Relative and Absolute References				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	hr	What distinguishes a relative reference? Assume you want to calculate in cell E1 the sum of the cells in range A1:B2. The formula to enter into E1 would be: =SUM(A1:B2). If you later decide to insert a new column in front of column A, the elements you want to add would then be in B1:C2 and the formula would be in F1, not in E1. After inserting the new column, you would therefore have to check and correct all formulas in the sheet, and possibly in other sheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	hr	Fortunately, $[officename] does this work for you. After having inserted a new column A, the formula =SUM(A1:B2) will be automatically updated to =SUM(B1:C2). Row numbers will also be automatically adjusted when a new row 1 is inserted. Absolute and relative references are always adjusted in $[officename] Calc whenever the referenced area is moved. But be careful if you are copying a formula since in that case only the relative references will be adjusted, not the absolute references.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	hr	Absolute references are used when a calculation refers to one specific cell in your sheet. If a formula that refers to exactly this cell is copied relatively to a cell below the original cell, the reference will also be moved down if you did not define the cell coordinates as absolute.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\relativ_absolut_ref.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	hr	Aside from when new rows and columns are inserted, references can also change when an existing formula referring to particular cells is copied to another area of the sheet. Assume you entered the formula =SUM(A1:A9) in row 10. If you want to calculate the sum for the adjacent column to the right, simply copy this formula to the cell to the right. The copy of the formula in column B will be automatically adjusted to =SUM(B1:B9).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	hr	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	hr	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	hr	The Find & Replace dialog				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	hr	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	hr	To find formulas or values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	hr	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	hr	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	hr	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	hr	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	hr	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	hr	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	hr	Finding text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	hr	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	hr	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	hr	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	hr	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (Ctrl+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	hr	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	hr	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	hr	The Navigator				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	hr	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	hr	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Izracunavanje u proracunskim tablicama				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	hr	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Spreadsheets\"\>Calculating in Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	hr	The following is an example of a calculation in $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	hr	Click in a cell, and type a number				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10656				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065D				0	hr	The cursor moves down to the next cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	hr	Enter another number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066F				0	hr	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	hr	The cursor moves to the right into the next cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	hr	Type in a formula, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A3 * A4 / 100.\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068B				0	hr	 Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	hr	The result of the formula appears in the cell. If you want, you can edit the formula in the input line of the Formula bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	hr	When you edit a formula, the new result is calculated automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Displaying Formulas or Values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153195				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; displaying in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; displaying in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; displaying formulas/values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>results display vs. formulas display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; formulas instead of results\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153195				0	hr	\<variable id=\"formula_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_value.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Formulas or Values\"\>Displaying Formulas or Values\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	hr	If you want to display the formulas in the cells, for example in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> box. Click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	hr	If you want to view the calculation results instead of the formula, do not mark the Formulasbox.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - View\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Defining Number of Pages for Printing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153194				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing sheet counts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page breaks; spreadsheet preview\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>viewing;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>previews;page breaks for printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153194				0	hr	\<variable id=\"print_exact\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_exact.xhp\" name=\"Defining Number of Pages for Printing\"\>Defining Number of Pages for Printing\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	hr	If a sheet is too large for a single printed page, $[officename] Calc will print the current sheet evenly divided over several pages. Since the automatic page break does not always take place in the optimal position, you can define the page distribution yourself.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	hr	Go to the sheet to be printed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	hr	You will see the automatic distribution of the sheet across the print pages. The automatically created print ranges are indicated by dark blue lines, and the user-defined ones by light blue lines. The page breaks (line breaks and column breaks) are marked as black lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3152578				0	hr	You can move the blue lines with the mouse. You will find further options in the Context menu, including adding an additional print range, removing the scaling and inserting additional manual line and column breaks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_exact.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Unos Broja sa Vodecim Nulama 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560				0	hr	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	hr	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	hr	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, '0987). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	hr	Format a cell with a number format such as \\0000. This format can be assigned in the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> field under the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\> tab, and defines the cell display as "always put a zero first and then the integer, having at least three places, and filled with zeros at the left if less than three digits".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	hr	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	hr	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter ^[0-9]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter &				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	hr	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	hr	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	hr	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Deleting DataPilot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; deleting tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	hr	\<variable id=\"datapilot_deletetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_deletetable.xhp\" name=\"Deleting DataPilot Tables\"\>Deleting DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_deletetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	hr	In order to delete a DataPilot table, select any cell in the DataPilot table, then choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> in the context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Unprotecting Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153252				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>cell protection; unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting; unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252	14			0	hr	\<variable id=\"cell_unprotect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_unprotect.xhp\" name=\"Unprotecting Cells\"\>Unprotecting Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	hr	Click the sheet for which you want to cancel the protection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, then choose \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> or \<emph\>Document\</emph\> to remove the check mark indicating the protected status.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	hr	If you have assigned a password, enter it in this dialog and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	hr	The cells can now be edited, the formulas can be viewed, and all cells can be printed until you reactivate the protection for the sheet or document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Filter: Primjena Naprednih Filtera 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148798				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>filters;defining advanced filters \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148798	18			0	hr	\<variable id=\"specialfilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/specialfilter.xhp\" name=\"Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\"\>Filter: Applying Advanced Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145785				0	hr	Copy the column headers of the sheet ranges to be filtered into an empty area of the sheet, and then enter the criteria for the filter in a row beneath the headers. Horizontally arranged data in a row will always be logically connected with AND, and vertically arranged data in a column will always be logically connected with OR.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	hr	Once you have created a filter matrix, select the sheet ranges to be filtered. Open the \<emph\>Advanced Filter\</emph\> dialog by choosing \<emph\>Data - Filter - Advanced Filter\</emph\>, and define the filter conditions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	21			0	hr	Then click OK, and you will see that only the rows from the original sheet whose contents have met the search criteria are still visible. All other rows are temporarily hidden and can be made to reappear with the \<emph\>Format - Row - Show \</emph\>command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\specialfilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664	22			0	hr	\<emph\>Example\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
