helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154017				0	hr	You can change the height of the rows with the mouse or through the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	hr	What is described here for rows and row height applies accordingly for columns and column width.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	hr	Using the mouse to change the row height or column width				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	hr	Click the area of the headers on the separator below the current row, keep the mouse button pressed and drag up or down in order to change the row height.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3159237				0	hr	Select the optimal row height by double-clicking the separator below the row.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154659				0	hr	Using the dialog to change the row height or column width				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150367				0	hr	Click the row so that you achieve the focus.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3166432				0	hr	Start the context menu on the header at the left-hand side.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\row_height.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	hr	You will see the commands \<emph\>Height\</emph\> and \<emph\>Optimal row height\</emph\>. Choosing either opens a dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
