helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	hr	\<variable id=\"rename_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\" name=\"Renaming Sheets\"\>Renaming Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	hr	Click the name of the sheet that you want to change.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976				0	hr	Open the context menu and choose the \<emph\>Rename\</emph\> command. A dialog box appears where you can enter a new name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	hr	Enter a new name for the sheet and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	hr	Alternatively, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click on any sheet name and enter the new name directly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502833				0	hr	Sheet names can contain almost any character. Some naming restrictions apply when you want to save the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050283				0	hr	When saving to Microsoft Excel format, the following characters are not allowed in sheet names:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050281				0	hr	colon :				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502897				0	hr	back slash \\				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050299				0	hr	forward slash /				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502913				0	hr	question mark ?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050298				0	hr	asterisk *				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502969				0	hr	left square bracket [				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502910				0	hr	right square bracket ]				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502971				0	hr	single quote ' as the first or last character of the name				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050307				0	hr	In cell references, a sheet name has to be enclosed in single quotes ' if the name contains other characters than alphanumeric or underscore. A single quote contained within a name has to be escaped by doubling it (two single quotes). For example, you want to reference the cell A1 on a sheet with the following name:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503071				0	hr	This year's sheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503054				0	hr	The reference must be enclosed in single quotes, and the one single quote inside the name must be doubled:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503069				0	hr	'This year''s sheet'.A1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155444				0	hr	The name of a sheet is independent of the name of the spreadsheet. You enter the spreadsheet name when you save it for the first time as a file. The document can contain up to 256 individual sheets, which can have different names.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Prepoznavanje Imena kao Adresiranje 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148797				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>automatic addressing in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural language addressing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; using row/column labels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; as addressing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>addressing; automatic\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>name recognition on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>row headers;using in formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>column headers;using in formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; finding labels automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; finding labels automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recognizing; column and row labels\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	hr	\<variable id=\"address_auto\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/address_auto.xhp\" name=\"Recognizing Names as Addressing\"\>Recognizing Names as Addressing\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	hr	You can use cells with text to refer to the rows or to the columns that contain the cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3154942\" src=\"res/helpimg/names_as_addressing.png\" width=\"4.2898inch\" height=\"1.6854inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154942\"\>Example spreadsheet\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3154512				0	hr	In the example spreadsheet, you can use the string \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Column One'\</item\> in a formula to refer to the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B3\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>B5\</item\>, or \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Column Two'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>C2\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>C5\</item\>. You can also use \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Row One'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B3\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>D3\</item\>, or \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Row Two'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B4\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>D4\</item\>. The result of a formula that uses a cell name, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>SUM('Column One')\</item\>, is 600.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	hr	This function is active by default. To turn this function off, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Automatically find column and row labels\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210				0	hr	If you want a name to be automatically recognized by Calc, the name must start with a letter and be composed of alphanumeric characters. If you enter the name in the formula yourself, enclose the name in single quotation marks ('). If a single quotation mark appears in a name, you must enter a backslash in front of the quotation mark, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Harry\\'s Bar'.\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Filtering DataPilot Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; filtering tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	hr	\<variable id=\"datapilot_filtertable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_filtertable.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Pivot Tables\"\>Filtering Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153192				0	hr	You can use filters to remove unwanted data from a pivot table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150441				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button in the sheet to call up the dialog for the filter conditions. Alternatively, call up the context menu of the pivot table and select the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> command. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090103.xhp\" name=\"Filter\"\>\<emph\>Filter\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears. Here you can filter the pivot table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id315044199				0	hr	You can also click the arrow on a button in the pivot table to show a pop-up window. In this pop-up window, you can edit the visibility settings of the associated field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344485				0	hr	The pop-up window displays a list of field members associated with that field. A check box is placed to the left of each field member name. When a field has an alternative display name that differs from its original name, that name is displayed in the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344449				0	hr	Enable or disable a checkbox to show or hide the associated field member in the pivot table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344493				0	hr	Enable or disable the \<emph\>All\</emph\> checkbox to show all or none of the field members.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344431				0	hr	Select a field member in the pop-up window and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Show only the current item\</item\> button to show only the selected field member. All other field members are hidden in the pivot table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344484				0	hr	Select a field member in the pop-up window and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide only the current item\</item\> button to hide only the selected field member. All other field members are shown in the pivot table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344578				0	hr	Commands enable you to sort the field members in ascending order, descending order, or using a custom sort list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344584				0	hr	To edit the custom sort lists, open \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344811				0	hr	The arrow to open the pop-up window is normally black. When the field contains one or more hidden field members, the arrow is blue and displays a tiny square at its lower-right corner.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_filtertable.xhp	0	help	par_id0720201001344884				0	hr	You can also open the pop-up window by positioning the cell cursor at the button and pressing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+D.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	User-defined Number Formats				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; user-defined formatting in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; user-defined numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats; millions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	hr	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-defined Number Formats\"\>User-defined Number Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	hr	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	hr	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	hr	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	hr	0.0,, "Million"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	hr	Click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	hr	The following table shows the effects of rounding, thousands delimiters (,), decimal delimiters (.) and the placeholders # and 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	hr	Broj				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	hr	.#,, "Million"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	hr	0.0,, "Million"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	hr	#,, "Million"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	hr	10200000				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147003				0	hr	10.2 Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	hr	10.2 Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155113				0	hr	10 Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	hr	500000				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3145585				0	hr	.5 Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	hr	0.5 Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114				0	hr	1 Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155810				0	hr	100000000				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	hr	100. Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241				0	hr	100.0 Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144771				0	hr	100 Million				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Tipka prečca (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Dostupnost)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145120				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Calc shortcuts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>shortcut keys;%PRODUCTNAME Calc accessibility\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145120				0	hr	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys (%PRODUCTNAME Calc Accessibility)\"\>Shortcut Keys (\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc Accessibility)\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	hr	Refer also to the lists of shortcut keys for \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc and \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> in general.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153360				0	hr	Cell Selection Mode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150870				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3150439\" src=\"sc/res/refinp1.png\" width=\"0.1327inch\" height=\"0.1327inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150439\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	hr	In a text box that has a button to minimize the dialog, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> to enter the cell selection mode. Select any number of cells, then press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F2\</item\> again to show the dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	hr	In the cell selection mode, you can use the common navigation keys to select cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148646				0	hr	Controlling the Outline				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	hr	You can use the keyboard in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"Outline\"\>Outline\</link\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F6\</item\> until the vertical or horizontal outline window has the focus.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	hr	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons from top to bottom or from left to right.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	hr	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> - cycle through all visible buttons in the opposite direction.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3149403				0	hr	\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+1\</item\> to \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+8\</item\> - show all levels up to the specified number; hide all higher levels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	hr	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>+\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>-\</item\> to show or hide the focused outline group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155446				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> to activate the focused button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	hr	Use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\>, \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\>, or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow to cycle through all buttons in the current level.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147343				0	hr	Selecting a Drawing Object or a Graphic				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AA				0	hr	Choose View - Toolbars - Drawing to open the Drawing toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> until the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> toolbar is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	hr	If the selection tool is active, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>. This selects the first drawing object or graphic in the sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3159240				0	hr	With \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+F6\</item\> you set the focus to the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	hr	Now you can use \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> to select the next drawing object or graphic and \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+Tab\</item\> to select the previous one.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	hr	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	hr	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	hr	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Link to External Data\</emph\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<emph\>External Data\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	hr	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialog. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	hr	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<emph\>External Data\</emph\> dialog, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	hr	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" minutes and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	hr	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	hr	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	hr	Under \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</emph\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialog under \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Oznacavanje negativnih brojeva				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers; highlighting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors;number formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number formats;colors\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	hr	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	hr	You can format cells with a number format that highlights negative numbers in red. Alternatively, you can define your own number format in which negative numbers are highlighted in other colors.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	hr	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	hr	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<emph\>Format code\</emph\>. For example, instead of "RED," enter "YELLOW". If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<emph\>Add\</emph\> icon, this is a valid entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Izbor tema za listove				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	hr	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	hr	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	hr	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	hr	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	hr	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	hr	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	hr	The \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog appears. This dialog lists the available themes for the whole spreadsheet and the Styles and Formatting window lists the custom styles for specific cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialog, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	hr	Click OK				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201				0	hr	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Converting Text to Numbers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>formats; text as numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>time format conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200901265171				0	hr	\<variable id=\"numbers_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/numbers_text.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text to Numbers\"\>Converting Text to Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265127				0	hr	Calc converts text inside cells to the respective numeric values if an unambiguous conversion is possible. If no conversion is possible, Calc returns a #VALUE! error.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265196				0	hr	Only integer numbers including exponent are converted, and ISO 8601 dates and times in their extended formats with separators. Anything else, like fractional numbers with decimal separators or dates other than ISO 8601, is not converted, as the text string would be locale dependent. Leading and trailing blanks are ignored.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265220				0	hr	The following ISO 8601 formats are converted:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265288				0	hr	CCYY-MM-DD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265267				0	hr	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265248				0	hr	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265374				0	hr	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss,s				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265327				0	hr	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.s				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265399				0	hr	hh:mm				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265347				0	hr	hh:mm:ss				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265349				0	hr	hh:mm:ss,s				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265342				0	hr	hh:mm:ss.s				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265491				0	hr	The century code CC may not be omitted. Instead of the T date and time separator, exactly one space character may be used.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265467				0	hr	If a date is given, it must be a valid Gregorian calendar date. In this case the optional time must be in the range 00:00 to 23:59:59.99999...				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265420				0	hr	If only a time string is given, it may have an hours value of more than 24, while minutes and seconds can have a maximum value of 59.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265448				0	hr	The conversion is done for single arguments only, as in =A1+A2, or ="1E2"+1. Cell range arguments are not affected, so SUM(A1:A2) differs from A1+A2 if at least one of the two cells contain a convertible string.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090126540				0	hr	Strings inside formulas are also converted, such as in ="1999-11-22"+42, which returns the date 42 days after November 22nd, 1999. Calculations involving localized dates as strings inside the formula return an error. For example, the localized date string "11/22/1999" or "22.11.1999" cannot be used for the automatic conversion.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id1005200903485368				0	hr	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485359				0	hr	In A1 enter the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>'1e2\</item\> (which is converted to the number 100 internally).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485341				0	hr	In A2 enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A1+1\</item\> (which correctly results in 101).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265544				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Racunanje Sa Datumima i Vremenima 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146120				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>dates; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>times; in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells;date and time formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>current date and time values\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146120				0	hr	\<variable id=\"calc_date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_date.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Dates and Times\"\>Calculating With Dates and Times\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	hr	In $[officename] Calc, you can perform calculations with current date and time values. As an example, to find out exactly how old you are in seconds or hours, follow the following steps:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750				0	hr	In a spreadsheet, enter your birthday in cell A1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3145642	14			0	hr	Enter the following formula in cell A3: =NOW()-A1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020				0	hr	After pressing the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key you will see the result in date format. Since the result should show the difference between two dates as a number of days, you must format cell A3 as a number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	hr	Place the cursor in cell A3, right-click to open a context menu and choose \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	hr	The \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog appears. On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, the \<emph\>Number\</emph\> category will appear already highlighted. The format is set to "General", which causes the result of a calculation containing date entries to be displayed as a date. To display the result as a number, set the number format to "-1,234" and close the dialog with the OK button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	hr	The number of days between today's date and the specified date is displayed in cell A3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	hr	Experiment with some additional formulas: in A4 enter =A3*24 to calculate the hours, in A5 enter =A4*60 for the minutes, and in A6 enter =A5*60 for seconds. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key after each formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149207				0	hr	The time since your date of birth will be calculated and displayed in the various units. The values are calculated as of the exact moment when you entered the last formula and pressed the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key. This value is not automatically updated, although "Now" continuously changes. In the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> menu, the menu item \<emph\>Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> is normally active; however, automatic calculation does not apply to the function NOW. This ensures that your computer is not solely occupied with updating the sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Calculating Time Differences				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;time differences\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time differences\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	hr	\<variable id=\"calc_timevalues\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_timevalues.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Time Differences\"\>Calculating Time Differences\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	hr	If you want to calculate time differences, for example, the time between 23:30 and 01:10 in the same night, use the following formula:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	hr	=(B2<A2)+B2-A2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598				0	hr	The later time is B2 and the earlier time is A2. The result of the example is 01:40 or 1 hour and 40 minutes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	hr	In the formula, an entire 24-hour day has a value of 1 and one hour has a value of 1/24. The logical value in parentheses is 0 or 1, corresponding to 0 or 24 hours. The result returned by the formula is automatically issued in time format due to the sequence of the operands.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Applying Sort Lists				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150870				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>filling;customized lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sort lists;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>geometric lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetic lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>series;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customized lists\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	3			0	hr	\<variable id=\"sorted_list\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/sorted_list.xhp\" name=\"Applying Sort Lists\"\>Applying Sort Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	hr	Sort lists allow you to type one piece of information in a cell, then drag it to fill in a consecutive list of items.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	hr	For example, enter the text "Jan" or "January" in an empty cell. Select the cell and click the mouse on the lower right corner of the cell border. Then drag the selected cell a few cells to the right or downwards. When you release the mouse button, the highlighted cells will be filled with the names of the months.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	hr	Hold down Ctrl if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	hr	The predefined series can be found under \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>. You can also create your own lists of text strings tailored to your needs, such as a list of your company's branch offices. When you use the information in these lists later (for example, as headings), just enter the first name in the list and expand the entry by dragging it with your mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	User Defined Borders in Cells 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	bm_id3457441				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>cells;borders\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>line arrangement;cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id4544816				0	hr	\<variable id=\"borders\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/borders.xhp\"\>User Defined Borders in Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2320017				0	hr	You can apply a variety of different lines to selected cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8055665				0	hr	Select the cell or a block of cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9181188				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9947508				0	hr	In the dialog, click the \<emph\>Borders\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7907956				0	hr	Choose the border options you want to apply and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1342204				0	hr	The options in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area can be used to apply multiple border styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id4454481				0	hr	Selection of cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id7251503				0	hr	Depending on the selection of cells, the area looks different.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8716696				0	hr	Odabir				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4677877				0	hr	Line arrangement area				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id807824				0	hr	One cell				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8473464				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id1737113\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_1.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.6146inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1737113\"\>borders with one cell selected\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3509933				0	hr	Cells in a column				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6635639				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id1680959\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_2.png\" width=\"1.2917inch\" height=\"1.6146inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1680959\"\>borders with a column selected\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8073366				0	hr	Cells in a row				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6054567				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id9623096\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_3.png\" width=\"1.2811inch\" height=\"1.6146inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9623096\"\>borders with a row selected\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id466322				0	hr	Cells in a block of 2x2 or more				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4511551				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id8139591\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_4.png\" width=\"1.2917inch\" height=\"1.6252inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8139591\"\>borders with a block selected\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5383465				0	hr	You cannot apply borders to multiple selections.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7790154				0	hr	Osnovne postavke				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2918485				0	hr	Click one of the \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icons to set or reset multiple borders.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	hr	The thin gray lines inside an icon show the borders that will be reset or cleared.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5212561				0	hr	The dark lines inside an icon show the lines that will be set using the selected line style and color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4818872				0	hr	The thick gray lines inside an icon show the lines that will not be changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id8989226				0	hr	Primjeri				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id622577				0	hr	Select a block of about 8x8 cells, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8119754				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id7261268\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_5.png\" width=\"1.1354inch\" height=\"0.25inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7261268\"\>default icon row of Borders tab page\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8964201				0	hr	Click the left icon to clear all lines. This removes all outer borders, all inner lines, and all diagonal lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6048463				0	hr	Click the second icon from the left to set an outer border and to remove all other lines.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1495406				0	hr	Click the rightmost icon to set an outer border. The inner lines are not changed, except the diagonal lines, which will be removed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id9269386				0	hr	Now you can continue to see which lines the other icons will set or remove.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id3593554				0	hr	User defined settings				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4018066				0	hr	In the \<emph\>User defined\</emph\> area, you can click to set or remove individual lines. The preview shows lines in three different states. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8004699				0	hr	Repeatedly click an edge or a corner to switch through the three different states.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8037659				0	hr	Line types				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2305978				0	hr	Slika				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8716086				0	hr	Značenje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id3978087				0	hr	A black line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4065065				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id9379863\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2811inch\" height=\"1.1354inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9379863\"\>solid line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6987823				0	hr	A black line sets the corresponding line of the selected cells. The line is shown as a dotted line when you choose the 0.05 pt line style. Double lines are shown when you select a double line style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1209143				0	hr	A gray line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6653340				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id6972563\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_gray.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.1563inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6972563\"\>gray line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2278817				0	hr	A gray line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will not be changed. No line will be set or removed at this position.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5374919				0	hr	A white line				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id52491				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3801080\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_white.png\" width=\"1.2811inch\" height=\"1.1354inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3801080\"\>white line for user defined border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id372325				0	hr	A white line is shown when the corresponding line of the selected cells will be removed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	hd_id7282937				0	hr	Primjeri				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id4230780				0	hr	Select a single cell, then choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Borders\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id1712393				0	hr	Click the lower edge to set a very thin line as a lower border. All other lines will be removed from the cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5149693				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id9467452\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_6.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.1563inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id9467452\"\>setting a thin lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5759453				0	hr	Choose a thicker line style and click the lower edge. This sets a thicker line as a lower border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id6342051				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id7431562\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_7.png\" width=\"1.2811inch\" height=\"1.1354inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7431562\"\>setting a thick line as a border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id5775322				0	hr	Click the second \<emph\>Default\</emph\> icon from the left to set all four borders. Then repeatedly click the lower edge until a white line is shown. This removes the lower border.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2882778				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id8155766.00000001\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_8.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.1354inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id8155766.00000001\"\>removing lower border\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id8102053				0	hr	You can combine several line types and styles. The last image shows how to set thick outer borders (the thick black lines), while any diagonal lines inside the cell will not be touched (gray lines).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\borders.xhp	0	help	par_id2102420				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id5380718\" src=\"res/helpimg/border_ca_9.png\" width=\"1.2709inch\" height=\"1.1563inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id5380718\"\>advanced example for cell borders\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
