helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Using Print Ranges on a Spreadsheet				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	bm_id14648				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ranges;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>PDF export of print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>clearing, see deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;printranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extending printranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;cells in print ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;print ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D7				0	hr	\<variable id=\"printranges\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/printranges.xhp\"\>Defining Print Ranges on a Sheet\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108F5				0	hr	You can define which range of cells on a spreadsheet to print.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FB				0	hr	The cells on the sheet that are not part of the defined print range are not printed or exported. Sheets without a defined print range are not printed and not exported to a PDF file, unless the document uses the Excel file format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	hr	For files opened in Excel format, all sheets that do not contain a defined print range are printed. The same behavior occurs when you export the Excel formatted spreadsheet to a PDF file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FE				0	hr	To Define a Print Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	hr	Select the cells that you want to print.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10909				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Define\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10910				0	hr	To Add Cells to a Print Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	hr	Select the cells that you want to add to the existing print range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091B				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10922				0	hr	To Clear a Print Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10929				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Remove\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10953				0	hr	Using the Page Break Preview to Edit Print Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093E				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, print ranges as well as page break regions are outlined by a blue border and contain a centered page number in gray. Nonprinting areas have a gray background.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	hr	To define a new page break region, drag the border to a new location. When you define a new page break region, an automatic page break is replaced by a manual page break.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10930				0	hr	To View and Edit Print Ranges				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10937				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>View - Page Break Preview\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082A				0	hr	To change the default zoom factor of the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, double click the percentage value on the \<emph\>Status\</emph\> bar, and select a new zoom factor.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10836				0	hr	Edit the print range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10944				0	hr	To change the size of a print range, drag a border of the range to a new location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	hr	To delete a manual page break that is contained in a print range, drag the border of the page break outside of the print range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10948				0	hr	To clear a print range, drag a border of the range onto the opposite border of the range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	hr	To exit the \<emph\>Page Break Preview\</emph\>, choose \<emph\>View - Normal\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\printranges.xhp	0	help	par_idN109CF				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\"\>Editing Print Ranges\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Tekstni eksponent/indeks				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>superscript text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subscript text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text super/sub\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters;superscript/subscript\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151112				0	hr	\<variable id=\"super_subscript\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/super_subscript.xhp\" name=\"Text Superscript / Subscript\"\>Text Superscript / Subscript\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	hr	In the cell, select the character that you want to put in superscript or subscript.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	hr	If, for example, you want to write H20 with a subscript 2, select the 2 in the cell (not in the input line).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	hr	Open the context menu for the selected character and choose \<emph\>Character\</emph\>. You will see the \<emph\>Character\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Font Position\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	hr	Select the \<emph\>Subscript\</emph\> option and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020500.xhp\" name=\"Context menu - Character - Font Position\"\>Context menu - Character - Font Position\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	 Importing and Exporting CSV Files 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id892361				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>number series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; text databases\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>delimited values and files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comma separated files and values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text file import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>csv files;importing and exporting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	hr	\<variable id=\"csv_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_files.xhp\"\>Opening and Saving Text CSV Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10880				0	hr	Comma Separated Values (CSV) is text file format that you can use to exchange data from a database or a spreadsheet between applications. Each line in a Text CSV file represents a record in the database, or a row in a spreadsheet. Each field in a database record or cell in a spreadsheet row is usually separated by a comma. However, you can use other characters to delimit a field, such as a tabulator character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10886				0	hr	If the content of a field or cell contains a comma, the contents of the field or cell \<emph\>must\</emph\> be enclosed by single quotes (') or double quotes (").				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10890				0	hr	To Open a Text CSV file in Calc				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089F				0	hr	Locate the CSV file that you want to open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	hr	If the file has a *.csv extension, select the file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	hr	If the CSV file has another extension, select the file, and then select "Text CSV" in the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082D				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	hr	The \<emph\>Text Import\</emph\> dialog opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B1				0	hr	Specify the options to divide the text in the file into columns.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BB				0	hr	You can preview the layout of the imported data at the bottom of the \<emph\>Text Import\</emph\> dialog. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id8444166				0	hr	Right-click a column in the preview to set the format or to hide the column.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	hr	If the CSV file uses a text delimiter character that is not listed in the \<emph\>Text delimiter\</emph\> box, click in the box, and type the character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FA				0	hr	To Save a Sheet as a Text CSV File				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FC				0	hr	When you export a spreadsheet to CSV format, only the data on the current sheet is saved. All other information, including formulas and formatting, is lost.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10901				0	hr	Open the Calc sheet that you want to save as a Text CSV file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	hr	Only the current sheet can be exported.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>File - Save as\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10915				0	hr	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, enter a name for the file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1090D				0	hr	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> box, select "Text CSV".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DD				0	hr	(Optional) Set the field options for the Text CSV file.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091C				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Edit filter settings\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog, select the options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FC				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options - Spreadsheet - View\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Primjena visestrukih operatora 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559				0	hr	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	hr	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	hr	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions. In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range where you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	hr	If the data of a data range is arranged in columns or arranged in rows, select the data range together with the cell or cell range next to or below it as the target range. In the \<emph\>Column/Row\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the first cell in the data range. In the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the cell with the formula that applies to the data range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	hr	Primjeri				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	hr	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239				0	hr	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888				0	hr	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	hr	In column D enter certain annual sales, one under the other; for example, in steps of 500 from 500 to 5000.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115				0	hr	Mark the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	46			0	hr	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	hr	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that: B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the marked column values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009				0	hr	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will see the profit in column E.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725				0	hr	Calculating with Several Formulas Simultaneously				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	hr	Delete column E.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675				0	hr	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885				0	hr	Select the range D2;F11, thus three columns.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846				0	hr	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, select cells B5 through C5.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	hr	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Columns\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862				0	hr	Close the dialog with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You will now see the profits in column E and the annual profit per item in column F.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	hr	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584				0	hr	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> allows you to carry out joint multiple operations for columns and rows in so-called cross-tables. The formula cell has to refer to both the data range arranged in rows and the one arranged in columns. Select the range defined by both data ranges and call the multiple operation dialog. Enter the reference to the formula in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> field. The \<emph\>Row\</emph\> field is used to enter the reference to the first cell of the range arranged in rows, and the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field the first cell of the range arranged in columns.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949				0	hr	Calculating with Two Variables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808				0	hr	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731				0	hr	Expand the table shown above. D2 through D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810				0	hr	Select the range D1:H11.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	hr	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	hr	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Rows\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049				0	hr	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141				0	hr	Close the dialog with OK. You will see the profits in the range E2:H11. In some cases you must first press F9 to update the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Applying Filters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153896				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>filters; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>advanced filters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; deleting with filters\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	hr	\<variable id=\"filters\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp\" name=\"Applying Filters\"\>Applying Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	hr	Filters and advanced filters allow you to work on certain filtered rows (records) of a data range. In the spreadsheets in $[officename] there are various possibilities for applying filters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	hr	One use for the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function is to quickly restrict the display to records with identical entries in a data field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> dialog, you can also define ranges which contain the values in particular data fields. You can use the standard filter to connect up to three conditions with either a logical AND or a logical OR operator.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	hr	The \<emph\>Advanced filter\</emph\> exceeds the three condition limitation and allows up to a total of eight filter conditions. With advanced filters you enter the conditions directly into the sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id9384746				0	hr	To remove a filter, so that you see all cells again, click inside the area where the filter was applied, then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	hr	When you select filtered rows and then either apply formatting, or delete the selected rows, this action then applies only to the filtered rows. The hidden rows are not affected. This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id218817				0	hr	This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Ispis redova ili stupaca na svakoj stranici				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheets on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repeating;columns/rows on printed pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; printing on all sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; rows/columns as table headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings;repeating rows/columns as\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153727				0	hr	\<variable id=\"print_title_row\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_title_row.xhp\" name=\"Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\"\>Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	hr	If you have a sheet that is so large that it will be printed multiple pages, you can set up rows or columns to repeat on each printed page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hr	As an example, If you want to print the top two rows of the sheet as well as the first column (A)on all pages, do the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Print Ranges - Edit\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Edit Print Ranges\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	hr	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	hr	The dialog shrinks so that you can see more of the sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	hr	Select the first two rows and, for this example, click cell A1 and drag to A2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	hr	In the shrunk dialog you will see $1:$2. Rows 1 and 2 are now rows to repeat.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	hr	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area. The dialog is restored again.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	hr	If you also want column A as a column to repeat, click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	hr	Click column A (not in the column header).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	hr	Click the icon again at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	hr	Rows to repeat are rows from the sheet. You can define headers and footers to be printed on each print page independently of this in \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155380				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146113				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\"\>Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Koristenje Scenarija 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149664				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>scenarios; creating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;sample scenarios\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;scenarios in Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	hr	\<variable id=\"scenario\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp\" name=\"Using Scenarios\"\>Using Scenarios\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	hr	$[officename] Calc Scenarios are important aids for making numbers that are dependent upon each other, and their resulting calculations, visible. Scenarios allow you create a list of values to select from for a given cell or group of cells. The contents of these cells change when you select different items from the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149255				0	hr	Creating Your Own Scenarios				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704	16			0	hr	To create a scenario, select all the cells that provide the data for the scenario. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	hr	Select the cells that are already highlighted by the frame of the existing scenario. You can also select multiple cells distributed across the table. To select multiple cells, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Command\</item\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl\</item\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key as you click each cell. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Scenarios\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Create Scenario\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	hr	Enter a name for the new scenario and leave the other fields unchanged with their default values. Close the dialog with OK. Your new scenario is automatically activated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	hr	Using Ready-Made Scenarios				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	hr	Scenarios can also be selected in the Navigator:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	12			0	hr	Open the Navigator with the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon on the Standard bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	13			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon in the Navigator (the icon with the question and exclamation marks).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	hr	In the Navigator, you see the defined scenarios with the comments that were entered when the scenarios were created.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id1243629				0	hr	Double-click a scenario name in the Navigator to apply that scenario to the current sheet.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id9044770				0	hr	To delete a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3674123				0	hr	To edit a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	hr	To hide the border of a set of cells that are part of a scenario, open the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog for each scenario that affects the cells and clear the Display border checkbox. Hiding the border also removes the listbox on the sheet where you can choose the scenarios.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	hr	If you want to know which values in the scenario affect other values, choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Trace Dependents\</emph\>. You will see arrows to the cells that are directly dependent on the current cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Creating Scenarios\"\>Creating Scenarios\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	User-Defined Functions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>functions; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic IDE for user-defined functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>IDE; Basic IDE\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>programming;functions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	hr	\<variable id=\"userdefined_function\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/userdefined_function.xhp\" name=\"Defining Functions Yourself\"\>User-Defined Functions\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969				0	hr	You can apply user-defined functions in $[officename] Calc in the following ways:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	hr	You can define your own functions using the Basic-IDE. This method requires a basic knowledge of programming.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	hr	You can program functions as \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060111.xhp\" name=\"add-ins\"\>add-ins\</link\>. This method requires an advanced knowledge of programming.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	hr	Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button. You will now see the Basic IDE.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	hr	Enter the function code. In this example, we define a \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> function that calculates the volume of a rectangular solid with side lengths \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\> and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	hr	Close the Basic-IDE window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	hr	Your function is automatically saved in the default module and is now available. If you apply the function in a Calc document that is to be used on another computer, you can copy the function to the Calc document as described in the next section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	hr	Copying a Function To a Document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145232	19			0	hr	In stage 2 of "Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic", in the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialog you clicked on \<emph\>Edit \</emph\>. As the default, in the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field the \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> module is selected. The \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> library resides locally in your user directory.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	hr	If you want to copy the user-defined function to a Calc document:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150086				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	hr	In the Basic-IDE, select the source of your user-defined function and copy it to the clipboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081D				0	hr	Close the Basic-IDE.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>(Name of the Calc document) - Standard - Module1\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699				0	hr	Paste the clipboard contents in the Basic-IDE of the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	hr	Applying a User-defined Function in $[officename] Calc				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148869				0	hr	Once you have defined the function \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> in the Basic-IDE, you can apply it the same way as the built-in functions of $[officename] Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	hr	Open a Calc document and enter numbers for the function parameters \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\> in cells A1, B1, and C1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	hr	Set the cursor in another cell and enter the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	hr	=VOL(A1;B1;C1)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3146776				0	hr	The function is evaluated and you will see the result in the selected cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Pridruživanje formata formulama				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145673				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>formats; assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell formats; assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>STYLE function example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles;assigning by formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;assigning cell formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;cell formats\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145673	13			0	hr	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_by_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_by_formula.xhp\" name=\"Assigning Formats by Formula\"\>Assigning Formats by Formula\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	hr	The STYLE() function can be added to an existing formula in a cell. For example, together with the CURRENT function, you can color a cell depending on its value. The formula =...+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3; "Red"; "Green")) applies the cell style "Red" to cells if the value is greater than 3, otherwise the cell style "Green" is applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385				0	hr	If you would like to apply a formula to all cells in a selected area, you can use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find & Replace\</item\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149456				0	hr	Select all the desired cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148797				0	hr	Select the menu command \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767	18			0	hr	For the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> term, enter: .*				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153770				0	hr	".*" is a regular expression that designates the contents of the current cell.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143	20			0	hr	Enter the following formula in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> field: =&+STYLE(IF(CURRENT()>3;"Red";"Green"))				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hr	The "&" symbol designates the current contents of the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> field. The line must begin with an equal sign, since it is a formula. It is assumed that the cell styles "Red" and "Green" already exist.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	hr	Mark the fields \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100000.xhp\" name=\"Regular expressions\"\>\<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>\</link\> and \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3144767				0	hr	All cells with contents that were included in the selection are now highlighted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_by_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3147127				0	hr	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace all\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Validity of Cell Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156442				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>values; limiting on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>limits; specifying value limits on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>permitted cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error messages; defining for incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>actions in case of incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips; defining text for cell input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>notes;help text for cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining input help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>macros; running when incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; validity check\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	hr	\<variable id=\"validity\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/validity.xhp\" name=\"Validity of Cell Contents\"\>Validity of Cell Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	hr	For each cell, you can define entries to be valid. Invalid entries to a cell will be rejected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	hr	The validity rule is activated when a new value is entered. If an invalid value has already been inserted into the cell, or if you insert a value in the cell either with drag-and-drop or by copying and pasting, the validity rule will not take effect.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id5174718				0	hr	You can choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective\</emph\> at any time and choose the command \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>\<emph\>Mark Invalid Data\</emph\>\</link\> to display which cells contain invalid values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603				0	hr	Using Cell Contents Validity				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	hr	Select the cells for which you want to define a new validity rule.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837	8			0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Validity\</item\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156020	9			0	hr	On the \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> tab page, enter the conditions for new values entered into cells. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159208				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Allow\</emph\> field, select an option.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011				0	hr	If you select "Whole Numbers", values such as "12.5" are not allowed. Choosing "Date" allows date information both in the local date format as well as in the form of a \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"serial date\"\>serial date\</link\>. Similarly, the "Time" condition permits time values such as "12:00" or serial time numbers. "Text Length" stipulates that cells are allowed to contain text only.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id9224829				0	hr	Select "List" to enter a list of valid entries.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149317				0	hr	Select the next condition under \<emph\>Data\</emph\>. According to what you choose, additional options will be selectable.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	hr	After you have determined the conditions for cell validity, you can use the other two tab pages to create message boxes:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159261				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Input Help\</emph\> tab page, enter the title and the text of the tip, which will then be displayed if the cell is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page, select the action to be carried out in the event of an error.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3147416				0	hr	If you select "Stop" as the action, invalid entries are not accepted, and the previous cell contents are retained.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033				0	hr	Select "Warning" or "Information" to display a dialog in which the entry can either be canceled or accepted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	hr	If you select "Macro", then by using the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button you can specify a macro to be run in the event of an error.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149011	35			0	hr	To display the error message, select \<emph\>Show error message when invalid values are entered\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	hr	After changing the action for a cell on the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page and closing the dialog with OK, you must first select another cell before the change takes effect.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3154805				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Validity\"\>Data - Validity\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Spajanje i dijeljenje celija				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147240				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>cells; merging/unmerging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; merging cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell merges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>unmerging cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging;cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id8005005				0	hr	\<variable id=\"table_cellmerge\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/table_cellmerge.xhp\" name=\"Merging and Unmerging Cells\"\>Merging and Unmerging Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id8049867				0	hr	You can select adjacent cells, then merge them into a single cell. Conversely, you can take a large cell that has been created by merging single cells, and divide it back into individual cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200913480176				0	hr	When you copy cells into a target range containing merged cells, the target range gets unmerged first, then the copied cells are pasted in. If the copied cells are merged cells, they retain their merge state.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id235602				0	hr	Merging Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id1272927				0	hr	Select the adjacent cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id6424146				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	hd_id451368				0	hr	Canceling the merging of cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id7116611				0	hr	Place the cursor in the cell to be split.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\table_cellmerge.xhp	0	help	par_id9493087				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Merge Cells\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Primjena pogofbenog oblikovanja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>conditional formatting; cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting; conditional formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles;conditional styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell formats; conditional\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>random numbers;examples\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; copying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; cell styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; copying cell styles\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263				0	hr	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_conditional\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_conditional.xhp\" name=\"Applying Conditional Formatting\"\>Applying Conditional Formatting\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159156				0	hr	Using the menu command \<emph\>Format - Conditional formatting\</emph\>, the dialog allows you to define up to three conditions per cell, which must be met in order for the selected cells to have a particular format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id8039796				0	hr	To apply conditional formatting, AutoCalculate must be enabled. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> (you see a check mark next to the command when AutoCalculate is enabled).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	hr	With conditional formatting, you can, for example, highlight the totals that exceed the average value of all totals. If the totals change, the formatting changes correspondingly, without having to apply other styles manually.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id4480727				0	hr	To Define the Conditions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	hr	Select the cells to which you want to apply a conditional style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	hr	Enter the condition(s) into the dialog box. The dialog is described in detail in \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] Help\"\>$[officename] Help\</link\>, and an example is provided below:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	hr	Example of Conditional Formatting: Generate Number Values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id4341868				0	hr	Step1: Generate Number Values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	hr	You want to give certain values in your tables particular emphasis. For example, in a table of turnovers, you can show all the values above the average in green and all those below the average in red. This is possible with conditional formatting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155337				0	hr	First of all, write a table in which a few different values occur. For your test you can create tables with any random numbers:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	hr	In one of the cells enter the formula =RAND(), and you will obtain a random number between 0 and 1. If you want integers of between 0 and 50, enter the formula =INT(RAND()*50).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149258				0	hr	Copy the formula to create a row of random numbers. Click the bottom right corner of the selected cell, and drag to the right until the desired cell range is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	hr	In the same way as described above, drag down the corner of the rightmost cell in order to create more rows of random numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149211				0	hr	Example of Conditional Formatting: Define Cell Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	hr	The next step is to apply a cell style to all values that represent above-average turnover, and one to those that are below the average. Ensure that the Styles and Formatting window is visible before proceeding.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	hr	Click in a blank cell and select the command \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> in the context menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> dialog on the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab, select a background color. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	hr	In the Styles and Formatting window, click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon. Enter the name of the new style. For this example, name the style "Above".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3152889				0	hr	To define a second style, click again in a blank cell and proceed as described above. Assign a different background color for the cell and assign a name (for this example, "Below").				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148704				0	hr	Example of Conditional Formatting: Calculate Average				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837				0	hr	In our particular example, we are calculating the average of the random values. The result is placed in a cell:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	hr	Set the cursor in a blank cell, for example, J14, and choose \<emph\>Insert - Function\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3156016				0	hr	Select the AVERAGE function. Use the mouse to select all your random numbers. If you cannot see the entire range, because Function Wizard is obscuring it, you can temporarily shrink the dialog using the \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#eingabesymbol\" name=\"Shrink or Maximize\"\>Shrink / Maximize\</link\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153246				0	hr	Close Function Wizard with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149898				0	hr	Example of Conditional Formatting: Apply Cell Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	hr	Now you can apply the conditional formatting to the sheet:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	hr	Select all cells with the random numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153801				0	hr	Choose the \<emph\>Format - Conditional Formatting\</emph\> command to open the corresponding dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153013				0	hr	Define the condition as follows: If cell value is less than J14, format with cell style "Below", and if cell value is greater than or equal to J14, format with cell style "Above".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155761				0	hr	Example of Conditional Formatting: Copy Cell Style				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3145320				0	hr	To apply the conditional formatting to other cells later:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3153074				0	hr	Click one of the cells that has been assigned conditional formatting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3149051				0	hr	Copy the cell to the clipboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3150436				0	hr	Select the cells that are to receive this same formatting.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3147298				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste Special\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Paste Special\</emph\> dialog appears.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3166465				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Selection\</emph\> area, check only the \<emph\>Formats\</emph\> box. All other boxes must be unchecked. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_conditional.xhp	0	help	par_id3159123				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05120000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Conditional formatting\"\>Format - Conditional formatting\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Printing Sheet Details				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>printing;sheet details\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing details\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids; printing sheet grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; printing, instead of results\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>notes; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet grids; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; printing grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; printing cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>zero values; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>null values; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	hr	\<variable id=\"print_details\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_details.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheet Details\"\>Printing Sheet Details\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	hr	When printing a sheet you can select which details are to be printed:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	hr	Row and column headers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	hr	Sheet grid				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	hr	Zabilješke				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	hr	Objects and graphics				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	hr	Grafikoni				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	hr	Crtani objekti				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	hr	Formule				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	hr	To choose the details proceed as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	hr	Select the sheet you want to print.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340	13			0	hr	The command is not visible if the sheet was opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
