helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Filtering Cell Ranges 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153541				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; filtering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;filtering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering; database ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtering;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>database ranges; removing filters\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	hr	\<variable id=\"database_filter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/database_filter.xhp\" name=\"Filtering Cell Ranges\"\>Filtering Cell Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	hr	You can use several filters to filter cell ranges in spreadsheets. A standard filter uses the options that you specify to filter the data. An AutoFilter filters data according to a specific value or string. An advanced filter uses filter criteria from specified cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	hr	To Apply a Standard Filter to a Cell Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150398				0	hr	Click in a cell range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10693				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Standard Filter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, specify the filter options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A5				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153143				0	hr	The records that match the filter options that you specified are shown.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	hr	To Apply an AutoFilter to a Cell Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	hr	Click in a cell range or a database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id9303872				0	hr	If you want to apply multiple AutoFilters to the same sheet, you must first define database ranges, then apply the AutoFilters to the database ranges.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106DB				0	hr	An arrow button is added to the head of each column in the database range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	hr	Click the arrow button in the column that contains the value or string that you want to set as the filter criteria.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	hr	Select the value or string that you want to use as the filter criteria.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074C				0	hr	The records that match the filter criteria that you selected are shown.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E8				0	hr	To Remove a Filter From a Cell Range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075C				0	hr	Click in a filtered cell range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EC				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\database_filter.xhp	0	help	par_id4525284				0	hr	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Defining_a_Data_Range\"\>Wiki page about defining a data range\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Using Rounded Off Numbers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; rounded off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounded off numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exact numbers in $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;number of decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;rounded in calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rounded off values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>precision as shown\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding precision\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; values as shown\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	hr	\<variable id=\"rounding_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rounding_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Using Rounded Off Numbers\"\>Using Rounded Off Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	hr	In $[officename] Calc, all decimal numbers are displayed rounded off to two decimal places.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	hr	To change this for selected cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	hr	Mark all the cells you want to modify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and go to the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> field, select \<emph\>Number\</emph\>. Under \<emph\>Options\</emph\>, change the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415				0	hr	To permanently change this everywhere				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	hr	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Modify the number of \<emph\>Decimal places\</emph\> and exit the dialog with OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154755				0	hr	To calculate with the rounded off numbers instead of the internal exact values				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\> .				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	hr	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Mark the\<emph\> Precision as shown\</emph\> field and exit the dialog with OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
