helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	DataPilot				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150448				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Pivot table, see DataPilot function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448				0	hr	\<variable id=\"datapilot\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot.xhp\" name=\"DataPilot\"\>DataPilot\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	hr	The \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\> (sometimes known as \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\>) allows you to combine, compare, and analyze large amounts of data. You can view different summaries of the source data, you can display the details of areas of interest, and you can create reports.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	hr	A table that has been created with the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090000.xhp\" name=\"DataPilot\"\>DataPilot\</link\> is an interactive table. Data can be arranged, rearranged or summarized according to different points of view.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Uredjivanje DataPilot Tabela. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot function; editing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;DataPilot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	hr	\<variable id=\"datapilot_edittable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_edittable.xhp\" name=\"Editing DataPilot Tables\"\>Editing DataPilot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	hr	Click one of the buttons in the table that the DataPilot has created and hold the mouse button down. A special symbol will appear next to the mouse pointer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	hr	By dragging the button to a different position in the same row you can alter the order of the columns. If you drag a button to the left edge of the table into the row headings area, you can change a column into a row.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id1648915				0	hr	In the DataPilot dialog, you can drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated DataPilot table. The listbox can be used to filter the DataPilot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated DataPilot table to use another page field as a filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	hr	To remove a button from the table, just drag it out of the DataPilot table. Release the mouse button when the mouse pointer positioned within the sheet has become a 'not allowed' icon. The button is deleted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	hr	To edit the DataPilot table, click a cell inside the DataPilot table and open the context menu. In the context menu you find the command \<emph\>Start\</emph\>, which displays the \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\> dialog for the current DataPilot table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id2666096				0	hr	In the pivot table, you can use drag-and-drop or cut/paste commands to rearrange the order of data fields.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_edittable.xhp	0	help	par_id266609688				0	hr	You can assign custom display names to fields, field members, subtotals (with some restrictions), and grand totals inside pivot tables. A custom display name is assigned to an item by overwriting the original name with another name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Automatically Calculating Series				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>series; calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>linear series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>growth series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>date series\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>powers of 2 calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; filling automatically\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>auto filling cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoFill function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filling;cells, automatically\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	hr	\<variable id=\"calc_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Calculating Series\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	hr	You can automatically fill cells with data with the AutoFill command or the Series command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D3				0	hr	Using AutoFill				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D7				0	hr	AutoFill automatically generates a data series based on a defined pattern.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	hr	On a sheet, click in cell, and type a number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	hr	Click in another cell and then click back in the cell where you typed the number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	hr	Drag the fill handle in the bottom right corner of the cell across the cells that you want to fill, and release the mouse button.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	hr	The cells are filled with ascending numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EE				0	hr	To quickly create a list of consecutive days, enter "Monday" in a cell, and drag the fill handle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9720145				0	hr	Hold down Ctrl if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	hr	If you select two or more adjacent cells that contain different numbers, and drag, the remaining cells are filled with the arithmetic pattern that is recognized in the numbers. The AutoFill function also recognizes customized lists that are defined under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	hr	You can double-click the fill handle to automatically fill all empty columns of the current data block. For example, first enter Jan into A1 and drag the fill handle down to A12 to get the twelve months in the first column. Now enter some values into B1 and C1. Select those two cells, and double-click the fill handle. This fills automatically the data block B1:C12.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	hr	Using a Defined Series				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	hr	Select the cell range in the sheet that you want to fill.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Fill - Series\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	hr	Select the parameters for the series. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	hr	If you select a \<emph\>linear\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>added\</emph\> to each consecutive number in the series to create the next value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073C				0	hr	If you select a \<emph\>growth\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>multiplied\</emph\> by each consecutive number to create the next value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10747				0	hr	If you select a \<emph\>date\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is added to the time unit that you specify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3159173				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Using AutoFormat for Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155132				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>tables; AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;AutoFormat function for tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>AutoFormat function;defining and applying formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; automatically formatting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>automatic formatting in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;AutoFormat function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;automatic formatting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155132				0	hr	\<variable id=\"autoformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autoformat.xhp\" name=\"Using AutoFormat for Tables\"\>Applying Automatic Formatting to a Selected Cell Range\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149401				0	hr	You can use the AutoFormat feature to quickly apply format a sheet or a selected cell range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10702				0	hr	To apply an AutoFormat to a sheet or selected cell range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CE				0	hr	Select the cells, including the column and row headers, that you want to format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - AutoFormat\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	hr	To select which properties to include in an AutoFormat, click \<emph\>More\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN10715				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	hr	The format is applied to the selected range of cells.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210				0	hr	If you do not see any change in color of the cell contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Value Highlighting\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155379				0	hr	To define an AutoFormat for spreadsheets				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autoformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	hr	You can define a new AutoFormat that is available to all spreadsheets.				20181231 09:50:43
