helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	hd_id9216284				0	hr	\<variable id=\"solver\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/solver.xhp\"\>Solver\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9210486				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Opens the Solver dialog. A solver allows to solve equations with multiple unknown variables by goal seeking methods.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id8538773				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter or click the cell reference of the target cell. This field takes the address of the cell whose value is to be optimized.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7564012				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation for a maximum value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id1186254				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation for a minimum value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7432477				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Try to solve the equation to approach a given value of the target cell.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7141026				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the value or a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id8531449				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the cell range that can be changed.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Select an operator from the list.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter a value or a cell reference.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id1939451				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to shrink or restore the dialog. You can click or select cells in the sheet. You can enter a cell reference manually in the input box.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to remove the row from the list. Any rows from below this row move up.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2423780				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Opens the Options dialog.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Click to solve the equation with the current settings. The dialog settings are retained until you close the current document.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5474410				0	hr	To solve equations with the solver				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id2216559				0	hr	The goal of the solver process is to find those variable values of an equation that result in an optimized value in the \<emph\>target cell\</emph\>, also named the "objective". You can choose whether the value in the target cell should be a maximum, a minimum, or approaching a given value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id7869502				0	hr	The initial variable values are inserted in a rectangular cell range that you enter in the \<emph\>By changing cells\</emph\> box. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id9852900				0	hr	You can define a series of limiting conditions that set constraints for some cells. For example, you can set the constraint that one of the variables or cells must not be bigger than another variable, or not bigger than a given value. You can also define the constraint that one or more variables must be integers (values without decimals), or binary values (where only 0 and 1 are allowed).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\solver.xhp	0	help	par_id5323953				0	hr	The default solver engine supports only linear equations.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	DATE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155511				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>DATE function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155511				0	hr	\<variable id=\"date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_date.xhp\"\>DATE\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153551				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATUM\"\>This function converts a date written as year, month, day to an internal serial number and displays it in the cell's formatting.\</ahelp\> The default format of a cell containing the DATE function is the date format, but you can format the cells with the \<emph\>0\</emph\> number format, which displays the internal serial number of the date as a number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148590				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150474				0	hr	DATE(year; month; day)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152815				0	hr	\<emph\>Year\</emph\> is an integer between 1583 and 9956 or 0 and 99.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153222				0	hr	In \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - General \</emph\>you can set from which year a two-digit number entry is recognized as 20xx.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155817				0	hr	\<emph\>Month\</emph\> is an integer between 1 and 12 indicating the month.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	hr	\<emph\>Day\</emph\> is a number between 1 and 31 indicating the day of the month.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	hr	If the values for month and day are higher, they are carried over to the next digit. If you enter =DATE(00;12;31) the result will be "12/31/00." If, on the other hand, you enter =DATE(00;13;31) the result will be "1/31/01."				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147477				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3152589				0	hr	DATE("00;1;1") yields 1/1/00				20181231 09:50:43
