helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150475				0	hr	Rate: the periodic interest rate.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921				0	hr	NPER: the payment period with the total number of periods. NPER can also be a non-integer value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	hr	pv: the current value in the sequence of payments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156259				0	hr	S: the first period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155990				0	hr	E: the last period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149777				0	hr	Type: the due date of the payment at the beginning or end of each period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153723				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147478	277			0	hr	What are the interest payments at a yearly interest rate of 5.5 %, a payment period of monthly payments for 2 years and a current cash value of 5,000 currency units? The start period is the 4th and the end period is the 6th period. The payment is due at the beginning of each period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819				0	hr	CUMIPMT(5.5%/12;24;5000;4;6;1) = -57.54 currency units. The interest payments for between the 4th and 6th period are 57.54 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3083280				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>CUMIPMT_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
