helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3145087				0	hr	CUMIPMT_ADD(Rate;NPER;Pv;Start period;End period;Type)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149277				0	hr	Rate: the interest rate for each period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149270				0	hr	NPER: the total number of payment periods. The rate and NPER must refer to the same unit, and thus both be calculated annually or monthly.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3152967				0	hr	Pv: the current value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156308				0	hr	Start period: the first payment period for the calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149453				0	hr	End period: the last payment period for the calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150962				0	hr	Type: the maturity of a payment at the end of each period (Type = 0) or at the start of the period (Type = 1).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152933				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156324				0	hr	The following mortgage loan is taken out on a house:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147566				0	hr	Rate: 9.00 per cent per annum (9% / 12 = 0.0075), Duration: 30 years (NPER = 30 * 12 = 360), Pv: 125000 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3151272				0	hr	How much interest must you pay in the second year of the mortgage (thus from periods 13 to 24)?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156130				0	hr	=CUMIPMT_ADD(0.0075;360;125000;13;24;0) returns -11135.23.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3150764				0	hr	How much interest must you pay in the first month?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146857				0	hr	=CUMIPMT_ADD(0.0075;360;125000;1;1;0) vraca -937.50.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150878				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>PRICE function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>prices; fixed interest securities\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sales values;fixed interest securities\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
