helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154289				0	hr	Settlement date: February 15 1999, maturity date: April 13 1999, issue date: November 11 1998. Interest rate: 6.1 per cent, yield: 6.1 per cent, basis: 30/360 = 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154905				0	hr	The price is calculated as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3158409				0	hr	=PRICEMAT("2/15/1999";"4/13/1999";"11/11/1998"; 0.061; 0.061;0)  vraca 99.98449888. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148448				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>calculating; durations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>durations;calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DURATION function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148448				0	hr	DURATION				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153056				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LAUFZEIT\"\>Calculates the number of periods required by an investment to attain the desired value.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148933				0	hr	DURATION(Rate;PV;FV)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148801				0	hr	Rate: a constant. The interest rate is to be calculated for the entire duration (duration period). The interest rate per period is calculated by dividing the interest rate by the calculated duration. The internal rate for an annuity is to be entered as Rate/12.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	hr	PV: the present (current) value. The cash value is the deposit of cash or the current cash value of an allowance in kind. As a deposit value a positive value must be entered; the deposit must not be 0 or <0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515				0	hr	FV: the expected value. The future value determines the desired (future) value of the deposit.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153579				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3148480				0	hr	At an interest rate of 4.75%, a cash value of 25,000 currency units and a future value of 1,000,000 currency units, a duration of 79.49 payment periods is returned. The periodic payment is the resulting quotient from the future value and the duration, in this case 1,000,000/79.49=12,850.20.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148912				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;linear depreciations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>depreciations;linear\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>linear depreciations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>straight-line depreciations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SLN function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148912				0	hr	SLN				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149154	291			0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LIA\"\>Returns the straight-line depreciation of an asset for one period.\</ahelp\>The amount of the depreciation is constant during the depreciation period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153240				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3166456				0	hr	SLN(COST; SALVAGE; LIFE)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3146955				0	hr	COST: the initial cost of an asset.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3149796				0	hr	SALVAGE: the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3166444				0	hr	LIFE: the depreciation period determining the number of periods in the depreciation of the asset.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155579				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154098				0	hr	Office equipment with an initial cost of 50,000 currency units is to be depreciated over 7 years. The value at the end of the depreciation is to be 3,500 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	hr	SLN(50000;3,500;84) = 553.57 currency units. The periodic monthly depreciation of the office equipment is 553.57 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
