helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:EDIT:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:ED_COPY_AREA\"\>Select the check box, and then select the cell range where you want to display the filter results.\</ahelp\> You can also select a named range from the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145272				0	hr	Regularni izraz				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_REGEXP\"\>Allows you to use wildcards in the filter definition.\</ahelp\> For a list of the regular expressions that $[officename] supports, click \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"here\"\>here\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	hr	If the \<emph\>Regular Expressions\</emph\> check box is selected, you can use regular expressions in the Value field if the Condition list box is set to '=' EQUAL or '<>' UNEQUAL. This also applies to the respective cells that you reference for an advanced filter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149958				0	hr	Nema dvostukog pojavljivanja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_SPEC_FILTER:BTN_UNIQUE\"\>Excludes duplicate rows in the list of filtered data.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154018				0	hr	Sačuvaj kriterij filtra				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SC:CHECKBOX:RID_SCDLG_FILTER:BTN_DEST_PERS\"\>Select the \<emph\>Copy results to\</emph\> check box, and then specify the destination range where you want to display the filtered data. If this box is checked, the destination range remains linked to the source range. You must have defined the source range under \<emph\>Data - Define range\</emph\> as a database range.\</ahelp\> Following this, you can reapply the defined filter at any time as follows: click into the source range, then choose \<emph\>Data - Refresh Range\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	hr	Data range				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	hr	Displays the cell range or the name of the cell range that you want to filter.				20181231 09:50:43
