helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3149638				0	hr	Odaberite domet te odaberite MINVERSE. Odaberite izlazni  niy,odaberite  \<emph\>NIZ\</emph\> polje te kliknite 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148546				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>MMULT function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148546				0	hr	MMULT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3148518				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MMULT\"\>Calculates the array product of two arrays.\</ahelp\> The number of columns for array 1 must match the number of rows for array 2. The square array has an equal number of rows and columns.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146767				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150798				0	hr	MMULT(array; array)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3150812				0	hr	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> at first place represents the first array used in the array product.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3152553				0	hr	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> at second place represents the second array with the same number of rows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN114C3				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152574				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3146826				0	hr	Select a square range. Choose the MMULT function. Select the first \<emph\>Array\</emph\>, then select the second \<emph\>Array\</emph\>. Using \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The output array will appear in the first selected range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154970				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>TRANSPOSE function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154970				0	hr	TRANSPOSE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155276				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MTRANS\"\>Transposes the rows and columns of an array.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155294				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3153843				0	hr	TRANSPOSE(array)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3153857				0	hr	\<emph\>Array\</emph\> represents the array in the spreadsheet that is to be transposed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN115A5				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159352				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3159366				0	hr	In the spreadsheet, select the range in which the transposed array can appear. If the original array has n rows and m columns, your selected range must have at least m rows and n columns. Then enter the formula directly, select the original array and press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Shift+Command+Enter \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Shift+Ctrl+Enter\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. Or, if you are using the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Array\</emph\> check box. The transposed array appears in the selected target range and is protected automatically against changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109846				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>LINEST function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109846				0	hr	LINEST				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3144733				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RGP\"\>Returns the parameters of a linear trend.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152825				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3152839				0	hr	LINEST(Data_Y; Data_X; Linear_Type; Stats)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3152853				0	hr	\<emph\>Data_Y\</emph\> represents the Y Data array.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154428				0	hr	\<emph\>Data_X\</emph\> (optional) represents the X Data array.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200804502119				0	hr	LINEST finds a straight line \<item type=\"literal\"\>y = a + bx\</item\> that best fits the data, using linear regression (the "least squares" method). With more than one set of variables the straight line is of the form \<item type=\"literal\"\>y = a + b1x1 + b2x2 ... + bnxn\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154448				0	hr	\<emph\>Linear_Type\</emph\> (optional). If the line goes through the zero point, then set Linear_Type = 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154142				0	hr	\<emph\>Stats\</emph\> (optional). If Stats=0, only the regression coefficient is to be calculated. Otherwise, you will see other stats.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200804502261				0	hr	LINEST returns a table (array) of statistics as below and must be entered as an array formula (for example by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+Return rather than just Return).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN11416				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_idN116C6				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#moreontop\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154162				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3154176				0	hr	This function returns an array and is handled in the same way as the other array functions. Select a range for the answers and then the function. Select Data_Y. If you want, you can enter other parameters. Select \<emph\>Array\</emph\> and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	par_id3155468				0	hr	The results returned by the system (if Stats = 0), will at least show the slope of the regression line and its intersection with the Y axis. If \<emph\>Stats\</emph\> do not equal 0, other results are to be displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060107.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155491				0	hr	Other LINEST Results:				20181231 09:50:43
