helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6807458				0	hr	COMBIN returns the number of ways to choose these items. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 3 different ways, namely AB, AC and BC.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7414471				0	hr	COMBIN implements the formula: count_1!/(count_2!*(count_1-count_2)!)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153171				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153517				0	hr	COMBIN(3;2) returns 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150284				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>COMBINA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations with repetitions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150284				0	hr	COMBINA				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of ordered combinations of a subset of items.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145752				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765				0	hr	COMBINA(count_1; count_2)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	hr	\<emph\>count_1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544				0	hr	\<emph\>count_2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	hr	COMBINA returns the number of ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is important. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AB, BA, AC, CA, BC and CB.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	hr	COMBINA implements the formula: count_1!/(count_1-count_2)!				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154584				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904				0	hr	COMBINA(3;2) returns 6.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156086				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>TRUNC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;cutting off\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156086				0	hr	TRUNC				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157866				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUERZEN\"\>Truncates a number by removing decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148499				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148511				0	hr	TRUNC(number; count)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150796				0	hr	Returns \<emph\>number\</emph\> with at most \<emph\>count\</emph\> decimal places. Excess decimal places are simply removed, irrespective of sign.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150816				0	hr	\<item type=\"literal\"\>TRUNC(number; 0)\</item\> behaves as \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(number)\</item\> for positive numbers, but effectively rounds towards zero for negative numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148548				0	hr	The \<emph\>visible\</emph\> decimal places of the result are specified in \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\"\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152555				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152569				0	hr	TRUNC(1.239; 2) returns 1.23. The 9 is lost.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7050080				0	hr	TRUNC(-1.234999; 3) returns -1.234. All the 9s are lost.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153601				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>LN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153601				0	hr	LN				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154974				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LN\"\>Returns the natural logarithm based on the constant e of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154993				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284				0	hr	LN(number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297				0	hr	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose natural logarithm is to be calculated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153852				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153866				0	hr	LN(3) returns the natural logarithm of 3 (approximately 1.0986).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5747245				0	hr	LN(EXP(321)) returns 321.				20181231 09:50:43
