helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158247				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>MOD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>remainders of divisions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158247				0	hr	MOD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158276				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_REST\"\>Returns the remainder when one integer is divided by another.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158294				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158308				0	hr	MOD(Dividend; Divisor)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158321				0	hr	 For integer arguments this function returns \<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> modulo \<emph\>Divisor\</emph\>, that is the remainder when \<emph\>Dividend\</emph\> is divided by \<emph\>Divisor\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158341				0	hr	This function is implemented as \<item type=\"literal\"\>Dividend - Divisor * INT(Dividend / Divisor)\</item\> , and this formula gives the result if the arguments are not integer.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158361				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158374				0	hr	MOD(22; 3) returns 1, the remainder when 22 is divided by 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1278420				0	hr	MOD(11.25; 2.5) returns 1.25.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144592				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>QUOTIENT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>divisions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144592				0	hr	QUOTIENT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144627				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_QUOTIENT\"\>Returns the integer part of a division operation.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144646				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144659				0	hr	QUOTIENT(Numerator;Denominator)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9038972				0	hr	Returns the integer part of \<emph\>numerator\</emph\> divided by \<emph\>denominator\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7985168				0	hr	QUOTIENT is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(numerator/denominator)\</item\>, except that it may report errors with different error codes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144674				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144687				0	hr	=QUOTIENT(11;3) vraća 3. Ostatak od 2 je preskočen				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144702				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>RADIANS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;degrees, into radians\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144702				0	hr	RADIANS				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158025				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RAD\"\>Converts degrees to radians.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158042				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158055				0	hr	RADIANS(number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158069				0	hr	\<emph\>number\</emph\> is the angle in degrees to be converted to radians.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id876186				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3939634				0	hr	RADIANS(90) returns 1.5707963267949, which is PI/2 to Calc's accuracy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158121				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>ROUND function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158121				0	hr	ROUND				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158150				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number to a certain number of decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158169				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158182				0	hr	ROUND(number; count)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158196				0	hr	Returns \<emph\>number\</emph\> rounded to \<emph\>count\</emph\> decimal places. If \<emph\>count\</emph\> is omitted or zero, the function rounds to the nearest integer. If \<emph\>count\</emph\> is negative, the function rounds to the nearest 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	hr	This function rounds to the nearest number. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUNDUP for alternatives.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145863				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145876				0	hr	ROUND(2.348; 2) returns 2.35				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145899				0	hr	Ako unesete broj -32.483 u \<emph\>brojcano\</emph\> polje, sa  brojkom 3 odredjenom kao broj zaukruznih mjesta, -32.48 ce biti  vraceno kao rezultat. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1371501				0	hr	ROUND(2.348; 0) returns 2.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id4661702				0	hr	ROUND(2.5) returns 3. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7868892				0	hr	ROUND(987.65; -2) returns 1000.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145991				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDDOWN function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145991				0	hr	ROUNDDOWN				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, toward zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146037				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051				0	hr	ROUNDDOWN(number; count)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146064				0	hr	Returns \<emph\>number\</emph\> rounded down (towards zero) to \<emph\>count\</emph\> decimal places. If \<emph\>count\</emph\> is omitted or zero, the function rounds down to an integer. If \<emph\>count\</emph\> is negative, the function rounds down to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	hr	This function rounds towards zero. See ROUNDUP and ROUND for alternatives.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163164				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163178				0	hr	ROUNDDOWN(1.234; 2) returns 1.23.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5833307				0	hr	ROUNDDOWN(45.67; 0) returns 45.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7726676				0	hr	ROUNDDOWN(-45.67) returns -45.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3729361				0	hr	ROUNDDOWN(987.65; -2) returns 900.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163268				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>ROUNDUP function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163268				0	hr	ROUNDUP				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163297				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_AUFRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number up, away from zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163315				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163328				0	hr	ROUNDUP(number; count)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163342				0	hr	Returns \<emph\>number\</emph\> rounded up (away from zero) to \<emph\>count\</emph\> decimal places. If \<emph\>count\</emph\> is omitted or zero, the function rounds up to an integer. If \<emph\>count\</emph\> is negative, the function rounds up to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9573961				0	hr	This function rounds away from zero. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUND for alternatives.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163381				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144786				0	hr	ROUNDUP(1.1111; 2) returns 1.12.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7700430				0	hr	ROUNDUP(1.2345; 1) returns 1.3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1180455				0	hr	ROUNDUP(45.67; 0) returns 46.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3405560				0	hr	ROUNDUP(-45.67) returns -46.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3409527				0	hr	ROUNDUP(987.65; -2) returns 1000.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3144877				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SIN function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144877				0	hr	SIN				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144906				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SIN\"\>Returns the sine of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144923				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144937				0	hr	SIN(number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144950				0	hr	Returns the (trigonometric) sine of \<emph\>number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8079470				0	hr	To return the sine of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144969				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144983				0	hr	SIN(PI()/2) returns 1, the sine of PI/2 radians.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3916440				0	hr	SIN(RADIANS(30)) returns 0.5, the sine of 30 degrees.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163397				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SINH function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163397				0	hr	SINH				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163426				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SINHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic sine of a number.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163444				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163457				0	hr	SINH(number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163471				0	hr	Returns the hyperbolic sine of\<emph\>number\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163491				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163504				0	hr	SINH(0) returns 0, the hyperbolic sine of 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3163596				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SUM function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;numbers in cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163596				0	hr	SUM				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163625				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMME\"\>Adds all the numbers in a range of cells.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163643				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163656				0	hr	SUM(number1; number 2; ...; number 30)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163671				0	hr	\<emph\>Number 1 to number 30\</emph\> are up to 30 arguments whose sum is to be calculated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163690				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163704				0	hr	If you enter the numbers 2; 3 and 4 in the Number 1; 2 and 3 text boxes, 9 will be returned as the result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151740				0	hr	SUM(A1;A3;B5) calculates the sum of the three cells. SUM (A1:E10) calculates the sum of all cells in the A1 to E10 cell range.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151756				0	hr	Conditions linked by AND can be used with the function SUM() in the following manner:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151774				0	hr	Example assumption: You have entered invoices into a table. Column A contains the date value of the invoice, column B the amounts. You want to find a formula that you can use to return the total of all amounts only for a specific month, e.g. only the amount for the period >=1.1.99 to <1.2.99. The range with the date values covers A1:A40, the range containing the amounts to be totaled is B1:B40. C1 contains the start date, 1.1.99, of the invoices to be included and C2 the date, 1.2.99, that is no longer included.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151799				0	hr	Enter the following formula as an array formula:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151813				0	hr	=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151828				0	hr	In order to enter this as an array formula, you must press the Shift \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>+ Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> + Enter key instead of simply pressing the Enter key to close the formula. The formula will then be shown in the \<emph\>Formula\</emph\> bar enclosed in braces.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151869				0	hr	{=SUM((A1:A40>=C1)*(A1:A40<C2)*B1:B40)}				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151884				0	hr	The formula is based on the fact that the result of a comparison is 1, if the criterion is met and 0 if it is not. The individual comparison results will be treated as an array and used in matrix multiplication, and at the end the individual values will be totaled to give the result matrix.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;specified numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957				0	hr	SUMIF				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWENN\"\>Adds the cells specified by a given criteria.\</ahelp\> This function is used to browse a range when you search for a certain value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028				0	hr	SUMIF(range; criteria; sum_range)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043				0	hr	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062				0	hr	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> is the cell in which the search criterion is shown, or the search criterion itself. If the criteria is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083				0	hr	\<emph\>Sum_range\</emph\> is the range from which values are summed. If this parameter has not been indicated, the values found in the \<emph\>Range\</emph\> are summed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8347422				0	hr	SUMIF supports the reference concatenation operator (~) only in the Criteria parameter, and only if the optional SumRange parameter is not given.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148				0	hr	Za zbrajanje samo negativnih brojeva: SUMIF(A1:A10;"<0")				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	hr	=SUMIF(A1:A10;">0";B1:10) - sums values from the range B1:B10 only if the corresponding values in the range A1:A10 are >0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	hr	See COUNTIF() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIF().				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151957K				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SUMIFS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;specified numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151957K				0	hr	SUMIFS				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3151986K				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_SUMMEWNRNG\"\>Sum the values of cells in a range that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\> 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152015K				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152028K				0	hr	SUMIFS( Reference R ; Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152043K				0	hr	Sums the value of cells in range R that meet the Criterion C1 in the reference range R1, and the Criterion C2 in the reference range R2, and so on. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152062K				0	hr	A \<emph\>Criterion\</emph\> is a single cell Reference, Number or Text. If the criterion is written into the formula, it has to be surrounded by double quotes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152083K				0	hr	All \<emph\>Reference\</emph\> ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152110K				0	hr	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152148K				0	hr	Sum up cells in range A1:10 if the entires in B1:B10 are positive, and the entries in D1:D10 are the letter "A": \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIFS(A1:A10;B1:B10;">0";D1:D10;"A")\</item\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196K				0	hr	See COUNTIFS() for some more syntax examples that can be used with SUMIFS().				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152195				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>TAN function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152195				0	hr	TAN				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152224				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TAN\"\>Returns the tangent of the given angle (in radians).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152242				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152255				0	hr	TAN(number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152269				0	hr	Returns the (trigonometric) tangent of \<emph\>number\</emph\>, the angle in radians.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5752128				0	hr	To return the tangent of an angle in degrees, use the RADIANS function.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152287				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152301				0	hr	TAN(PI()/4) returns 1, the tangent of PI/4 radians.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1804864				0	hr	TAN(RADIANS(45)) returns 1, the tangent of 45 degrees.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3165434				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>TANH function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165434				0	hr	TANH				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165462				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TANHYP\"\>Returns the hyperbolic tangent of a number.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165480				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165494				0	hr	TANH(number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165508				0	hr	Returns the hyperbolic tangent of \<emph\>number\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165527				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165541				0	hr	TANH(0) returns 0, the hyperbolic tangent of 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3165633				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function; subtotals\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sums;of filtered data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>filtered data; sums\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>SUBTOTAL function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165633				0	hr	SUBTOTAL				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165682				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_TEILERGEBNIS\"\>Calculates subtotals.\</ahelp\> If a range already contains subtotals, these are not used for further calculations. Use this function with the AutoFilters to take only the filtered records into account.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165704				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165717				0	hr	SUBTOTAL(function; range)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165731				0	hr	\<emph\>Function\</emph\> is a number that stands for one of the following functions:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165782				0	hr	Function index				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165806				0	hr	Funkcija				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165833				0	hr	1				20181231 09:50:43
