helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143606				0	hr	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range whose cells are included.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143625				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143638				0	hr	You have a table in the cell range A1:B5 containing cities in column A and accompanying figures in column B. You have used an AutoFilter so that you only see rows containing the city Hamburg. You want to see the sum of the figures that are displayed; that is, just the subtotal for the filtered rows. In this case the correct formula would be:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143658				0	hr	=SUBTOTAL(9; B2:B5)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143672				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>Euro; converting in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>CONVERT function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143672				0	hr	CONVERT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143708				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UMRECHNEN\"\>Converts old European national currency to and from Euros.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143731				0	hr	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143748				0	hr	CONVERT(value;"currency1"; "currency2")				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143763				0	hr	\<emph\>value\</emph\> is the amount of the currency to be converted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143782				0	hr	\<emph\>currency1\</emph\> and \<emph\>currency2\</emph\> are the currency units to convert from and to respectively. These must be text, the official abbreviation for the currency (for example, "EUR"), as shown in the table below. The rates (shown per Euro) were set by the European Commission.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200904301810				0	hr	\<emph\>Full_precision\</emph\> is optional. If omitted or False, the result is rounded according to the decimals of the To currency. If Full_precision is True, the result is not rounded.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200904301815				0	hr	\<emph\>Triangulation_precision\</emph\> is optional. If Triangulation_precision is given and >=3, the intermediate result of a triangular conversion (currency1,EUR,currency2) is rounded to that precision. If Triangulation_precision is omitted, the intermediate result is not rounded. Also if To currency is "EUR", Triangulation_precision is used as if triangulation was needed and conversion from EUR to EUR was applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143819				0	hr	\<emph\>Examples:\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143837				0	hr	=CONVERT(100;"ATS";"EUR") converts 100 Austrian Schillings into Euros.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3143853				0	hr	=CONVERT(100;"EUR";"DEM") converts 100 Euros into German Marks.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id0908200902090676				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>CONVERT function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902074836				0	hr	CONVERT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200902131122				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Converts a value from one unit of measurement to another unit of measurement. The conversion factors are given in a list in the configuration.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200902475420				0	hr	At one time the list of conversion factors included the legacy European currencies and the Euro (see examples below). We suggest using the new function EUROCONVERT for converting these currencies.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902131071				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200902131191				0	hr	CONVERT(value;"text";"text")				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200902131152				0	hr	Example				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090213112				0	hr	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CONVERT(100;"ATS";"EUR")\</item\> returns the Euro value of 100 Austrian Schillings.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200902475431				0	hr	=CONVERT(100;"EUR";"DEM") converts 100 Euros into German Marks. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157177				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>ODD function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;up/down to nearest odd integer\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157177				0	hr	NEPARNO				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157205				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UNGERADE\"\>Rounds a positive number up to the nearest odd integer and a negative number down to the nearest odd integer.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157223				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157237				0	hr	ODD(broj)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157250				0	hr	 Returns \<emph\>number\</emph\> rounded to the next odd integer up, away from zero.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157270				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157283				0	hr	ODD(1.2) returns 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id8746910				0	hr	ODD(1) returns 1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9636524				0	hr	ODD(0) returns 1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5675527				0	hr	ODD(-3.1) returns -5.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157404				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>FLOOR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;down to nearest multiple of significance\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157404				0	hr	POD				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157432				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_UNTERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number down to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157451				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157464				0	hr	FLOOR(broj; značajnost; način)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157478				0	hr	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded down.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157497				0	hr	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the value to whose multiple the number is to be rounded down.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157517				0	hr	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> value is given and not equal to zero, and if \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of the number. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163894				0	hr	If both parameters \<emph\>Number\</emph\> and \<emph\>Significance\</emph\> are negative, and if the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> value is equal to zero or is not specified, then the results in $[officename] Calc and Excel will differ after exporting. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163932				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163945				0	hr	=FLOOR( -11; -2) returns -12				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163966				0	hr	=FLOOR( -11; -2; 0) returns -12				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163988				0	hr	=FLOOR( -11; -2; 1) returns -10				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164086				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SIGN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>algebraic signs\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164086				0	hr	SIGN				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164115				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VORZEICHEN\"\>Returns the sign of a number. Returns 1 if the number is positive, -1 if negative and 0 if zero.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164136				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164150				0	hr	SIGN(number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164164				0	hr	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number whose sign is to be determined.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164183				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164197				0	hr	SIGN(3.4) returns 1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164212				0	hr	SIGN(-4.5) returns -1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164252				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>MROUND function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>nearest multiple\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164252				0	hr	MROUND				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164288				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_MROUND\"\>Returns a number rounded to the nearest multiple of another number.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164306				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164320				0	hr	MROUND(Number; Multiple)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3486434				0	hr	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to the nearest multiple of \<emph\>Multiple\</emph\>. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3068636				0	hr	An alternative implementation would be \<item type=\"literal\"\>Multiple * ROUND(Number/Multiple)\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164333				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164347				0	hr	MROUND(15.5; 3) returns 15, as 15.5 is closer to 15 ( = 3*5) than to 18 ( = 3*6).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_idN14DD6				0	hr	MROUND(1.4; 0.5) returns 1.5 ( = 0.5*3).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164375				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SQRT function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square roots;positive numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164375				0	hr	SQRT				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164404				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WURZEL\"\>Returns the positive square root of a number.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164424				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164437				0	hr	SQRT(number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164451				0	hr	Returns the positive square root of \<emph\>number\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6870021				0	hr	\<emph\>number\</emph\> must be positive.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164471				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164484				0	hr	SQRT(16) returns 4.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3591723				0	hr	SQRT(-16) returns an \<item type=\"literal\"\>invalid argument\</item\> error.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164560				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>SQRTPI function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>square roots;products of Pi\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
