helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164596				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_SQRTPI\"\>Returns the square root of (PI times a number).\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164614				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164627				0	hr	SQRTPI(Number)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1501510				0	hr	Returns the positive square root of (PI multiplied by \<emph\>number\</emph\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9929197				0	hr	This is equivalent to \<item type=\"literal\"\>SQRT(PI()*number)\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164641				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164654				0	hr	SQRTPI(2) returns the squareroot of (2PI), approximately 2.506628.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164669				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>random numbers; between limits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>RANDBETWEEN function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164669				0	hr	RANDBETWEEN				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164711				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_RANDBETWEEN\"\>Returns an integer random number in a specified range.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164745				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164758				0	hr	RANDBETWEEN(Bottom; Top)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7112338				0	hr	Returns an integer random number between integers \<emph\>bottom\</emph\> and \<emph\>top\</emph\> (both inclusive).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2855616				0	hr	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+Ctrl+F9.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2091433				0	hr	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells containing this function, and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<emph\>Paste All\</emph\> and \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> not marked and \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> marked).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164772				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164785				0	hr	=RANDBETWEEN(20;30) returns an integer of between 20 and 30.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164800				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>RAND function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>random numbers;between 0 and 1\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164800				0	hr	RAND				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164829				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZUFALLSZAHL\"\>Returns a random number between 0 and 1.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164870				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164884				0	hr	RAND()				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5092318				0	hr	This function produces a new random number each time Calc recalculates. To force Calc to recalculate manually press Shift+Ctrl+F9.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9312417				0	hr	To generate random numbers which never recalculate, copy cells each containing =RAND(), and use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste Special\</item\> (with \<emph\>Paste All\</emph\> and \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> not marked and \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> marked).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id9089022				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id9569078				0	hr	RAND() returns a random number between 0 and 1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIF function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;specified cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897				0	hr	COUNTIF				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWENN\"\>Returns the number of cells that meet with certain criteria within a cell range.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953				0	hr	Syntax:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967				0	hr	COUNTIF(range; criteria)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980				0	hr	\<emph\>Range\</emph\> is the range to which the criteria are to be applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000				0	hr	\<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. "b.*" for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037				0	hr	Primjer:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505				0	hr	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers 2000 to 2009. Cell B1 contains the number 2006. In cell B2, you enter a formula:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652				0	hr	=COUNTIF(A1:A10;2006) - this returns 1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id708639				0	hr	=COUNTIF(A1:A10;B1) - this returns 1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	hr	=COUNTIF(A1:A10;">=2006") - this returns 3				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	hr	=COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<"&B1) - when B1 contains 2006, this returns 6				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id166020				0	hr	=COUNTIF(A1:A10;C2) where cell C2 contains the text ">2006" (without the double quotes) - counts the number of cells in the range A1:A10 which are > 2006 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	hr	To count only negative numbers: COUNTIF(A1:A10;"<0")				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3164897K				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>COUNTIFS function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting;specified cells\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164897K				0	hr	COUNTIFS				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164926K				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZAEHLENWNRNG\"\>Count the number of cells that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3164953K				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164967K				0	hr	COUNTIFS( Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3164980K				0	hr	\<emph\>Reference R1\</emph\> is the  range to which the \<emph\>Criterion C1\</emph\>applies. \<emph\>Reference R2\</emph\> is the  range to which the \<emph\>Criterion C2\</emph\>applies, and so on.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3165000K				0	hr	All \<emph\>Reference \</emph\> ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned. \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> indicates the criteria in the form of a number, an expression or a character string. These criteria determine which cells are counted. You may also enter a search text in the form of a regular expression, e.g. b.* for all words that begin with b. You may also indicate a cell range that contains the search criterion. If you search for literal text, enclose the text in double quotes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3165037K				0	hr	Examples:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3166505K				0	hr	A1:A10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2009\</item\>. B1:B10 is a cell range containing the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>2007\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>2016\</item\>:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3581652K				0	hr	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIFS(A1:A10;2006;B1:B10;2014)\</item\> - this returns 2				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225K				0	hr	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COUNTIFS(A1:A10;">=2006";B1:B10;">=2006") \</item\>- this returns 14				20181231 09:50:43
