helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145166				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>DECIMAL function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145166				0	hr	DECIMAL				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3156361				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DEZIMAL\"\>Converts text with characters from a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#zahlensystem\" name=\"number system\"\>number system\</link\> to a positive integer in the base radix given.\</ahelp\> The radix must be in the range 2 to 36. Spaces and tabs are ignored. The\<emph\> text\</emph\> field is not case-sensitive.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3157994				0	hr	If the radix is 16, a leading x or X or 0x or 0X, and an appended h or H, is disregarded. If the radix is 2, an appended b or B is disregarded. Other characters that do not belong to the number system generate an error.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150014				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3154328				0	hr	DECIMAL(Text; Radix)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3150128	230			0	hr	\<emph\>text\</emph\> is the text to be converted. To differentiate between a hexadecimal number, such as A1 and the reference to cell A1, you must place the number in quotation marks, for example, "A1" or "FACE".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145241	231			0	hr	\<emph\>radix\</emph\> indicates the base of the number system. It may be any positive integer between 2 and 36.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156062				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3145355	233			0	hr	DECIMAL("17";10) returns 17.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3155622	234			0	hr	DECIMAL("FACE";16) returns 64206.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151015	235			0	hr	DECIMAL("0101";2) vraca 5. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148402				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>DOLLAR function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148402				0	hr	DOLLAR				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3153049	12			0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DM\"\>Converts a number to an amount in the currency format, rounded to a specified decimal place.\</ahelp\> In the \<emph\>value\</emph\> field enter the number to be converted to currency. Optionally, you may enter the number of decimal places in the \<emph\>decimals\</emph\> field. If no value is specified, all numbers in currency format will be displayed with two decimal places. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151280				0	hr	You set the currency format in your system settings.				20181231 09:50:43
