helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3158002				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_ODDLYIELD\"\>Calculates the yield of a security if the last interest date falls irregularly.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147366				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150018				0	hr	ODDLYIELD(Settlement;Maturity;Last interest;Rate;Price;Redemption;Frequency;Basis)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3159132				0	hr	Settlement: the date of purchase of the security.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150134				0	hr	Maturity: the date on which the security matures (expires).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	hr	Last interest: the last interest date of the security.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151014				0	hr	Rate: the annual rate of interest.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149003				0	hr	Price: the price of the security.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148880				0	hr	Redemption: the redemption value per 100 currency units of par value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155622				0	hr	Frequency: number of interest payments per year (1, 2 or 4).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145303				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145350				0	hr	Settlement date: April 20 1999, maturity date: June 15 1999, last interest: October 15 1998. Interest rate: 3.75 per cent, price: 99.875 currency units, redemption value: 100 currency units, frequency of payments: half-yearly = 2, basis: = 0				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3157990				0	hr	The yield of the security, that has an irregular last interest date, is calculated as follows:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150572				0	hr	=ODDLYIELD("4/20/1999";"6/15/1999"; "10/15/1998"; 0.0375; 99.875;  100;2;0) vraca 0.044873 or 4.4873%. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148768				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variable declining depreciations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>depreciations;variable declining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>VDB function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768				0	hr	VDB				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154636				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_VDB\"\>Returns the depreciation of an asset for a specified or partial period using a variable declining balance method.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155519				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149025				0	hr	VDB(Cost;Salvage;Life;S;End;Factor;Type)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150692				0	hr	Cost: the initial value of an asset.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155369				0	hr	Salvage: the value of an asset at the end of the depreciation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154954				0	hr	Life: the depreciation duration of the asset.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3152817				0	hr	S: the start of the depreciation. A must be entered in the same date unit as the duration.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153221				0	hr	End: the end of the depreciation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3147536				0	hr	Factor (optional): the depreciation factor. Factor=2 is double rate depreciation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3154865	232			0	hr	Tip (opcionalno): Tip = 1 znači prebacivanje na linearnu deprecijaciju. Pri tip = 0 ne radi se prebacivanje.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A0D				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148429				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153927				0	hr	What is the declining-balance double-rate depreciation for a period if the initial cost is 35,000 currency units and the value at the end of the depreciation is 7,500 currency units. The depreciation period is 3 years. The depreciation from the 10th to the 20th period is calculated.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155991				0	hr	VDB(35000;7500;36;10;20;2) = 8603.80 currency units. The depreciation during the period between the 10th and the 20th period is 8,603.80 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147485				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;internal rates of return, irregular payments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>internal rates of return;irregular payments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>XIRR function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147485				0	hr	XIRR				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_XIRR\"\>Calculates the internal rate of return for a list of payments which take place on different dates.\</ahelp\> The calculation is based on a 365 days per year basis, ignoring leap years.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E62				0	hr	If the payments take place at regular intervals, use the IRR function.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146149				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149826				0	hr	XIRR(Values;Dates;Guess)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3163821				0	hr	Values and dates: a series of payments and the series of associated date values. The first pair of dates defines the start of the payment plan. All other date values must be later, but need not be in any order. The series of values must contain at least one negative and one positive value (receipts and deposits).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149708				0	hr	Guess (optional): a guess can be input for the internal rate of return. The default is 10%.				20181231 09:50:43
