helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3151052				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ZINS\"\>Returns the constant interest rate per period of an annuity.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154272				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3158423				0	hr	RATE(NPER;PMT;PV;FV;Type;GUESS)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148910				0	hr	NPER: the total number of periods, during which payments are made (payment period).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148925				0	hr	PMT: the constant payment (annuity) paid during each period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149160				0	hr	PV: the cash value in the sequence of payments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3166456				0	hr	FV (optional): the future value, which is reached at the end of the periodic payments.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3153243				0	hr	Type (optional): the due date of the periodic payment, either at the beginning or at the end of a period.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	hr	GUESS (optional): determines the estimated value of the interest with iterative calculation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_idN10E2A				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149791				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3150706				0	hr	What is the constant interest rate for a payment period of 3 periods if 10 currency units are paid regularly and the present cash value is 900 currency units.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	hr	RATE(3;10;900) = -121% The interest rate is therefore 121%.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149106				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>INTRATE function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149106				0	hr	INTRATE				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149918				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_INTRATE\"\>Calculates the annual interest rate that results when a security (or other item) is purchased at an investment value and sold at a redemption value. No interest is paid.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149974				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3149800				0	hr	INTRATE(Settlement;Maturity;Investment;Redemption;Basis)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148618				0	hr	Settlement: the date of purchase of the security.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060118.xhp	0	help	par_id3148988				0	hr	Maturity: the date on which the security is sold.				20181231 09:50:43
