helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148394				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>OR function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148394				0	hr	ILI				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns TRUE if at least one argument is TRUE.\</ahelp\> This function returns the value FALSE, if all the arguments have the logical value FALSE.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771				0	hr	The arguments are either logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3) containing logical values.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3153546				0	hr	When a function expects a single value, but you entered a cell range, then the value from the cell range is taken that is in the same column or row as the formula.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027				0	hr	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468				0	hr	OR(Logical value 1; Logical value 2 ...Logical value 30)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819	24			0	hr	\<emph\>Logical value 1; Logical value 2 ...Logical value 30\</emph\> are conditions to be checked. All conditions can be either TRUE or FALSE. If a range is entered as a parameter, the function uses the value from the range that is in the current column or row.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228				0	hr	Examples:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3154870				0	hr	The logical values of entries 12<11; 13>22, and 45=45 are to be checked.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371	27			0	hr	OR(12<11; 13>22; 45=45) returns TRUE.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412	59			0	hr	OR(FALSE;TRUE) returns TRUE.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148394K				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>XOR function\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148394K				0	hr	XOR				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060K				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ODER\"\>Returns the exclusive "or" of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3148771K				0	hr	The arguments are either numbers, logical expressions themselves (TRUE, 1<5, 2+3=7, B8<10) that return logical values, or arrays (A1:C3).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3149027K				0	hr	If the entered range is outside of the current column or row of the formula, the function returns the error value #VALUE!				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155517K				0	hr	Syntax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3150468K				0	hr	XOR(Value1; Value2 ...Value30)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155819K				0	hr	\<emph\>Value1; Value2 ...Value30\</emph\> are added modulo 2. TRUE is returned if the result of this addition is 1;FALSE is returned if the result of this addition is 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153228K				0	hr	Examples:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3155371K				0	hr	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XOR(12<11;13>22;10)\</item\> returns TRUE since this converts to (1+0+10) mod 2 = 0				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060105.xhp	0	help	par_id3158412K				0	hr	\<item type=\"input\"\>=XOR(FALSE;TRUE)\</item\> returns TRUE.				20181231 09:50:43
