helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3154729\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleobjectrotatemode.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154729\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3150716				0	hr	Select the object you want to rotate. On the \<emph\>Mode\</emph\> toolbar in $[officename] Draw or on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar in $[officename] Impress, click the \<emph\>Rotate\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	hr	Move the pointer to a corner handle so that the pointer changes to a rotate symbol. Drag the handle to rotate the object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id0930200803002335				0	hr	Hold down the Shift key to restrict the rotation to multiples of 15 degrees.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id0930200803002463				0	hr	Right-click the object to open the context menu. Choose Position and Size - Rotation to enter an exact rotation value.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3154023\" src=\"res/helpimg/rotate.png\" width=\"5.424cm\" height=\"3.916cm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154023\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3166424				0	hr	To change the pivot point, drag the small circle in the center of the object to a new location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\rotate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	hr	To skew the object vertically or horizontally, drag one of the side handles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Umnožavanje objekata				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145750				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>doubling draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; duplicating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>duplicating draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multiplying draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145750				0	hr	\<variable id=\"duplicate_object\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/duplicate_object.xhp\" name=\"Duplicating Objects\"\>Duplicating Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	hr	You can create duplicate or multiple copies of an object. The copies can be identical or can differ in size, color, orientation and location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	hr	The following example creates a stack of coins by making multiple copies of a single ellipse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129				0	hr	Use the \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> tool to draw a solid yellow ellipse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149209				0	hr	Select the ellipse and choose \<emph\>Edit - Duplicate\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3145585	9			0	hr	Enter 12 as \<emph\>Number of copies.\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151192				0	hr	Enter a negative value for the \<emph\>Width\</emph\> and \<emph\>Height\</emph\> so that the coins decrease in size as you go up the stack.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387				0	hr	To define a color transition for the coins, select different colors in the \<emph\>Start\</emph\> and \<emph\>End\</emph\> boxes. The \<emph\>Start\</emph\> color is applied to the object that you are duplicating.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to create the duplicates.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\duplicate_object.xhp	0	help	par_id3153935				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/02120000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Duplicate\"\>Edit - Duplicate\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156443				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>combining; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>merging; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>connecting; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; combining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>intersecting draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>polygons; intersecting/subtracting/merging\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subtracting polygons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>constructing shapes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443	64			0	hr	\<variable id=\"combine_etc\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/combine_etc.xhp\" name=\"Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes\"\>Combining Objects and Constructing Shapes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020	65			0	hr	Combined drawing objects act as grouped objects, except that you cannot enter the group to edit the individual objects. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154659				0	hr	You can only combine 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	hr	To combine 2D objects:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	hr	Select two or more 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Modify - Combine\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	hr	Unlike groups, a combined object takes on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order. You can split apart combined objects, but the original object properties are lost.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3155088				0	hr	When you combine objects, holes appear where the objects overlap.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3157978\" src=\"res/helpimg/kombi1.png\" width=\"212.46mm\" height=\"63.5mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3157978\"\>Illustration for combining objects\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153249				0	hr	In the illustration, the uncombined objects are on the left and the combined objects on the right.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159229				0	hr	Constructing Shapes				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150049				0	hr	You can construct shapes by applying the \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13180000.xhp\" name=\"Shapes\"\>\<emph\>Shapes\</emph\>\</link\>\<emph\>- Merge, Subtract and Intersect\</emph\> commands to two or more drawing objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147403				0	hr	Shape commands only work on 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150539				0	hr	Constructed shapes take on the properties of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156402				0	hr	To construct a shape:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3157874				0	hr	Select two or more 2D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150650				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Modify - Shapes\</emph\> and one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3145829	91			0	hr	\<emph\>Merge\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3154680	92			0	hr	\<emph\>Subtract\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153034				0	hr	\<emph\>Intersect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145144				0	hr	Shape Commands				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	hr	In the following illustrations, the original objects are on the left and the modified shapes on the right.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149950				0	hr	Shapes - Merge				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3148585				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3145593\" src=\"res/helpimg/formvers.png\" width=\"88.37mm\" height=\"33.34mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145593\"\>Illustration for merging shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150001				0	hr	Adds the area of the selected objects to the area of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153002				0	hr	Shapes - Subtract				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150338				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3154505\" src=\"res/helpimg/formsubt.png\" width=\"88.11mm\" height=\"33.34mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154505\"\>Illustration for subtracting shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150022				0	hr	Subtracts the area of the selected objects from the area of the lowermost object in the stacking order.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147370				0	hr	Shapes - Intersect				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150570				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3150658\" src=\"res/helpimg/formschn.png\" width=\"87.05mm\" height=\"33.07mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150658\"\>Illustratoin for intersecting shapes\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3157972				0	hr	The overlapping area of the selected objects creates the new shape.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\combine_etc.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	hr	The area outside the overlap is removed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Definiranje korisnickih boja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149263				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>colors; defining and saving\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined colors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom colors\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149263				0	hr	\<variable id=\"color_define\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/color_define.xhp\" name=\"Defining Custom Colors\"\>Defining Custom Colors\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154511				0	hr	If you want, you can mix a custom color and add it to a color table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155600				0	hr	To define a custom color				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Colors\</emph\> tab. A table of the predefined colors is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3154657				0	hr	Changes made to the standard color table are permanent and are saved automatically.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	hr	Click a color in the table that is similar to the one you want to mix. The color appears in the upper preview box to the right of the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	hr	Select the RGB or CMYK color model in the box below the preview boxes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id4979705				0	hr	%PRODUCTNAME uses only the RGB color model for printing in color. The CMYK controls are provided only to ease the input of color values using CMYK notation.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152987	16			0	hr	The RGB color model mixes red, green and blue light to create colors on a computer screen. In the RGB model, the three color components are additive and can have values ranging from 0 (black) to 255 (white). The CMYK color model combines Cyan (C), Magenta (M), Yellow (Y), and blacK (K, also used for "Key") to create colors for printing. The four colors of the CMYK models are subtractive and are defined as percentages. Black corresponds to 100 % and white to 0 %.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145386				0	hr	Enter a numeric value in the boxes next to the color components. The new color appears in the preview box directly above the color model box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3152871				0	hr	You can also create a color using a color spectrum. Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button to open the \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010501.xhp\" name=\"Color\"\>\<emph\>Color\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. Click a color and click OK. Use the Hue, Saturation, and Brightness boxes to adjust your color selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011				0	hr	Učinite nešto od navedenog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3147244				0	hr	If you want to replace the color in the standard color table that your custom color is based on, click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	hr	If you want to add your custom color to the standard color table, enter a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> text box and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\color_define.xhp	0	help	par_id3145236				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/03170000.xhp\" name=\"Color bar\"\>Color bar\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Cross-Fading Two Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150715				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; cross-fading two objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-fading; two draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	hr	\<variable id=\"cross_fading\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/cross_fading.xhp\" name=\"Cross-Fading Two Objects\"\>Cross-Fading Two Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	hr	Cross-fading creates shapes and distributes them by uniform increments between two drawing objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155112				0	hr	The cross-fading command is only available in $[officename] Draw. You can, however, copy and paste cross-faded objects into $[officename] Impress.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149209				0	hr	To cross-fade two objects:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	hr	Hold down Shift and click each object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Cross-fading\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	hr	Enter a value to specify the number of objects between the start and end of the cross-fade in the \<emph\>Increments\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3149405				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3151240				0	hr	A group containing the two original objects and the specified number (increments) of cross-faded objects is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3159203				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3150210\" src=\"res/helpimg/ueberblenden.png\" width=\"74.88mm\" height=\"65.62mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150210\"\>Illustration for crossfading\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3154766				0	hr	You can edit the individual objects of a group by selecting the group and pressing F3. Press Ctrl+F3 to exit the group editing mode.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\cross_fading.xhp	0	help	par_id3155760				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Editing - Cross-fading\"\>Editing - Cross-fading\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149656				0	hr	\<variable id=\"align_arrange\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/align_arrange.xhp\" name=\"Arranging and Aligning Objects\"\>Arranging, Aligning and Distributing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	bm_id3125863				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>arranging; objects (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects;aligning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distributing draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>aligning;draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	hr	Arranging Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3153727				0	hr	Each object that you place in your document is successively stacked on the preceding object. To re-arrange the stacking order of a selected object proceed as follows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	hr	Click the object that you want to re-arrange.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to bring up the context menu and choose one of the arrange options:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E6				0	hr	\<emph\>Bring to Front\</emph\> places the object on top of all other objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EC				0	hr	\<emph\>Bring Forward\</emph\> places the object one place forward in the stack of objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F2				0	hr	\<emph\>Send Backward\</emph\> places the object one place back in the stack of objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	hr	\<emph\>Send to Back\</emph\> places the object behind all other objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FE				0	hr	\<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\> places the object behind another object that you select				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155766				0	hr	Arranging an Object Behind Another Object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN10811				0	hr	Click the object that you want to re-arrange.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Behind Object\</emph\>. The mouse pointer changes to a hand.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3149126				0	hr	Click the object behind which you want to arrange the selected object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145789				0	hr	Reversing The Stacking Order of Two Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	hr	Shift-click both objects to select them.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Arrange\</item\> to open the context menu and choose \<emph\>Reverse\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166425				0	hr	Aligning Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3152994				0	hr	The \<emph\>Alignment\</emph\> function enables you to align objects relative to each other or relative to the page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	hr	Select an object to align it to the page or select multiple objects to align them relative to each other.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A7				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Alignment\</item\> and select one of the alignment options.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	hr	Distributing Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3151390				0	hr	If you select three or more objects in Draw, you can also use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05360000.xhp\" name=\"Distribution\"\>\<emph\>Distribution\</emph\>\</link\> command to distribute the vertical and horizontal spacing evenly between the objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108CE				0	hr	Select three or more objects to be distributed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D2				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify - Distribution\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DA				0	hr	Select the horizontal and vertical distribution option and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\align_arrange.xhp	0	help	par_id3150535				0	hr	Selected objects are distributed evenly along the horizontal or vertical axis. The two outermost objects are used as reference points and do not move when the \<emph\>Distribution\</emph\> command is applied.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Grupiranje objekata				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>groups; entering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;group objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793				0	hr	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	hr	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	hr	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	hr	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	hr	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716				0	hr	To group objects:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346				0	hr	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	hr	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002				0	hr	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	hr	Selecting Objects in a Group				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450				0	hr	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"4.23mm\" height=\"4.23mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	hr	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Upute za koristenje $[officename] Crtanja 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>Draw instructions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>instructions; $[officename] Draw\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	hr	\<variable id=\"main\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/main.xhp\" name=\"Instructions for Using $[officename] Draw\"\>Instructions for Using $[officename] Draw\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143218				0	hr	Editing and Grouping Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149018				0	hr	Editing Colors and Textures				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	hr	Editing Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147003				0	hr	Working with Layers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145585				0	hr	Razno				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Zamjena boje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>eyedropper tool\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>colors; replacing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing;colors in bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>metafiles;replacing colors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps;replacing colors\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>GIF images;replacing colors\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	hr	\<variable id=\"eyedropper\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/eyedropper.xhp\" name=\"Replacing Colors\"\>Replacing Colors\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	hr	You can replace colors in bitmaps with the \<emph\>Eyedropper\</emph\> tool.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	hr	Up to four colors can be replaced at once.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	hr	You can also use the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> option to replace the transparent areas of an image with a color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	hr	Similarly, you can use the \<emph\>Eyedropper\</emph\> to make a color on your image transparent.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	hr	To replace colors with the Eyedropper tool				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	hr	Ensure that the image you are using is a bitmap (for example, BMP, GIF, JPG, or PNG) or a metafile (for example, WMF).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Eyedropper\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	hr	Click the Eyedropper icon and position the mouse pointer over the color you want to replace in the image. The color appears in the box next to the eyedropper icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	hr	Click the color in the image. The color appears in the first \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> box and the check box next to the color is selected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, select the new color.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	hr	This replaces all occurrences of the \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the image.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3151191				0	hr	If you want to replace another color while the dialog is open, select the check box in front of \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the next row and repeat steps 3 to 5.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3149876				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	hr	If you want to expand or contract the color selection area, increase or decrease the tolerance of the \<emph\>Eyedropper\</emph\> tool and repeat your selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3146878				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06030000.xhp\" name=\"Eyedropper\"\>Eyedropper\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155628				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; %PRODUCTNAME Draw\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; text entry mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text entry mode for draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155628				0	hr	\<variable id=\"keyboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/keyboard.xhp\" name=\"Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects\"\>Shortcut Keys for Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148663				0	hr	You can create and edit drawing objects using the keyboard.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	hr	To Create and Edit a Drawing Object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>F6\</item\> to navigate to the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	hr	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> arrow key until you reach the toolbar icon of a drawing tool.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CD				0	hr	If there is an arrow next to the icon, the drawing tool opens a sub toolbar. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Up\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Down\</item\> arrow key to open the sub toolbar, then press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Right\</item\> or \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Left\</item\> key to select an icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154705				0	hr	The object is created at the center of the current document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155962				0	hr	To return to the document, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+F6\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155062				0	hr	You can use the arrow keys to position the object where you want. To choose a command from the context menu for the object, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Shift+F10\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150306				0	hr	To Select an Object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+F6\</item\> to enter the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145587				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Tab\</item\> until you reach the object you want to select.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Crtanje Sektora i Segmenata 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146974				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>sectors of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>segments of circles/ellipses\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>circle segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ellipses; segments\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drawing; sectors and segments\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	hr	\<variable id=\"draw_sector\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/draw_sector.xhp\" name=\"Drawing Sectors and Segments\"\>Drawing Sectors and Segments\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	hr	The \<emph\>Ellipse\</emph\> toolbar contains tools for drawing ellipses and circles. You can also draw segments and sectors of circles and ellipses.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075				0	hr	To draw a sector of a circle or an ellipse:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335	33			0	hr	Open the \<emph\>Ellipses\</emph\> toolbar and click one of the \<emph\>Circle Pie\</emph\> or \<emph\>Ellipse Pie\</emph\> icons \<image id=\"img_id3155768\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_circlepie_unfilled.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155768\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>. The mouse pointer changes to a cross hair with a small icon of a sector.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3150199				0	hr	Position the pointer at the edge of the circle you want to draw and drag to create the circle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148868				0	hr	To create a circle by dragging from the center, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3145361				0	hr	Release the mouse button when the circle has reached the size you want. A line corresponding to the circle radius appears in the circle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	hr	Position the pointer where you want to place the first boundary of the sector and click.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	hr	As the radius line that follows the pointer is constrained to the circle boundaries, you can click anywhere in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3146874				0	hr	Position the pointer where you want to place the second boundary of the sector and click. The completed sector is displayed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3148581				0	hr	To draw a segment of a circle or ellipse, follow the steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\draw_sector.xhp	0	help	par_id3153084				0	hr	To draw an arc based on an ellipse, choose one of the arc icons and follow the same steps for creating a sector based on a circle.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Adding Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153144				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;text from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153144				0	hr	\<variable id=\"text_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/text_enter.xhp\" name=\"Adding Text\"\>Adding Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	46			0	hr	There are several types of text you can add to a drawing or presentation: 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	hr	Text in a text frame				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	hr	Text that changes character size to fill the frame size				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	hr	Text that is added to any drawing object by double-clicking the object				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10830				0	hr	Text that is copied from a Writer document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	hr	Text that is inserted from a text or HTML document				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202				0	hr	Adding a Text Frame				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052				0	hr	Drag a text frame to the size you want in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194				0	hr	Ispišite ili ubacite vaš tekst u tekstualni okvi.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118				0	hr	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text object to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437				0	hr	Fitting Text to Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877				0	hr	Create a text frame as described in the steps above. The size of the frame determines the size of the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	hr	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id0610200902133994				0	hr	Now you can resize the text box to change the size and shape of the text characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155955				0	hr	Text Tied to a Graphic				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10917				0	hr	You can add text to any graphic after double-clicking the graphic.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1827448				0	hr	To determine the position of the text, use the settings in \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147366	59			0	hr	For example, click the arrow next to the \<emph\>Callouts\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3154508\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_calloutshapes.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154508\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> to open the Callouts toolbar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FD				0	hr	Select a callout and move the mouse pointer to where you want the callout to start.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150272				0	hr	Drag to draw the callout.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1978514				0	hr	Enter the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091A				0	hr	Copying Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10921				0	hr	Select the text in your Writer document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10925				0	hr	Copy the text to the clipboard (\<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1092D				0	hr	Click the page or slide where you want to paste the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10931				0	hr	Paste the text using \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit - Paste special\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093C				0	hr	Using \<emph\>Paste special\</emph\>, you can choose the text format to be pasted. Depending on formats, you can copy different text attributes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1093F				0	hr	Importing Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10946				0	hr	Click the page or slide where you want to import the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1094A				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10952				0	hr	Select a text file (*.txt) or an HTML file and click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Insert Text\</emph\> dialog opens. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to insert the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Creating Gradient Fills				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>gradients; applying and defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparency;adjusting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	hr	\<variable id=\"gradient\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/gradient.xhp\" name=\"Creating Gradient Fills\"\>Creating Gradient Fills\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	hr	A gradient fill is an incremental blend of two different colors, or shades of the same color, that you can apply to a drawing object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	hr	To apply a gradient:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	hr	Select a drawing object.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\> as the \<emph\>Fill\</emph\> type.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	hr	Select a gradient style from the list and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702				0	hr	Creating Custom Gradients				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791				0	hr	You can define your own gradients and modify existing gradients, as well as save and load a list of gradient files.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384				0	hr	To create a custom gradient:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046				0	hr	Select a gradient from the list to use as the basis for your new gradient and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116				0	hr	Type a name for the gradient in the text box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id6535843				0	hr	The name appears at the end of the gradient list and is selected for editing.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391				0	hr	Set the gradient properties and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> to save the gradient.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396	16			0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK.\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149947				0	hr	Using Gradients and Transparency				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3157905				0	hr	You can adjust the properties of a gradient as well as the transparency of a drawing object with your mouse.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653				0	hr	To adjust the gradient of a drawing object:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844				0	hr	Select a drawing object with the gradient that you want to modify.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145592				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	hr	Adjust the values for the gradient to suit your needs and click \<emph\>Ok\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659				0	hr	To adjust the transparency of an object, select the object, choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
