helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	hr	Select the second 3D object (sphere) and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	hr	Double-click the first object (cube) to enter its group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>. Both objects are now part of the same group. If you want, you can edit the individual objects or change their position within the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	hr	Double-click outside the group to exit the group.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	hr	You cannot intersect or subtract 3D objects.				20181231 09:50:43
