helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153167				0	hr	If you want, you can use a condition to hide specific text in your document from a specific user.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190				0	hr	Select the text in the document that you want to hide.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3145297				0	hr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> area, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533	105			0	hr	In the \<emph\>With Condition\</emph\> box, type \<emph\>user_lastname == "Doe"\</emph\>, where "Doe" is the last name of the user that you want to hide the text from. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3155573				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then save the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields_userdata.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	hr	The name of the hidden section can still be seen in the Navigator.				20181231 09:50:43
