helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147682				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>outlines;numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;heading numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chapter numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings; numbering\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering;headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings; own paragraph styles\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147682				0	hr	\<variable id=\"chapter_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Outline Numbering\"\>Outline Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155605				0	hr	You can modify the heading hierarchy or assign a level in the hierarchy to a custom paragraph style. You can also add chapter and section numbering to heading paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading 1" paragraph style is at the top of the outline hierarchy.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155626				0	hr	To add automatic numbering to a heading style:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891				0	hr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paragraph Style\</item\> box, select the heading style that you want to add chapter numbers to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513				0	hr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> box, select the numbering style that you want to use, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CE				0	hr	To remove automatic outline numbering from a heading paragraph:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	hr	Click at the beginning of the text in the heading paragraph, after the number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D9				0	hr	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Backspace\</item\> key to delete the number.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155552				0	hr	To use a custom paragraph style as a heading:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155571				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147758				0	hr	Select the custom style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147782	39			0	hr	Click the heading level that you want to assign to the custom paragraph style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> list. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147808				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Defining Different Headers and Footers				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	hr	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	hr	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147105				0	hr	You can also use the mirrored page layout if you want to add a header to a page style that has different inner and outer page margins. To apply this option to a page style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page\</item\> tab, and in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Layout settings\</item\> area, choose “Mirrored” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page layout\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	hr	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	hr	Open a new text document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	hr	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	hr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	hr	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865				0	hr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Left Page".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748				0	hr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	hr	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147061				0	hr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Right Page".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263				0	hr	Double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles to apply the style to the current page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145284	43			0	hr	Enter text or graphics in the header for the Left Page style. After the next page is added to your document, enter text or graphics in the header for the Right Page style. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Using Captions 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147691				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>inserting; captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>captions; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adding;captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>objects; captioning\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text frames; labeling\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; inserting captions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>legends, see also captions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150537				0	hr	\<variable id=\"captions\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/captions.xhp\" name=\"Using Captions\"\>Using Captions\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153156				0	hr	In text documents, you can add continuously numbered captions to graphics, tables, frames, and drawing objects.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172				0	hr	You can edit the text and the number ranges for different types of captions.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153186				0	hr	When you add a caption to a picture or to an object, the object and the caption text are placed together in a new frame. When you add a caption to a table, the caption text is inserted as a paragraph next to the table. When you add a caption to a frame, the caption text is added to the text inside the frame, either before or after the existing text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	hr	To move both the object and the caption, drag the frame that contains these items. To update the caption numbering after you move the frame, press F9.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155541				0	hr	Defining Captions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155567				0	hr	Select the item that you want to add a caption to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Caption\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147765				0	hr	Select the options that you want, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>. If you want, you can also enter different text in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Category\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Figure\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147254				0	hr	You can edit caption text directly in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3147271				0	hr	A caption is formatted with the paragraph style that matches the name of the caption \<emph\>Category\</emph\>. For example, if you insert a "Table" caption, the "Table" paragraph style is applied to the caption text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145671				0	hr	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, frame, or table. Choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
