helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155911				0	hr	\<variable id=\"stylist_fromselect\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fromselect.xhp\" name=\"Creating New Styles From Selections\"\>Creating New Styles From Selections\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149829				0	hr	You can quickly create a new style from an existing style that you have applied manual formatting to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156097				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153402				0	hr	Click the icon of the style category that you want to create.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153119				0	hr	Click in the document where you want to copy the style from, for example, in a paragraph that you applied manual formatting to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153138				0	hr	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Style from Selection\</item\> icon and choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Style from Selection\</item\> from the submenu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fromselect.xhp	0	help	par_id3156260				0	hr	Type a name in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style Name\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
