helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Conditional Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619				0	hr	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text\"\>Conditional Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	hr	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	hr	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175				0	hr	To define a conditional variable:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	hr	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759				0	hr	Click "Set variable" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147784				0	hr	Type a name for the variable in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "Reminder".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	hr	Click "Text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	hr	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	hr	To define a condition and the conditional text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659				0	hr	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	hr	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert -\</emph\>\<emph\>Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	hr	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	hr	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	hr	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446				0	hr	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073				0	hr	To display the conditional text:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	hr	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	hr	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	hr	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box with 3, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	hr	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145714				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of conditional operators\"\>List of conditional operators\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Primjena stilova u način popunjavanja obrasca				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; styles, by fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>brush for copying styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; transferring\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145084				0	hr	\<variable id=\"stylist_fillformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fillformat.xhp\" name=\"Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\"\>Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	hr	You can quickly apply styles, such as paragraph and character styles, in your document by using the Fill Format Mode in the Styles and Formatting window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	hr	Click the icon of the style category that you want to apply.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	17			0	hr	Click the style, and then click the \<emph\>Fill Format Mode\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149644\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149644\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371				0	hr	Move the mouse pointer to where you want to apply the style in the document, and click. To apply the style to more than one item, drag to select the items, and then release.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	hr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> when finished.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159259				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;protecting/unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting;tables and sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id6007263				0	hr	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</item\>\</link\> \</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id1924802				0	hr	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150114				0	hr	Protecting Sections in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	hr	Any section of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text document can be protected against changes with a password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4545426				0	hr	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the section against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	hr	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	hr	Select the text. Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section - Section\</emph\>, then under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> mark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> and \<emph\>With password\</emph\> check boxes. (If the section already exists: \<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>.) Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	hr	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> clear the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146081				0	hr	Protecting Cells in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	hr	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	hr	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	hr	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	hr	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	hr	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	hr	Place the cursor in the cell or select the cells. First, if necessary, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>. Then right-click the cell to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Cell - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	hr	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	hr	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149259				0	hr	Automatic Protection of Indexes and Tables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	hr	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	hr	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidental changes.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767				0	hr	Turning on protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	hr	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3159088				0	hr	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, mark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	hr	Turning off protection				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	49			0	hr	Place the cursor in the index. First of all, if necessary, under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids \</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	hr	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	hr	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	hr	         \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>      				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id7858516				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/protection.xhp\"\>Protecting Other Contents\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Uredjivanje dijela				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149816				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>sections; editing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>read-only sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>protecting;sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting;sections, into normal text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;sections\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149816				0	hr	\<variable id=\"section_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_edit.xhp\" name=\"Editing Sections\"\>Editing Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	hr	You can protect, hide, and convert sections to normal text in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154224				0	hr	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>\<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>\</link\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149848				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Section \</emph\>list, click the section you want to modify. You can press Ctrl+A to select all sections in the list, and you can Shift+click or Ctrl+click to select some sections.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153397				0	hr	Učinite nešto od navedenog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3153120				0	hr	To convert a section into normal text, click \<emph\>Remove\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149631				0	hr	To make a section read-only, select the \<emph\>Protected \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Write Protection \</emph\>area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	hr	To hide a section, select the \<emph\>Hide \</emph\>check box in the \<emph\>Hide \</emph\>area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3156255				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02170000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Sections\"\>Format - Sections\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id973540				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\"\>Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>settings;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;settings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;word completion settings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>weekdays; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>months; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	hd_id4745017				0	hr	\<variable id=\"word_completion_adjust\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id4814294				0	hr	If you like it that $[officename] automatically completes the words that you frequently use, you can make further adjustments to refine that behavior. If you want, you can also save the current list of collected words so that it can be used in the next session.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2593462				0	hr	To fine-tune the word completion choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\> and select any of the following options:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	hr	To Insert an Additional Space Character				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B03				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Append space\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0E				0	hr	The space character is appended after you type the first character of the next word after the auto-completed word. The space character is suppressed if the next character is a delimiter, such as a full stop or a new line character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	hr	To Define the Accept Key				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B20				0	hr	Choose the key to accept the suggested word using the \<emph\>Accept with\</emph\> list box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D2				0	hr	To Select the Minimum Number of Characters				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B36				0	hr	Use the \<emph\>Min. word length\</emph\> box to set the minimum number of characters a word must have to be collected into the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	hr	To Select the Scope of Collected Words				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4C				0	hr	Disable the option \<emph\>When closing a document, remove the words collected from it from the list\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B53				0	hr	Now the list is also valid for other documents that you open. When you close the last %PRODUCTNAME document, the word list is deleted.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B56				0	hr	If you enable the checkbox, the list is only valid as long as the current document is open.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2634968				0	hr	If you want the word list to exist longer than the current %PRODUCTNAME session, save it as a document, as described in the following section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	hr	To Use the Word List for Further Sessions				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B94				0	hr	If the automatic spellcheck option is enabled, only the words that are recognized by the spellcheck are collected.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA1				0	hr	Use the word list to always start with a defined set of technical terms for the word completion feature.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA7				0	hr	Open the text document that contains the terms that you want to use for word completion.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BAB				0	hr	The word completion feature collects the words.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	hr	Select all or some of the words in the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	hr	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy all selected words into the clipboard. Paste the clipboard into a new document and save it to get a reference list of collected words.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BC6				0	hr	Later you can open the reference list and automatically collect the words, so that the word completion feature starts with a defined set of words.				20181231 09:50:43
