helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3156021				0	hr	Locate the graphic file that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_dialog.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	hr	By default, the inserted graphic is centered above the paragraph that you clicked in.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156108				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>cells; enlarging and reducing in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells; enlarging/reducing in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>keyboard; resizing rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;rows and columns in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>enlarging columns,cells and table rows\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>reducing rows and columns in text tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; resizing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156108				0	hr	\<variable id=\"table_sizing\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_sizing.xhp\" name=\"Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table\"\>Resizing Rows and Columns in a Text Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153140				0	hr	You can resize the width of table cells and columns, as well as change the height of table rows.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149615				0	hr	\<image id=\"img_id3149622\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_optimizetable.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149622\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3146497				0	hr	You can also distribute rows and columns evenly using the icons on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Optimize\</item\> toolbar on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table\</item\> Bar.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145109				0	hr	Changing the Width of Columns and Cells				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149574				0	hr	To Change the Width of a Column				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3149587				0	hr	Do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3156246				0	hr	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3145390				0	hr	Rest the mouse pointer over the column dividing line on the ruler until the pointer becomes a separator icon, and then drag the line to a new location.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id0918200811260957				0	hr	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and then click and drag a line to scale all cells right or above the line proportionally.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3145411				0	hr	Place the cursor in a cell in the column, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153364				0	hr	To increase the distance from the left edge of the page to the edge of the table, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift, and then press the right arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891				0	hr	You can specify the behavior for the arrow keys by choosing \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</emph\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\<emph\> - \</emph\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - Table\</emph\>, and selecting the options that you want in the \<emph\>Keyboard handling\</emph\> area.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149993				0	hr	To Change the Width of a Cell				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3148676				0	hr	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153014				0	hr	Changing the Height of a Row				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3153035				0	hr	To change the height of a row, place the cursor in a cell in the row, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, and then press the up or the down arrow key.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	hd_id8478041				0	hr	Resizing a whole Table				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id3358867				0	hr	To change the width and height of a table, do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5366679				0	hr	Click inside the table. In the rulers, drag the border between the white and the gray area to resize the table.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id1279030				0	hr	Click inside the table. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Table - Table Properties\</item\> to open a dialog and set the properties to the numbers.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id5009308				0	hr	To wrap text to the sides of a table, and to arrange two tables next to another, you must insert the tables into a frame. Click inside the table, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+A\</item\> twice to select the whole table, then choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_sizing.xhp	0	help	par_id4190496				0	hr	Tables within HTML pages do not offer the full range of properties and commands as tables in OpenDocument format.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Creating and Applying Page Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id7071138				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;creating and applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>applying;page styles\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;page styles\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182	1			0	hr	\<variable id=\"pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Creating and Applying Page Styles\"\>Creating and Applying Page Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	hr	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the layout of a page, including the page orientation, background, margins, headers, footers, and text columns. To change the layout of an individual page in a document, you must create and apply a custom page style to the page.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071A				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp#pageorientation\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_idN10722				0	hr	\<embedvar href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#pagebackground\"/\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156109				0	hr	To define a new page style:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153411	3			0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting.\</emph\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	hr	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149614				0	hr	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab, type a name in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145110				0	hr	Učinite nešto od navedenog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156252				0	hr	To apply the custom page style to a single page, select the default page style that is used in your document in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153376				0	hr	To apply the custom page style to more than one page, select its name in the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box. To stop using the style, insert a manual page break and assign it a different page style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154252				0	hr	Use the tabs in the dialog to set the layout options for the page style, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154851				0	hr	To apply a page style:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154873				0	hr	Click in the page that you want to apply the page style to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3155888				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Style\</item\> icon.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3148685				0	hr	Double-click a name in the list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	hr	To apply a page style to a new page:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147122				0	hr	Click in the document where you want a new page to start.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150210				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150235				0	hr	Select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150939				0	hr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the page that follows the manual break.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150965				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Skriveni tekst				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>comparisons; hidden text fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hidden text; displaying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;hiding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>non-printing text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; non-printable\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying;hidden text\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856	1			0	hr	\<variable id=\"hidden_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	hr	You can use fields and sections to hide or display text in your document if a condition is met.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409				0	hr	Before you can hide text, you must first create a variable to use in the condition for hiding the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id5174108				0	hr	To Create a Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153131				0	hr	Click in your document and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640	21			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab and click "Set Variable" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970	22			0	hr	Click "General" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620				0	hr	Type a name for the variable in the \<emph\>Name \</emph\>box, for example, "Hide".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149869				0	hr	Enter a value for the variable in the \<emph\>Value \</emph\>box, for example, "1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	hr	To hide the variable in your document, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156245				0	hr	To hide text:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145391				0	hr	Click in the document where you want to add the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409	5			0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	29			0	hr	Click "Hidden Text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154404				0	hr	Enter a statement in the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371	31			0	hr	Type the text that you want to hide in the \<emph\>Hidden text \</emph\>box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	hr	To hide a paragraph:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853				0	hr	Click in the paragraph where you want to add the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154872	35			0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	6			0	hr	Click "Hidden Paragraph" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155947				0	hr	Enter a statement in the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3793450				0	hr	You must enable this feature by removing the check mark from menu \<emph\>View - Hidden Paragraphs\</emph\>. When the check mark is set, you cannot hide any paragraph.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148675				0	hr	To hide a section:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148697				0	hr	Select the text that you want to hide in your document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148950				0	hr	In the\<emph\> Hide\</emph\> area, select\<emph\> Hide\</emph\>, and then enter an expression in the\<emph\> Condition\</emph\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter "Hide==1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153636				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
