helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689				0	hr	\<variable id=\"indices_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_enter.xhp\" name=\"Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\"\>Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155862				0	hr	Defining Index Entries				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380				0	hr	Click in a word, or select the words in your document that you want to use as an index entry.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147409				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	hr	To change the text that appears in the index, type the text that you want in the \<emph\>Entry\</emph\> box. The text that you type here does not replace the selected text in the document.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	hr	To add an index mark to similar words in your document, select \<emph\>Apply to all similar texts\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155889				0	hr	To add the entries to a custom index, click the \<emph\>New User-defined Index\</emph\> icon, enter the name of the index, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147119				0	hr	Defining Table of Contents Entries				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147132				0	hr	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. You can also use custom paragraph styles, so long as you assign them one of the predefined outline levels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150230				0	hr	To use a custom paragraph style as a table of contents entry:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150933				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964				0	hr	Select the paragraph style that you want to include in your table of contents in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Level\</emph\> list, click the hierarchical level that you want to apply the paragraph style to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153730	17			0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You can now apply the style to headings in your document and include them in your table of contents. 				20181231 09:50:43
