helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147104				0	hr	\<variable id=\"indices_toc\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_toc.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Table of Contents\"\>Creating a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150942				0	hr	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents. After you apply these styles, you can then create a table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id5876949				0	hr	To Insert a Table of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	hr	Click in your document where you want to create the table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120211.xhp\" name=\"Index/Table\"\>\<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153746				0	hr	Select "Table of Contents" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146856				0	hr	Select any options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146872				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3146896				0	hr	If you want to use a different paragraph style as a table of contents entry, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Additional Styles\</item\> check box in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Create from\</item\> area, and then click the (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) button next to the check box. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Assign Styles\</item\> dialog, click the style in the list, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>>>\</item\> or the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\><<\</item\> button to define the outline level for the paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153148				0	hr	Updating a Table of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153161				0	hr	Učinite nešto od navedenog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3153183				0	hr	Right-click in the table of contents and choose \<emph\>Update Index/Table\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_toc.xhp	0	help	par_id3147066				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - All Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Umetanje, Uredjivanje i Povezivanje Tekstualnih Okvira 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing; size of text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>links;text frames\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text;not printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text from printing\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	hr	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	hr	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	hr	Inserting Text Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	hr	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	hr	Editing Text Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	hr	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	hr	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	hr	To resize a text frame, click an edge of frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	hr	Hiding Text From Printing				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	hr	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	hr	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame - Options\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	hr	Linking Text Frames				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	hr	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	hr	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	hr	On the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> Bar, click the \<emph\>Link Frames\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	hr	Click the frame that you want to link to.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	hr	You can only link frames if:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	hr	The target frame is empty.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	hr	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	hr	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	hr	The source frame does not have a next link.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	hr	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	hr	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	hr	The Autosize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Unaprijedjivanje , Uredjivanje i Brisanje Indeksa i Tabela Sadrzaja 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing/updating/deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing and deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	hr	\<variable id=\"indices_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_edit.xhp\" name=\"Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\"\>Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	hr	Place the cursor in the index or table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155871				0	hr	If you cannot place your cursor in the index or table of contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</item\>, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Enable\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Cursor in protected areas\</item\> section.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	hr	Right-click and choose an editing option from the menu.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	hr	You can also make changes directly to an index or table of contents. Right-click in the index or table of contents, choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Protected from manual changes\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155855				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing; index format\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; formatting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entries; in tables of contents, as hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; hyperlinks as entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; in tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;indexes and tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155855				0	hr	\<variable id=\"indices_form\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_form.xhp\" name=\"Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\"\>Formatting an Index or a Table of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3154259				0	hr	You can apply different paragraph styles, assign hyperlinks to entries, change the layout of indexes, and change the background color of indexes in the \<emph\>Insert Index\</emph\> dialog.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155888				0	hr	To apply a different paragraph style to an index level:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	hr	Right-click in the index or table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147135	46			0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Styles \</emph\>tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150229	47			0	hr	Click an index level in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934	48			0	hr	Click the style that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	hr	Click the assign button \<emph\><\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150516				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146878				0	hr	To assign hyperlinks to entries in a table of contents:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3146890				0	hr	You can assign a cross-reference as a hyperlink to entries in a table of contents.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150712				0	hr	Right-click in the table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150738				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399				0	hr	Click the heading level that you want to assign hyperlinks to in the \<emph\>Level \</emph\>list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148424	53			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>area, click in the box in front of \<emph\>E#\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3153171				0	hr	Click in the box behind the \<emph\>E\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147060				0	hr	Repeat for each heading level that you want to create hyperlinks for, or click the \<emph\>All levels\</emph\> button to apply the formatting to all levels.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Brojanje Rijeci 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149686				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>words; counting in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of words\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>documents; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; number of words/characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; counting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of characters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>counting words\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>word counts\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	hr	\<variable id=\"words_count\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/words_count.xhp\" name=\"Counting Words\"\>Counting Words\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D1				0	hr	If you want to count only some text of your document, select the text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3149821				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Word Count\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	hd_id1116200901133957				0	hr	How does %PRODUCTNAME count words?				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133998				0	hr	In general, every string of characters between two spaces is a word. Tabs, line breaks, and paragraph breaks are word limits, too.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id1116200901133985				0	hr	Words with dashes or always visible hyphens, as in plug-in, add-on, user/config, are counted as one word each.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id111620090113399				0	hr	The words can be a mix of letters, numbers, and special characters. So the following text counts as four words: abc123 1.23 "$" http://www.example.com.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E2				0	hr	To get some more statistics about the document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties - Statistics\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\words_count.xhp	0	help	par_id3147418				0	hr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01100400.xhp\" name=\"File - Properties - Statistics\"\>File - Properties - Statistics\</link\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Templates and Styles				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153396				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>formatting styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>styles; styles and templates\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>organizing; templates (guide)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>templates; organizing (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153396				0	hr	\<variable id=\"templates_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/templates_styles.xhp\" name=\"Templates and Styles\"\>Templates and Styles\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	hr	A template is a document that contains specific formatting styles, graphics, tables, object, and other information. A template is used as the basis for creating other documents. For example, you can define paragraph and character styles in a document, save the document as a template, and then use the template to create a new document with the same styles.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149957				0	hr	Unless you specify otherwise, every new $[officename] text document is based on the default template.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149974				0	hr	$[officename] has a number of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"predefined templates\"\>predefined templates\</link\> that you can use to create different types or text documents, such as business letters.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149613				0	hr	Viewing and Organizing Styles in Templates				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B0				0	hr	Use the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/01110100.xhp\" name=\"Template Management\"\>Template Management\</link\> dialog to copy styles from one document to another.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\templates_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	hr	To copy a style, drag it to another template or document.				20181231 09:50:43
