helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154896				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; creating user-defined indexes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined indexes\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154896				0	hr	\<variable id=\"indices_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-Defined Indexes\"\>User-Defined Indexes\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155184				0	hr	You can create as many user-defined indexes as you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155915				0	hr	Creating a User-Defined Index				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155867				0	hr	Select a word or words that you want to add to a user-defined index.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3153410				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	hr	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New User-defined Index\</item\> button next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Index\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	hr	Type a name for the index in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147114	52			0	hr	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> to add the selected word(s) to the new index. 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147139				0	hr	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150231				0	hr	Inserting a User-Defined Index				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150933				0	hr	Click in the document where you want to insert the index.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	hr	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Index/Table\</item\> tab, select the name of the user-defined index that you created in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146881				0	hr	Select any options that you want.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146897				0	hr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150720				0	hr	If you want to use a different paragraph style as a table of contents entry, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles\</item\>, and then click the (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) button next to the box. Click the style in the list, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>>>\</item\> or the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\><<\</item\> button to define the outline level for the paragraph style.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Combining Numbered Lists				20181231 09:50:43
