helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150495				0	hr	\<variable id=\"join_numbered_lists\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/join_numbered_lists.xhp\" name=\"Combining Numbered Lists\"\>Combining Numbered Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149692				0	hr	You can combine numbered lists into a single consecutively numbered list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149452				0	hr	To combine consecutive numbered lists:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3154479				0	hr	Select all of the paragraphs in the lists.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3155911				0	hr	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering On/Off\</item\> icon twice.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155870				0	hr	To create a numbered list from non-consecutive paragraphs:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417				0	hr	Hold down Ctrl and drag a selection in the first numbered paragraph. You only have to select one character.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	hr	Continue to hold down Ctrl, and drag a selection in each numbered paragraph of the lists you want to combine.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\join_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	hr	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering On/Off\</item\> icon twice.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Racunanje i Naljepljivanje rezultata Formule u Teksutalnom  Dokumentu 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147692				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>pasting;results of formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>clipboard;calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas;pasting results in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147692				0	hr	\<variable id=\"calculate_clipboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_clipboard.xhp\" name=\" Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\"\> Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156366				0	hr	If your text already contains a formula, for example "12+24*2", $[officename] can calculate, and then paste the result of the formula in your document, without using the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	hr	Select the formula in the text. The formula can only contain numbers and operators and cannot contain spaces.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155496	38			0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Calculate\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Plus Sign (+).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id5172582				0	hr	Place the cursor where you want to insert the result of the formula, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste\</item\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.\<br/\>The selected formula is replaced by the result.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Changing the Case of Text				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155182				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>characters; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters; text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>uppercase; formatting text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;cases of text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>initial capitals in titles\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182				0	hr	\<variable id=\"text_capital\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_capital.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Case of Text\"\>Changing the Case of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	hr	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	hr	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	hr	To capitalize text:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	hr	Select the text that you want to capitalize.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	hr	Učinite nešto od navedenog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485778				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485775				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select the type of capitalization in the Effects box. "Capitals" capitalizes all letters. "Title" capitalizes the first letter of each word. "Small capitals" capitalizes all letters, but in a reduced font size.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	hr	To change text to lowercase:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	hr	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606				0	hr	Učinite nešto od navedenog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id112020091049000				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</item\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910490034				0	hr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select "Lowercase" in the Effects box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_numbered_lists.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Adding Bullets				20181231 09:50:43
