helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	hr	\<variable id=\"optionentext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"SW:PUSHBUTTON:DLG_CAPTION:BTN_OPTION\"\>Adds the chapter number to the caption label. To use this feature, you must first assign an \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"outline level\"\>outline level\</link\> to a paragraph style, and then apply the style to the chapter headings in your document.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149805				0	hr	Numeriranje po poglavljima				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153532				0	hr	When you add chapter numbers to caption labels, the caption numbering is reset when a chapter heading is encountered. For example, if the last figure in chapter 1 is "Figure 1.12", the first figure in the next chapter would be "Figure 2.1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154574				0	hr	Razina				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152954				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_SEQUENCE_OPTION:LB_LEVEL\"\>Select the number of outline levels from the top of the chapter hierarchy down to include in the caption label.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151316				0	hr	Razdjelnik				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:EDIT:DLG_SEQUENCE_OPTION:ED_SEPARATOR\"\>Enter the character that you want to insert between the chapter number and the caption number.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10633				0	hr	Oblik kategorija i okvira				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_idN10639				0	hr	Vrsta znaka				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_idN1063F				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the character style.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143280				0	hr	Primijeni obrub i sjenu				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149826				0	hr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_CAPTION:CB_COPY_ATTR\"\>Applies the border and shadow of the object to the caption frame.\</ahelp\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	tit				0	hr	Odredjivanje Uvjeta 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145828				0	hr	\<bookmark_value\>logical expressions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulating conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>conditions; in fields and sections\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields;defining conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sections;defining conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables; in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user data;in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;in conditions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding; database fields\</bookmark_value\>				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145828				0	hr	Odredjivanje Uvjeta 				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145242				0	hr	Conditions are logical expressions that you can use to control the display of \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\"\>fields\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04020000.xhp\"\>sections\</link\> in your document. Although the following examples apply to fields, they also apply to sections.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147171				0	hr	You can define conditions for the following field types:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151185				0	hr	Conditional text: displays text A if the condition is true, or text B if the condition is false.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149289				0	hr	Hidden text: hides the contents of the field if the condition is true.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145412				0	hr	Hidden paragraph: hides the paragraph if the condition is true.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147515				0	hr	Any record and next record: controls the access to database records.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149802	18			0	hr	The simplest way to define a condition is to type the logical expression directly in a \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box using the following values:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153677				0	hr	Točno				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152960				0	hr	The condition is always met. You can also enter any value not equal to 0 as the conditional text.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900				0	hr	Netočno				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154191				0	hr	The condition is not met. You can also enter the value 0.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147090	23			0	hr	If you leave the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box empty, the condition is interpreted as not being met.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148980				0	hr	When you define a condition, use the same \<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\"\>elements\</link\> for defining a formula, namely comparative operators, mathematical and statistical functions, number formats, variables and constants.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153638				0	hr	You can use the following types of variables when you define a condition:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155135				0	hr	Predefined \<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\"\>$[officename] variables\</link\> that use statistics on document properties				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156273				0	hr	Custom variables, that are a created with the "Set variable" field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149174				0	hr	Variables based on user data				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145781				0	hr	Variables based on the contents of database fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	hr	You cannot use internal variables, such as page and chapter numbers, in condition expression.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151375				0	hr	Conditions and Variables				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150122				0	hr	The following examples use a variable called "x":				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147417				0	hr	x == 1 or x EQ 1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147500				0	hr	The condition is true if "x" is equal to 1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145259				0	hr	x != 1 or x NEQ 1				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150551				0	hr	The condition is true if "x" does not equal 1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147749				0	hr	sinx == 0				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146345				0	hr	The condition is true if "x" is a multiple of pi.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149846				0	hr	To use comparative operators with strings, the operands must be bounded by double quotation marks:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151078				0	hr	x == "ABC" or x EQ "ABC"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150162				0	hr	Checks if variable "x" contains (true) the "ABC" string, or not (false).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153301				0	hr	x == "" or x EQ ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156120				0	hr	ili				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156133				0	hr	!x or NOT x				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156112				0	hr	Checks if the variable "x" contains an empty string.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150097				0	hr	The "equal" comparative operator must be represented by two equal signs (==) in a condition. For example, if you define a variable "x" with the value of 1, you can enter the condition as x==1.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148791				0	hr	Korisnički podaci				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028				0	hr	You can include user data when you define conditions. To change your user data, choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] - User data\</emph\>. User data must be entered in the form of strings. You can query the user data with "==" (EQ), "!=" (NEQ), or "!"(NOT).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153124				0	hr	The following table lists user data variables and their meanings:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632				0	hr	Varijabla				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150662				0	hr	Značenje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154026				0	hr	user_firstname				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149953				0	hr	Ime				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147272				0	hr	user_lastname				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149601				0	hr	Prezime				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150770				0	hr	user_initials				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155529				0	hr	Inicijali				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148705				0	hr	user_company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	hr	Tvrtka				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155361				0	hr	user_street				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	hr	Ulica				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108				0	hr	user_country				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146885				0	hr	Zemlja				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149580				0	hr	user_zipcode				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	hr	Poštanski broj				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922				0	hr	user_city				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148945				0	hr	Grad				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156053				0	hr	user_title				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159219				0	hr	Naslov				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156435				0	hr	user_position				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145178				0	hr	Položaj				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150797				0	hr	user_tel_work				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150820				0	hr	Business telephone number				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150894				0	hr	user_tel_home				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155320				0	hr	Home telephone number				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154400				0	hr	user_fax				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	hr	Broj faksa				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153390				0	hr	user_email				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154948				0	hr	Adresom e-pošte				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145603				0	hr	user_state				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150129				0	hr	State (not in all $[officename] versions)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150147				0	hr	For example, to hide a paragraph, text, or a section from a user with a specific initial, such as "LM", enter the condition: user_initials=="LM".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154115				0	hr	Conditions and Database Fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154128				0	hr	You can define conditions for accessing databases, or database fields. For example, you can check the contents of a database field from a condition, or use database fields in logical expressions. The following table lists a few more examples of using databases in conditions:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156066				0	hr	Primjer				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156088				0	hr	Značenje				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155948				0	hr	Database.Table.Company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148673				0	hr	Database.Table.Company NEQ ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148687				0	hr	Database.Table.Company != ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155373				0	hr	The condition is true if the COMPANY field is not empty. (In the first example, no operator is required.)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149977				0	hr	!Database.Table.Company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991				0	hr	NOT Database.Table.Company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150004				0	hr	Database.Table.Company EQ ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3146911				0	hr	Database.Table.Company ==""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148733				0	hr	Returns TRUE if the COMPANY field is empty. (Exclamation sign represents a logical NOT.)				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148762				0	hr	Database.Table.Company !="Sun Microsystems"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153016				0	hr	Database.Table.Company NEQ "Sun Microsystems"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153040				0	hr	Returns TRUE if the current entry in the COMPANY field is "Sun Microsystems".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154605				0	hr	Database.Table.Firstname AND Database.Table.Name				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153059				0	hr	Returns TRUE if the record contains the first and the last name.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3159247				0	hr	Note the difference between the boolean NOT "!" and the comparative operator not equal "!=" (NEQ).				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	hr	When you refer to a database field in a condition, use the form Databasename.Tablename.Fieldname. If one of the names contains a character that is an operator, such as a minus sign (-), enclose the name in square brackets, for example, Databasename.[Table-name].Fieldname. Never use spaces inside field names.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153891				0	hr	Example: Hiding an Empty Database Field				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150051				0	hr	You may want to create a condition that hides an empty field, for example, if the COMPANY field is empty for some of the data records.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150067				0	hr	Select the \<emph\>Hidden Paragraph\</emph\> box, and type the following condition: Addressbook.Addresses.Company EQ ""				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	hr	or type the following				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	hr	NOT Addressbook.Addresses.Company				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147136				0	hr	If the COMPANY database field is empty, the condition is true and the paragraph is hidden.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150232				0	hr	To display hidden paragraphs on the screen, you can choose \<emph\>Tools - Options - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>, and clear the \<emph\>Hidden paragraphs\</emph\> check box.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145218				0	hr	Examples of Conditions in Fields				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145231				0	hr	The following examples use the Conditional text field, although they can be applied to any fields that can be linked to a condition. The syntax used for conditions is also used for the Hidden text, Hidden paragraph, Any record or Next record fields.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150311				0	hr	To display conditional text based on the number of pages:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150333				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147471				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list, click "Conditional text".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154294	63			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box, type "page == 1".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box, type "There is only one page".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150640	65			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box, type "There are several pages".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153086				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155814				0	hr	To display conditional text based on a user-defined Variable				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155836				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Variables\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155109	68			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list, click "Set Variable".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147008	139			0	hr	In the\<emph\> Name\</emph\> box, type "Profit".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147032	140			0	hr	In the\<emph\> Value\</emph\> box, type "5000".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152974				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3152998				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab, and click "Conditional text" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150952				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Condition\</emph\> box, type "Profit < 5000".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156291				0	hr	In the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box, type "Target is not met".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3156317	72			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box, type "Target is met".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154366				0	hr	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154389				0	hr	To edit the contents of the "Profit" variable, double-click the variable field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155573				0	hr	To display conditional text based on the contents of a database field:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155587				0	hr	The first part of this example inserts a space between the "First Name" and "Last Name" fields in a document, and the second part inserts text based on the contents of a field. This example requires that an address data source is registered with $[officename].				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523				0	hr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Database\</emph\> tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148811	75			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list, click "Mail merge fields".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3148841	76			0	hr	In the\<emph\> Database selection\</emph\> box, double-click an address book, click "First Name", and then click\<emph\> Insert\</emph\>. Repeat for "Last Name".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3147549	78			0	hr	In the document, place the cursor between the two fields, press Space, and then return to the \<emph\>Fields \</emph\>dialog:				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150416				0	hr	Click the \<emph\>Functions\</emph\> tab, and then click "Conditional text" in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153589	146			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box, type: "Addressbook.addresses.firstname".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153615	80			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box, type a space and leave the \<emph\>Or \</emph\>box blank.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3153562				0	hr	You can now use a condition to insert text based on the contents of the First Name field.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150574	147			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Fields \</emph\>dialog, click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150605	85			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box, click "Conditional text".				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151277	86			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Condition \</emph\>box, type: Addressbook.addresses.firstname == "Michael"				20181231 09:50:43
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3151303	87			0	hr	In the \<emph\>Then \</emph\>box, type "Dear".				20181231 09:50:43
